INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-001-rd003',1,'vv11345',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4455,18,304,'Section: What This Project Is

vv11345 is a browser application titled Egyptinator that turns a specialized Ancient-Egyptian lexical mapping into an interactive user-facing utility.

A user types English or hieroglyphic text into the page. JavaScript normalizes the input, routes it through lookup logic, and writes generated output back into the DOM. The application also provides direction switching, a definition mode, clipboard copying, and clear/reset actions.

The project is significant because the software is not merely static presentation. The browser is the full application runtime: interface events trigger domain-specific text transformation and immediate generated output.

Section: Project Scope

The functional scope includes:

live input processing;

English-to-hieroglyph lookup;

hieroglyph-to-English reverse lookup;

one-to-many definition lookup;

literal character transliteration fallback;

repeated-space cleanup;

lowercasing before lookup;

clipboard copying;

clear/reset behavior;

a large embedded lexical mapping.

The root implementation is concentrated in:

index.html for the functional interface;

style.css for presentation;

code.js for interaction, state, lookup, transliteration, and embedded data;

README.md for project status and usage context.

Section: Technical Stack > JavaScript

JavaScript implements the complete runtime behavior. It handles DOM reads/writes, translation mode state, input normalization, dictionary scanning, transliteration, alerts, and clipboard interaction.

Section: Technical Stack > HTML

HTML defines the text field, output surface, controls, mode toggle, and user guidance. Event handlers are connected directly from markup.

Section: Technical Stack > CSS

CSS provides the visual styling required to use the translator as a standalone browser page.

Section: Technical Stack > Unicode Hieroglyphs

Egyptian hieroglyphic characters are stored and emitted directly as Unicode text. This keeps generated results selectable and copyable.

Section: Technical Stack > GitHub Pages

GitHub Pages is enabled for the repository, providing static deployment evidence for the browser application.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Bidirectional Lookup

One mode scans English entries and returns mapped Egyptian values. The reverse mode scans Egyptian values to recover English entries.','["javascript","html","ancient-egyptian","hieroglyphs","scope","technical","stack","unicode","github","pages","major","engineering","work","bidirectional","lookup"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-001-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-001-vv11345/README.md","source_line_end":29,"source_line_start":29,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`vv11345` is a browser application titled **Egyptinator** that turns a specialized Ancient-Egyptian lexical mapping into an interactive user-facing utility.","text_sha256":"17b2b1066dd38367992f770f8c7571d5d95e0f3b286fb5c3873ebbd9c0dfcd7b","unit_id":"s004","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-001-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-001-vv11345/README.md","source_line_end":31,"source_line_start":31,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"A user types English or hieroglyphic text into the page. JavaScript normalizes the input, routes it through lookup logic, and writes generated output back into the DOM. The application also provides direction switching, a definition mode, clipboard copying, and clear/reset actions.","text_sha256":"39e35fafb8ff63e1525e0905b9f46b72b76c6d32f7d070b9554ffbb80e192f11","unit_id":"s004","word_count":41},{"block_id":"repo-001-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This