INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-001-rd006',1,'vv11345',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3744,13,370,'Section: Major Engineering Work > Definition Mode

Definition mode gathers all mappings associated with a matching English term and displays multiple hieroglyphic forms where the data contains several entries.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Transliteration Fallback

When a direct lexical match is unavailable, the application uses a character-level Latin-to-hieroglyph table. This gives the tool a deterministic fallback path for names and other unrecognized terms.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Input Normalization

The input is normalized before lookup through lowercasing and repeated-space cleanup. This is an early example of defensive preprocessing around user-entered text.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Clipboard Interaction

The copy flow temporarily selects generated output through the input element, invokes the browser copy operation, and restores the original input.

Section: Engineering Practices > Event-Driven Interaction

The application responds directly to browser input and click events.

Section: Engineering Practices > Explicit Mode State

Translation direction and definition behavior are represented explicitly through application state.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Languages

JavaScript — strong evidence. Implements interaction and the text-processing pipeline.

HTML — strong evidence. Defines the functional browser interface.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Data and Text Processing

Dictionary lookup — strong evidence.

Reverse lookup — strong evidence.

Input normalization — moderate evidence.

Character transliteration — strong evidence.

Unicode text handling — strong evidence.

Section: Capability Developed

Within the processed chronology, this repository establishes the earliest observed capability of turning domain-specific programming logic into a directly usable browser application.

It also establishes an early pattern of combining a specialized data corpus with an interaction layer to solve a concrete domain problem.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

JavaScript application logic;

HTML/CSS interface construction;

Section: Historical Significance

vv11345 establishes the initial software baseline of the processed portfolio. It is a real interactive utility in which user input flows through custom domain logic to generated output.

It also establishes the Ancient-Egyptian computing theme that recurs in later repositories and provides a useful baseline for later questions about frontend, data-processing, and product evolution.

Section: Overall Repository Narrative

vv11345 is an early static web application that packages Ancient-Egyptian lexical data into an interactive browser experience. HTML and CSS create the user surface, while JavaScript performs normalization, bidirectional lookup, definition lookup, transliteration fallback, DOM rendering, and clipboard interaction.','["javascript","html","ancient-egyptian","major","engineering","work","definition","mode","transliteration","fallback","input","normalization","clipboard","interaction","practices","event-driven","state","skills","demonstrated","languages","data","text","processing","capability"]','["Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Repository Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-001-s016-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Definition Mode"],"section_title":"Definition Mode","source_file":"repositories/repo-001-vv11345/README.md","source_line_end":111,"source_line_start":111,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Definition mode gathers all mappings associated with a matching English term and displays multiple hieroglyphic forms where the data contains several entries.","text_sha256":"090f2c6e29c2d69c81f86f72b57c21de0545510e159a23e41da490dbfbc41490","unit_id":"s016","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-001-s017-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Transliteration Fallback"],"section_title":"Transliteration Fallback","source_file":"repositories/repo-001-vv11345/README.md","source_line_end":115,"source_line_start":115,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"When a direct lexical match is unavailable, the application uses a character-level Latin-to-hieroglyph table. This gives the tool a d