INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-003-rd005',3,'xml_Parse_project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3515,6,354,'Section: Technical Stack > JSON

The repository includes recursive XML-to-JSON transformation logic, including repeated-tag handling for array-like structures.

Section: Technical Stack > Huffman Coding

The compression subsystem includes tree construction, min-heap operations, frequency tables, binary packing, and decompression traversal.

Section: Major Engineering Work > XML Parsing

The parser exposes multiple operations for loading file content, tokenizing it, extracting tags, locating tags, and obtaining data values.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Tree-Based XML Representation

XML hierarchy is modeled through a custom tree structure, enabling recursive algorithms that align naturally with nested documents.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Pretty Printing

Recursive traversal emits opening tags, content, nested children, and closing tags with indentation derived from structural depth.

Section: Major Engineering Work > XML Minification

The same structured representation is serialized without formatting whitespace to produce a compact XML form.

Section: Major Engineering Work > XML-to-JSON Conversion

The conversion logic maps hierarchical XML into JSON-like output, distinguishes scalar value forms, and handles repeated siblings as arrays.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Error Detection and Correction

The correction interface reports structural errors with tag/line context and can produce a corrected tree. This is a repository-level capability with explicit collaborator attribution.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Huffman Compression

The compression subsystem contains:

character-frequency tracking;

min-heap operations;

Huffman tree construction;

code generation;

bit-packed output;

decompression traversal;

file-size tracking.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Social Graph Analysis

Follower relationships are represented using adjacency-style structures to derive influence, activity, mutual-follow, and recommendation-style queries.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Desktop Integration

The GUI integrates the file-processing and analytical operations into an interactive desktop workspace rather than leaving them as isolated classes.

Section: Engineering Practices > Modular File Organization

Parsing, correction, compression, graph analysis, GUI windows, and supporting structures are separated into distinct source/header units.

Section: Engineering Practices > Data-Structure Selection

trees model XML hierarchy;

stacks support structural processing;

adjacency structures model social relationships;

min-heaps support Huffman coding.

Section: Engineering Practices > Recursive Algorithms

Recursive traversal is used for hierarchical formatting, minification, and JSON conversion.

Section: Engineering Practices > Diagnostic Error Reporting

The correction interface associates errors with tags and lines, supporting user-facing diagnosis.','["xml-to-json","min-heap","technical","stack","json","huffman","coding","major","engineering","work","parsing","tree-based","representation","pretty","printing","minification","conversion","error","detection","correction","compression","social","graph","desktop"]','["Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-003-s017-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Technical Stack","JSON"],"section_title":"JSON","source_file":"repositories/repo-003-xml_Parse_project/README.md","source_line_end":147,"source_line_start":147,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository includes recursive XML-to-JSON transformation logic, including repeated-tag handling for array-like structures.","text_sha256":"2e86bae67e5b40c7de26715806afc76ba735c0e1efbd1b2619df28b61316ebfc","unit_id":"s017","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-003-s018-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s018","section_path":["Technical Stack","Huffman Coding"],"section_title":"Huffman Coding","source_file":"repositories/repo-003-xml_Parse_project/README.md","source_line_end":151,"source_line_start":151,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The compression subsystem includes tree construction, min-heap operations, frequency tables, binary packing, and decompression traversal.","text_sha256":"4196fa6cefc2925d29d2b26ca002365855138053c1abecdec4fa43f64bfcb0a3","unit_id":"s018","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-003-s020-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","XML Parsing"],"section_title":"XML Parsing","source_file":"repositories/repo-003-xml_Parse_project/README.md","source_line_