INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-004-rd003',4,'MIPS_verilog_Model',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3759,16,313,'Section: What This Project Is

MIPS_verilog_Model is a compact Verilog model of a simplified MIPS-style processor.

The source contains a register file, program counter, instruction memory, data memory, instruction decoding, selected arithmetic/logical operations, load/store behavior, a clock generator, and a minimal testbench wrapper.

The README includes simulator-state screenshots, making HDL simulation an explicit part of the project rather than an inferred development method.

Section: Project Scope

MIPS.v defines:

registerfile — 32 registers with two asynchronous reads and clocked writes;

CPU — program counter, memories, instruction register, decode logic, ALU-style operations, and memory behavior;

clock_Gen — a simulation clock;

CPU_tb — a testbench entry point.

Visible R-format function cases include:

shift left;

shift right;

add;

subtract;

AND;

OR;

XOR;

NOR.

Opcode cases also implement selected immediate and memory operations.

Section: Technical Stack > Verilog

Verilog models signal widths, register arrays, memory arrays, procedural logic, clocked state changes, and instruction decoding.

Section: Technical Stack > HDL Simulation

A dedicated clock module and testbench provide an executable simulation context.

Section: Technical Stack > MIPS-Style ISA Concepts

The implementation extracts opcode, rs, rt, rd, function, and shift fields from encoded instructions and dispatches behavior accordingly.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Register File Modeling

The register-file module implements 32 32-bit registers, two continuously readable ports, and a clocked write path controlled by RegWrite.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Program Counter and Instruction Fetch

The CPU reads instruction memory using IMemory[PC >> 2] and advances the program counter by four, modeling word-aligned sequential fetch.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Instruction Field Extraction

The model explicitly decomposes the instruction register into conventional MIPS fields.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Simulation Clock and Testbench

The clock generator toggles at a fixed simulation interval, and CPU_tb instantiates the model for simulator execution.

Section: Engineering Practices > Architectural Decomposition

The register file, CPU, clock generator, and testbench are separated into distinct Verilog modules.','["verilog","register-file","scope","technical","stack","simulation","mips-style","concepts","major","engineering","work","file","modeling","program","counter","instruction","fetch","field","extraction","clock","testbench","practices","architectural","decomposition"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-004-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-004-MIPS_verilog_Model/README.md","source_line_end":28,"source_line_start":28,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`MIPS_verilog_Model` is a compact Verilog model of a simplified MIPS-style processor.","text_sha256":"2fd4dda54a219cc4c2cfc417ca61c8f67bc48fb872824a11c52a9cfc692531a8","unit_id":"s004","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-004-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-004-MIPS_verilog_Model/README.md","source_line_end":30,"source_line_start":30,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The source contains a register file, program counter, instruction memory, data memory, instruction decoding, selected arithmetic/logical operations, load/store behavior, a clock generator, and a minimal testbench wrapper.","text_sha256":"95ed3d0ee1a82927bf1c9640b2a886d7da1684d002c7df3a0aeb8fdb5d437f43","unit_id":"s004","word_count":27},{"block_id":"repo-004-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project 