se to the behavior of those modules.","text_sha256":"30af82d53a2837f9747444975e901248088ce3738f60b61daff5855ada8c362b","unit_id":"s003","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-005-s043-b001","canonical_categories":["authorship_attribution"],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s043","section_path":["Collaboration and Authorship"],"section_title":"Collaboration and Authorship","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":224,"source_line_start":224,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- `individual-project`","text_sha256":"d37d3796856631d165d1ea7b024c43b8797da439be1d8255def21d1ecc31bd07","unit_id":"s043","word_count":2}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","document_text_sha256":"57ce70fb96b3ad8c900285a87ad31116e57317263dc80f1aa2480415162c2a20","earliest_source_line":18,"embedding_text_sha256":"a582bbe81804076adab081a2706f560883db413ff2c7c6a770e85e5914ab6e85","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"f59ad7437ede361792f3298e541dbdf5b47b9b0b196c45a550ecd1dbe32d58fd","repository_source_line_end":254,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-005-rd003',5,'VerilogTools',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3881,12,396,'Section: What This Project Is

VerilogTools is a small collection of independent Verilog exercises or reusable simulation snippets.

The project broadens the Verilog concepts visible after the preceding MIPS model by isolating smaller digital-design ideas that can be exercised independently.

Section: Project Scope > Clock Generator

CLK_ON_WIRE.v initializes a clock to zero and toggles it every five simulation time units, producing a 50% duty-cycle simulation signal.

Section: Project Scope > Parameterized Decoder

Generic_Decoder.v defines a decoder parameterized by input width n. The output width is derived as 2**n, and the active bit is selected through a left shift.

The same file contains a testbench that instantiates a four-bit decoder and applies timed input changes.

Section: Project Scope > Truth-Table Enumeration

TruthTable.v loops through all 16 combinations of four input bits and prints each combination with the result of a Boolean expression.

Section: Project Scope > Keypad / Peripheral Interface

keypad.v captures one-hot key inputs on a clock edge, maps them to buffered numeric values, and conditionally drives a shared data bus using request/acknowledge and enable signals.

The design also models high-impedance z behavior.

Section: Technical Stack > Verilog

The repository uses module definitions, parameters, bit vectors, procedural blocks, timing delays, case statements, continuous assignments, high-impedance values, and $display.

Section: Technical Stack > HDL Simulation Constructs

initial blocks, #5 delays, $display, and the decoder testbench establish explicit simulation-oriented use.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Reusable Simulation Clock

The clock module provides a small reusable timing source for HDL experiments.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Parameterized Decoder Design

The decoder''s input and output widths are derived from a parameter, making it a generic design rather than a fixed 2-to-4 or 3-to-8 implementation.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Exhaustive Small-State Enumeration

The truth-table module systematically enumerates every input combination in a four-bit state space.

Section: Major Engineering Work > One-Hot Key Capture

The keypad module maps one-hot key patterns into numeric buffer values on the rising clock edge.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Tri-State Bus Modeling

The keypad conditionally drives the data bus and otherwise assigns high impedance, introducing shared-bus behavior and basic peripheral control concepts.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Request/Acknowledge Control

Signals such as DREQ, DACK, and IO_EN model a simple control handshake around access to the shared bus.

Section: Engineering Practices > Parameterization

The decoder uses a width parameter to derive both interface sizes and behavior.','["verilog","digital-design","scope","clock","generator","parameterized","decoder","truth-table","enumeration","keypad","peripheral","interface","technical","stack","simulation","constructs","major","engineering","work","reusable","design","exhaustive","small-state","one-hot"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-005-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":28,"source_line_start":28,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`VerilogTools` is a small collection of independent Verilog exercises or reusable simulation snippets.","text_sha256":"07a300fc002e81f6fe5655e4a1acd4a6fe143ebb54a9ac5cf80831de74586d4a","unit_id":"s004","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-005-s004-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The project broadens the Verilog concepts visible after the preceding MIPS model by isolating smaller digital-design ideas that can be exercised independently.","text_sha256":"759418d837f06ec30d2afa5b9d19e8b9cf942a3441b90d1deafef501ab2fdf40","unit_id":"s004","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-005-s006-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Project Scope","Clock Generator"],"section_title":"Clock Generator","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`CLK_ON_WIRE.v` initializes a clock to zero and toggles it every five simulation time units, producing a 50% duty-cycle simulation signal.","text_sha256":"fd11146e861e580bedcd279b3b195a487c372f035b541cac6f6e3b35cace4b87","unit_id":"s006","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-005-s007-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Project Scope","Parameterized Decoder"],"section_title":"Parameterized Decoder","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":47,"source_line_start":47,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Generic_Decoder.v` defines a decoder parameterized by input width `n`. The output width is derived as `2**n`, and the active bit is selected through a left shift.","text_sha256":"9cf383b91bc54de29b0fb7bdd676fbd6c1710f202183017e1787b678f612eb3d","unit_id":"s007","word_count":26},{"block_id":"repo-005-s007-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Project Scope","Parameterized Decoder"],"section_title":"Parameterized Decoder","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":49,"source_line_start":49,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The same file contains a testbench that instantiates a four-bit decoder and applies timed input changes.","text_sha256":"7b04fe8969341d2adce50626a88455babb1a84ce268c79df9c81065ba3f2479c","unit_id":"s007","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-005-s008-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Project Scope","Truth-Table Enumeration"],"section_title":"Truth-Table Enumeration","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":53,"source_line_start":53,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`TruthTable.v` loops through all 16 combinations of four input bits and prints each combination with the result of a Boolean expression.","text_sha256":"977ee5dbce201e90db09719cdba73017cceecb09f730ec1cc2c047d98e66cf8a","unit_id":"s008","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-005-s009-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Project Scope","Keypad / Peripheral Interface"],"section_title":"Keypad / Peripheral Interface","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":57,"source_line_start":57,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`keypad.v` captures one-hot key inputs on a clock edge, maps them to buffered numeric values, and conditionally drives a shared data bus using request/acknowledge and enable signals.","text_sha256":"3adacccbdf55a2a227a3c305952f327ead187512f30b6f85ce5b73392d7733ac","unit_id":"s009","word_count":27},{"block_id":"repo-005-s009-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Project Scope","Keypad / Peripheral Interface"],"section_title":"Keypad / Peripheral Interface","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":59,"source_line_start":59,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The design also models high-impedance `z` behavior.","text_sha256":"42a220c82b5d185cff47737a2e8fec0aefccc3e5aa8384d299ebbce249bd18a3","unit_id":"s009","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-005-s012-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Technical Stack","Verilog"],"section_title":"Verilog","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":78,"source_line_start":78,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository uses module definitions, parameters, bit vectors, procedural blocks, timing delays, `case` statements, continuous assignments, high-impedance values, and `$display`.","text_sha256":"ad1a77d3ebce785daf184b19852e4d7bf8ca3c54c45ba518186e9dab6b9e1aee","unit_id":"s012","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-005-s013-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Technical Stack","HDL Simulation Constructs"],"section_title":"HDL Simulation Constructs","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":82,"source_line_start":82,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`initial` blocks, `#5` delays, `$display`, and the decoder testbench establish explicit simulation-oriented use.","text_sha256":"77e72a3b372b01ca87fafe18cb0d0366c02e7d9e76c5a59cf0796a43886e3130","unit_id":"s013","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-005-s015-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Reusable Simulation Clock"],"section_title":"Reusable Simulation Clock","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":88,"source_line_start":88,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The clock module provides a small reusable timing source for HDL experiments.","text_sha256":"e221527898838e6c71af810f99f42e5bf3e0ab160e8b6bf6ecf9c65bc9d4d23c","unit_id":"s015","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-005-s016-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Parameterized Decoder Design"],"section_title":"Parameterized Decoder Design","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":92,"source_line_start":92,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The decoder''s input and output widths are derived from a parameter, making it a generic design rather than a fixed 2-to-4 or 3-to-8 implementation.","text_sha256":"3926ba74848060b5d2a57324b2c3ff88d335880b6ce303be7a0aaa2ed71b4c93","unit_id":"s016","word_count":24},{"block_id":"repo-005-s017-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Exhaustive Small-State Enumeration"],"section_title":"Exhaustive Small-State Enumeration","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":96,"source_line_start":96,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The truth-table module systematically enumerates every input combination in a four-bit state space.","text_sha256":"5fec648eebd5cebdb8f4fcf0af2cb008a849ed1719330b730a69f6c5f430b70e","unit_id":"s017","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-005-s018-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s018","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","One-Hot Key Capture"],"section_title":"One-Hot Key Capture","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":100,"source_line_start":100,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The keypad module maps one-hot key patterns into numeric buffer values on the rising clock edge.","text_sha256":"05ee195a53c5a7976e4b125002b621853862f81661f3131a58fa803056acadf2","unit_id":"s018","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-005-s019-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Tri-State Bus Modeling"],"section_title":"Tri-State Bus Modeling","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":104,"source_line_start":104,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The keypad conditionally drives the data bus and otherwise assigns high impedance, introducing shared-bus behavior and basic peripheral control concepts.","text_sha256":"2c0b216b6da7b06f21004b35990375279c045b0c7dcfadf296bd31d2840f52a3","unit_id":"s019","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-005-s020-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Request/Acknowledge Control"],"section_title":"Request/Acknowledge Control","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":108,"source_line_start":108,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Signals such as `DREQ`, `DACK`, and `IO_EN` model a simple control handshake around access to the shared bus.","text_sha256":"a7cf27bd877432c93394796e88af41d743c0064135ba0440ffda53a01d9776a6","unit_id":"s020","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-005-s026-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Engineering Practices","Parameterization"],"section_title":"Parameterization","source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","source_line_end":128,"source_line_start":128,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The decoder uses a width parameter to derive both interface sizes and behavior.","text_sha256":"f56aff2176cf56fb3afc252ddea9b546650e73af375aa50e034c2cd26d8580a7","unit_id":"s026","word_count":13}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-005-VerilogTools/README.md","document_text_sha256":"051e539919808b6fb8aefb99ae9a01ff0929a690f47fd85e382f6372d8b26263","earliest_source_line":28,"embedding_text_sha256":"28ad4959bb6e262a0a24263360bbb277ea14769e30a03358bbefa29bc1a913b0","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"f59ad7437ede361792f3298e541dbdf5b47b9b0b196c45a550ecd1dbe32d58fd","repository_source_line_end":254,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
