INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-009-rd003',9,'LeetCode',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3673,9,241,'Section: What This Repository Is

LeetCode is a multi-year archive of C++ algorithm and data-structure solutions.

Each problem is an independent exercise rather than part of one shared application architecture.

The repository is active from its 2022 creation through September 2025, making it useful evidence of repeated algorithm practice over time.

Section: Visible Problem Breadth

The current tree includes examples such as:

Container With Most Water;

3Sum;

Remove Nth Node From End of List;

Valid Parentheses;

Merge K Sorted Lists;

Group Anagrams;

Maximum Subarray;

Climbing Stairs;

Same Tree;

Maximum Depth of Binary Tree;

Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock;

additional problem directories across the repository.

These problems span arrays, strings, linked lists, stacks, hashing, sorting, dynamic programming, trees, recursion, and pointer-based techniques.

Section: Repository Shape

The repository acts as a chronological archive of independent accepted/submitted solutions.

Section: Technical Stack > C++

C++ is the primary implementation language.

Visible solutions use standard-library features including:

std::vector;

std::sort;

std::min;

std::max;

nested vectors;

problem-provided linked-list/tree node types where applicable.

Section: Technical Stack > LeetSync

LeetSync automates synchronization of solution submissions and generated problem metadata into GitHub.

The automation is part of the repository workflow while the solution code remains the relevant personal engineering evidence.

Section: Major Algorithmic Work > Two-Pointer Technique

The Container With Most Water solution uses left/right indices, computes candidate area, updates the maximum, and advances the pointer associated with the limiting height.

This is direct evidence of the linear two-pointer pattern.','["arrays","strings","sorting","stacks","hashing","recursion","leetsync","visible","problem","breadth","shape","technical","stack","major","algorithmic","work","two-pointer","technique"]','["What This Repository Is","Visible Problem Breadth","Repository Shape","Technical Stack","Major Algorithmic Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-009-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-009-LeetCode/README.md","source_line_end":34,"source_line_start":34,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`LeetCode` is a multi-year archive of C++ algorithm and data-structure solutions.","text_sha256":"213fe6b1b68afced6d7ecf86996d0d7b5a99bc7fb675102786d2f3499aa11527","unit_id":"s004","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-009-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-009-LeetCode/README.md","source_line_end":36,"source_line_start":36,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Each problem is an independent exercise rather than part of one shared application architecture.","text_sha256":"eade588c7794aec01fa7761e44ff7bfa9a8e8b55a78e499d1bb66b8136f01d01","unit_id":"s004","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-009-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-009-LeetCode/README.md","source_line_end":38,"source_line_start":38,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository is active from its 2022 creation through September 2025