INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-010-rd003',10,'Creational-Design-Patterns',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4357,29,243,'Section: What This Repository Is

Creational-Design-Patterns is a compact Java learning repository that implements object-creation patterns as separate Maven projects.

The subject of the code is software architecture itself: object creation is isolated behind interfaces, abstract creators, builders, and controlled construction relationships.

Section: Repository Structure

The presence of compiled target/classes artifacts provides build evidence for the Maven projects.

Section: Technical Stack > Java

Java is used to express:

classes;

interfaces;

abstract classes;

overriding;

encapsulated construction;

polymorphism;

composition.

Section: Technical Stack > Maven

Each pattern example is organized as its own Maven project through a pom.xml.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Builder Pattern

The Builder example contains:

Car;

Builder interface;

CarBuilder;

Director;

BuilderPattern entry point.

The Builder interface defines incremental construction operations for:

reset;

seat configuration;

engine configuration;

trip-computer configuration;

GPS configuration.

CarBuilder stores the in-progress Car, returns the completed product, and resets itself for reuse.

Director defines reusable construction recipes such as a sports car and SUV.

This demonstrates separation among product representation, construction steps, concrete construction logic, and higher-level recipes.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Factory Method Pattern

The Factory Method example centers on an abstract Dialog.

Dialog.createButton() is the factory method.

Concrete creators select product implementations:

WindowsDialog → WindowsButton;
WebDialog → HTMLButton.

The shared render() workflow consumes the result through the Button interface.

This demonstrates product variation behind an abstract creator contract.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Singleton Pattern

The Singeleton Maven project contains the Singleton example and compiled Database/application classes.','["java","maven","interfaces","polymorphism","composition","creational-design-patterns","structure","technical","stack","major","engineering","work","builder","pattern","factory","method","singleton"]','["What This Repository Is","Repository Structure","Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-010-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":5,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-010-Creational-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":36,"source_line_start":36,"specificity_score":0.78,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Creational-Design-Patterns` is a compact Java learning repository that implements object-creation patterns as separate Maven projects.","text_sha256":"ba397359c55f232d28b7d14d048b4221c4b80efbaa45400adc42ec3813e4bd2d","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-010-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-010-Creational-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":38,"source_line_start":38,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The subject of the code is software architecture itself: object creation is isolated behind interfaces, abstract creators, builders, and controlled construction relationships.","text_sha256":"74538b019ba40a03502d3988fd0fd5ef022b1ebaf3797d1f93fd710e53452fe2","unit_id":"s004","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-010-s005-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s005","section_path":["Repository Structure"],"section_title":"Repository Structure","source_file":"repositori