INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-011-rd006',11,'Structural-Design-Patterns',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3929,21,284,'Section: Flyweight Pattern

Circles are keyed by color.

When getCircle(color) is called:

the factory checks the cache;

an existing circle is returned when present;

a new intrinsic color-specific circle is created and stored when required.

The main loop requests twenty circles while supplying varying external coordinates and radius values.

Section: Flyweight Pattern > Engineering concept represented

The example separates shared intrinsic state, represented by color-keyed circle instances, from changing extrinsic drawing state such as position.

It demonstrates object reuse through a factory-managed cache.

Section: Proxy Pattern

The Proxy example defines a shared Internet interface.

RealInternet performs the connection behavior.

ProxyInternet also implements Internet, owns a RealInternet, and checks a list of banned hostnames before delegation.

The main program attempts a permitted connection and a blocked connection.

Section: Proxy Pattern > Engineering concept represented

The proxy controls access to another implementation while preserving the same client-facing contract.

Section: Engineering Practices > Pattern Isolation

Each structural pattern has its own project boundary.

Section: Engineering Practices > Interface-Oriented Design

Interfaces such as Device, Graphic, Shape, and Internet define stable contracts around variation.

Section: Engineering Practices > Composition and Delegation

Composition is central to multiple examples:

Bridge stores a Device;

Composite stores child Graphic objects;

Decorator stores a wrapped Shape;

Proxy stores a real Internet implementation.

Section: Engineering Practices > Controlled Object Sharing

Flyweight uses a map-backed factory to reuse objects keyed by intrinsic state.

Section: Engineering Practices > Encapsulation of Subsystem Access

Facade moves concrete subsystem object handling behind a dedicated access layer.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Java

Java — strong evidence.

Interfaces — strong evidence.

Abstract classes — strong evidence.

Inheritance — strong evidence.

Polymorphism — strong evidence.

Composition — strong evidence.

Delegation — strong evidence.','["java","interfaces","inheritance","polymorphism","composition","delegation","flyweight","pattern","engineering","concept","represented","proxy","practices","isolation","interface-oriented","design","controlled","object","sharing","encapsulation","subsystem","access","skills","demonstrated"]','["Flyweight Pattern","Proxy Pattern","Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-011-s022-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["Flyweight Pattern"],"section_title":"Flyweight Pattern","source_file":"repositories/repo-011-Structural-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":208,"source_line_start":208,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Circles are keyed by color.","text_sha256":"8f3b6761c704b48a273a311ca23b33a2054b8e25318ae7411726c00bf92b91ef","unit_id":"s022","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-011-s022-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["Flyweight Pattern"],"section_title":"Flyweight Pattern","source_file":"repositories/repo-011-Structural-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":210,"source_line_start":210,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"When `getCircle(color)` is called:","text_sha256":"0bf6e27270e6bf025dc56d45cf3bcbae4b839a99de83b7cffff90ed7b43ff7dd","unit_id":"s022","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-011-s022-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["Flyweight Pattern"],"section_title":"Flyweight Pattern","source_file":"repositories/repo-011-Structural-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":212,"source_line_start":212,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"1. the factory checks the cache;","text_sha256":"33e9c8f2cb6c39b81f404b0b9ef3fd67740bd6eccaff5a85485117b7245e7e06","un