INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-012-rd003',12,'DMA-Model',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3831,15,241,'Section: What This Project Is

DMA-Model is a Verilog model of a small computer system in which a CPU and a DMA controller share address, data, and control buses while servicing peripheral transfer requests.

Section: System Scenario

The repository README describes a concrete sequence.

The CPU begins by executing a store-byte-style memory operation followed by R-format instructions.

A DMA request can arrive while the CPU is using the shared bus.

The CPU completes its active memory operation before handing control of the bus to the DMA controller.

The DMA controller then services external I/O transfers while the CPU can continue operations that do not require the shared memory bus.

Two peripheral workflows are described:

a disk-like I/O device transfers four values from one memory region to another;
a keypad request is serviced afterward through the DMA-assigned transfer path.

When simultaneous requests exist, fixed priority determines the serviced request.

Section: Repository Structure

Each HDL file represents a distinct system component.

Section: Technical Stack > Verilog

Verilog models:

synchronous state changes;

inout buses;

tri-state ownership;

one-hot request/acknowledge signaling;

fixed-priority arbitration;

register/memory arrays;

CPU instruction decoding;

integrated testbench stimulus.

Section: Technical Stack > HDL Simulation

DMAtb.v wires the system together and applies timed changes to peripheral enable signals.

The README also includes signal-scope imagery documenting the simulated behavior.

Section: DMA Controller

DMA.v exposes:

CLK;

HLDA;

four DREQ inputs;

shared data bus DB;

shared address bus AB;

shared control bus CB;

HRQ;

four DACK outputs.','["verilog","system","scenario","structure","technical","stack","simulation","controller"]','["What This Project Is","System Scenario","Repository Structure","Technical Stack","DMA Controller"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-012-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-012-DMA-Model/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`DMA-Model` is a Verilog model of a small computer system in which a CPU and a DMA controller share address, data, and control buses while servicing peripheral transfer requests.","text_sha256":"23842447e28ccabf114a6f08cb18f16d9a1bad703afff19aa2d0d4cc0989704f","unit_id":"s004","word_count":29},{"block_id":"repo-012-s005-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s005","section_path":["System Scenario"],"section_title":"System Scenario","source_file":"repositories/repo-012-DMA-Model/README.md","source_line_end":61,"source_line_start":61,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository README describes a concrete sequence.","text_sha256":"10f01deb58ca52620b7115359c32d556e830879d5d9c4f5fc2d2a0f8568af137","unit_id":"s005","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-012-s005-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s005","section_path":["System Scenario"],"section_title":"System Scenario","source_file":"repositories/repo-012-DMA-Model/README.md","source_line_end":63,"source_line_start":63,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The CPU begins by executing a store-byte-style memory operation followed by R-format instructions.","text_sha256":"bb651a6121813c6b995dccb2c72c1b8533577b393abcaebedad9d06f000bcc19","unit_id":"s005"