INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-015-rd003',15,'Go-Back-N-Protocol',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','repository_specific',0.3544,18,215,'Section: What This Project Is

Go-Back-N-Protocol explores reliable frame transmission using a sliding-window protocol.

an event-oriented Go-Back-N protocol implementation based around sequence numbers, sender/receiver window state, acknowledgements, and timeout retransmission;
a standalone console simulation that lets the user enter frames and then models successful transmissions, acknowledgement progression, a 10% error event, and retransmission of the affected window.

Section: Networking Model

The header defines:

sequence numbers;

packet structure;

frame kinds;

frame sequence number;

acknowledgement number;

payload;

protocol event types.

Visible event types include:

frame_arrival;

cksum_err;

timeout;

network_layer_ready.

The code therefore models networking as an event-driven state process rather than a simple data-copy loop.

Section: Static Protocol Configuration

GoBackN.h defines values including:

sender window size: 4;

maximum sequence number: 7;

packet size: 1024 bytes;

buffer size: 5;

simulated error denominator: 10;

output delay.

These constants make the simulated protocol behavior explicit.

Section: Go-Back-N Window Logic > Sender state

Protocol5.cpp maintains:

next_frame_to_send;

ack_expected;

outbound packet buffer;

nbuffered.

Section: Go-Back-N Window Logic > Receiver state

The receiver tracks:

frame_expected;
incoming frame r.

Section: Go-Back-N Window Logic > Circular sequence-number reasoning

The between(a, b, c) helper checks whether an acknowledgement lies inside a circular sequence-number interval.

This is important because sequence numbers wrap around at MAX_SEQ.

Section: Go-Back-N Window Logic > Sending

send_data() constructs a frame with:

sequence number;

