INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-017-rd007',17,'Neural-Networks-and-Deep-Learning-Coursera',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','testing_quality','positive','repository_specific',0.3409,2,112,'Section: Verification > Course-Supplied Public Tests

The assignments import public_tests.py and call named test helpers against completed functions.

The repository therefore contains an automated correctness-checking layer, although the test infrastructure itself is supplied by the course.

Section: Verification > Python Assertions

The preprocessing assignment includes assertions that verify flattened image values against expected arrays.

Section: Verification > Expected Outputs

Assignments include expected values for shapes, parameters, costs, and other intermediate results so completed code can be checked against known outputs.

Section: Verification > AutoGrader Contract

The assignment text documents constraints required by the Coursera grader, including preserving function signatures and graded-cell structure.

