INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-018-rd003',18,'Behavioral-Design-Patterns',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4125,23,239,'Section: What This Project Is

Behavioral-Design-Patterns is a Java learning repository that explores how object-oriented systems distribute responsibility and coordinate behavior between objects.

Rather than focusing on object construction or structural composition, these examples concentrate on runtime interaction:

The repository complements the earlier Creational and Structural design-pattern repositories and completes a broader period of explicit GoF-style pattern study.

Section: Repository Shape

Each implemented pattern is isolated in its own small executable project.

Section: Technical Stack > Java

Java provides the object-oriented mechanisms used throughout the examples:

interfaces;

abstract classes;

inheritance;

composition;

encapsulated state;

polymorphic dispatch;

collections.

Section: Technical Stack > Maven

Each pattern directory contains a pom.xml, giving the examples separate Maven project boundaries.

Generated target/classes and Maven compiler-status artifacts are committed for multiple examples, providing direct evidence that the projects were compiled through the Maven build path.

Section: Mediator

The Mediator example models a simplified air-traffic-control interaction.

The main participants are:

ATCMediator;

Flight;

Runway;

IATCMediator;

Command.

The flight and runway do not coordinate by directly owning each other''s behavior.

They communicate landing state through the mediator abstraction.

The mediator registers the active flight and runway and stores whether landing is permitted.

This demonstrates centralized coordination between peer objects and reduces direct coupling between the collaborating domain classes.

Section: Memento

The Memento example separates current state from saved snapshots.

The main roles are:

Originator — owns mutable state;

Memento — stores a state snapshot;

CareTaker — stores multiple mementos.','["java","interfaces","inheritance","composition","maven","behavioral-design-patterns","shape","technical","stack","mediator","memento"]','["What This Project Is","Repository Shape","Technical Stack","Mediator","Memento"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-018-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":4,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-018-Behavioral-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":44,"source_line_start":44,"specificity_score":0.72,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Behavioral-Design-Patterns` is a Java learning repository that explores how object-oriented systems distribute responsibility and coordinate behavior between objects.","text_sha256":"12bfa8649f0fb1d81e6c6d66c62fe585f4f55eb411bfdab48cfc306878d5bc24","unit_id":"s004","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-018-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-018-Behavioral-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":46,"source_line_start":46,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Rather than focusing on object construction or structural composition, these examples concentrate on runtime interaction:","text_sha256":"d4a792602a1d5028481299d57f397152db222b7c926f333223abafaa25da1b06","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-018-s004-b010","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-018-Behavioral-Design-Patterns/README.md","source_line_end":56,"source_line_start":56,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":