INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-019-rd005',19,'RADAR-Experiement-SENSOR-FUSION-TEAM',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3542,7,290,'Section: Simulation Ecosystem Integrations

The corpus treats these as repository-level integration artifacts rather than claiming that every plugin was personally implemented from source.

Section: 3D Environment Assets

The Models hierarchy includes:

road/asphalt textures;

material data;

a world model;

image resources.

These assets support a physically rendered simulation scene used by the experiment.

Section: Engineering Practices > Topic-Oriented Integration

Radar measurements are exposed as named ROS topics.

This turns simulator outputs into an interface that can be consumed by independently developed components.

Section: Engineering Practices > Signal-Level Interface Definition

The README documents the semantics and units of each radar field.

That is important in a multi-team integration context because downstream consumers need shared meaning, not only transport connectivity.

Section: Engineering Practices > Simulation Artifact Preservation

The repository preserves the model, world, sensor configuration, plugin configuration, and runtime artifacts together.

This creates a concrete snapshot of the simulation environment used for integration work.

Section: Engineering Practices > Cross-Team Boundary

The repository description explicitly says the radar experiment supports integration with other teams in the autonomous vehicle project.

The ROS topic layer acts as that cross-team technical boundary.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Simulation and Modeling

PreScan-style vehicle simulation workflow — strong repository evidence.

MATLAB/Simulink model workflow — strong evidence.

Radar sensor configuration — strong evidence.

3D simulation environment assets — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Robotics and Messaging

ROS initialization from MATLAB — strong evidence.

ROS topic publication — strong evidence.

ROS topic subscription — strong evidence.

Signal-oriented interface design — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Radar / Sensor Fusion

Radar range measurement integration — strong evidence.

Doppler velocity signals — strong evidence.

Azimuth/elevation signal handling — strong evidence.

Target identity signals — strong evidence.

Energy-loss signal handling — strong evidence.','["matlab","simulink","prescan","energy-loss","simulation","ecosystem","integrations","environment","assets","engineering","practices","topic-oriented","integration","signal-level","interface","definition","artifact","preservation","cross-team","boundary","skills","demonstrated","modeling","robotics"]','["Simulation Ecosystem Integrations","D Environment Assets","Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-019-s021-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s021","section_path":["Simulation Ecosystem Integrations"],"section_title":"Simulation Ecosystem Integrations","source_file":"repositories/repo-019-RADAR-Experiement-SENSOR-FUSION-TEAM/README.md","source_line_end":197,"source_line_start":197,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The corpus treats these as repository-level integration artifacts rather than claiming that every plugin was personally implemented from source.","text_sha256":"46323b5a4bbed4a9cdc99089c4766d2dba685bd90cc73f89bd7d15cd3d31b0e4","unit_id":"s021","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-019-s022-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["3D Environment Assets"],"section_title":"3D Environment Assets","source_file":"repositories/repo-019-RADAR-Experiement-SENSOR-FUSION-TEAM/README.md","source_line_end":201,"source_line_start":201,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The `Models` hierarchy includes:","text_sha256":"77233228d6a4abca2f4ba9146a7d20e99e9324a5ba6920d3544659cb2c16d36a","unit_id":"s022","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-019-s022-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["3D Environment Assets"],"section_title":"3D Environment Assets","source_file":"repositories/repo-019-RADAR-Experiement-SENSOR-FUSION-TEAM