INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-020-rd003',20,'Sedra-Platformer-Game',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4234,31,285,'Section: What This Project Is

Sedra-Platformer-Game is a Java desktop game prototype built directly with Swing/AWT-style rendering and event listeners.

The project implements a controllable protagonist with:

Section: Technical Stack > Java

Java provides the application runtime and object model.

Section: Technical Stack > Swing

JPanel is used as the rendering surface.

The panel overrides paintComponent(Graphics) and delegates drawing to the game controller.

Section: Technical Stack > AWT Graphics and Events

The project uses:

Graphics for rendering;

BufferedImage for sprite data;

KeyListener for keyboard input;

MouseListener and MouseMotionListener for mouse input.

Section: Technical Stack > ImageIO

ImageIO.read() loads the committed sprite sheet from the classpath.

Section: Runtime Game Loop

SedraPlatformer implements Runnable and starts a dedicated thread for the game loop.

The loop defines separate targets:

FPS_REQUIRED = 120;
UPS_REQUIRED = 200.

Nanosecond timing accumulators independently track when the next update and render should occur.

This is important because simulation updates and display refreshes are not treated as one identical cadence.

Section: Runtime Game Loop > Update Path

When the update accumulator reaches its threshold, the loop calls refresh().

That delegates to Protagonist.refresh().

Section: Runtime Game Loop > Render Path

When the frame accumulator reaches its threshold, the loop invokes mainPanel.repaint().

Swing then calls the panel''s paintComponent() method, which delegates drawing back through the game object.

Section: Runtime Game Loop > Runtime Instrumentation

Once per second, the loop prints measured frame and update counts:

fps: <count> ups: <count>

This provides a simple runtime observation mechanism for whether the loop is reaching its configured cadence.

Section: Keyboard Input

Keyboard implements KeyListener.

The movement controls are:

A → left;

S → down;

D → right;

W → up.

On key press, the corresponding movement flag becomes true.','["prototype","java","swing","technical","stack","graphics","events","imageio","runtime","game","loop","path","render","instrumentation","keyboard","input"]','["What This Project Is","Technical Stack","Runtime Game Loop","Keyboard Input"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-020-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":5,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-020-Sedra-Platformer-Game/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":41,"specificity_score":0.78,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Sedra-Platformer-Game` is a Java desktop game prototype built directly with Swing/AWT-style rendering and event listeners.","text_sha256":"7f7885292c2d69a28d1a517b807544c546c00fc34f2c1145138acc400ccac42d","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-020-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-020-Sedra-Platformer-Game/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The project implements a controllable protagonist with:","text_sha256":"3b3ff9afce2d0f14f685399401c9fbd87f1f337c851b4a9df64f3a7b67757fdc","unit_id":"s004","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-020-s007-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Technical Stack","Java"],"section_title":"Java","source_file":"repositories/repo-020-Sedra-Platformer-Game/README.md","source_line_end":81,"source_line_start":81,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Java provides the application runtime and object model.","text_sha256":"b9f713bea8a0ad1ac63f6bb6e7d