INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-021-rd003',21,'Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3692,30,257,'Section: What This Project Is

This repository implements and verifies a small stateful game around a three-bit multi-mode counter.

Landing on one boundary produces a winner event, while landing on the other produces a loser event.

When either score reaches the configured winning score, the design asserts gameover and reports which side won.

The repository combines functional design and explicit simulation verification in one SystemVerilog source.

Section: Design Interface

MMC_Game exposes:

Section: Design Interface > Inputs

clk;

rst;

two-bit ctrl;

init;

three-bit init_val.

Section: Design Interface > Outputs

three-bit count;

winner;

loser;

gameover;

two-bit who.

The interface therefore exposes both the immediate counter state and higher-level game outcome state.

Section: Symbolic Control Definitions

The source defines macros for control and outcome values.

Examples include:

UP_1;

UP_2;

DW_1;

DW_2;

LOSER_WON;

WINNER_WON;

WIN_SCORE.

Named definitions make the testbench and design easier to read than repeated raw bit patterns.

Section: Counter Modes > Increment by 1

UP_1 advances the counter one step and wraps from the maximum value back to the minimum.

Section: Counter Modes > Increment by 2

UP_2 advances two steps with special handling around the upper edge.

Section: Counter Modes > Decrement by 1

DW_1 decrements one step and wraps the minimum back to the maximum.

Section: Counter Modes > Decrement by 2

DW_2 decrements two steps with explicit edge cases near the lower boundary.

These modes deliberately create different visitation patterns over the counter states.

That visitation behavior is what drives winner/loser scoring.

Section: Initialization

When init is asserted, the current count is loaded from init_val.','["systemverilog","design","interface","inputs","outputs","symbolic","control","definitions","counter","modes","increment","decrement","initialization"]','["What This Project Is","Design Interface","Symbolic Control Definitions","Counter Modes","Initialization"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-021-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This repository implements and verifies a small stateful game around a three-bit multi-mode counter.","text_sha256":"7bc2112121bdcc9f5fd7d6e6ef0213c1cd54e2ad8fe20be0108eb8936d108b20","unit_id":"s004","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-021-s004-b009","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":51,"source_line_start":51,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Landing on one boundary produces a `winner` event, while landing on the other produces a `loser` event.","text_sha256":"16c226ae36967f05d13a8adfcaa6803d74aafe5f77cabf5bb6512447f2b9ea3b","unit_id":"s004","word_count":17},{"block_id":"repo-021-s004-b011","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-a