03adee14e6259ce2dc8eaa3746360e9b7c2316bd277fbb4eef4afe3f968","unit_id":"s023","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-021-s023-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s023","section_path":["Test Case 1: Increment by 2"],"section_title":"Test Case 1: Increment by 2","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":243,"source_line_start":241,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"```text\nwho == LOSER_WON\n```","text_sha256":"84c6038d03631a930e4621ca0b8edbcaf5d0393343fc83de66c5cb6f3e950cda","unit_id":"s023","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-021-s023-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s023","section_path":["Test Case 1: Increment by 2"],"section_title":"Test Case 1: Increment by 2","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":245,"source_line_start":245,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The result is stored into the first test-case slot.","text_sha256":"42b862e14d767890951ec0592344de39ed4ddd0084b00b0af1fa3d6cd9ce8d39","unit_id":"s023","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-021-s024-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s024","section_path":["Test Case 2: Increment by 1"],"section_title":"Test Case 2: Increment by 1","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":249,"source_line_start":249,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The design is allowed to run with one-step increments.","text_sha256":"1cee5df2f1ae5ac933a4cfd2192b877f6ed134079ab49b8e217464fd3e4eba5a","unit_id":"s024","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-021-s024-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s024","section_path":["Test Case 2: Increment by 1"],"section_title":"Test Case 2: Increment by 1","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":251,"source_line_start":251,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The scenario expects the loser score to reach the game threshold before the winner score.","text_sha256":"e54e7b776076848c19e5399580891c998fde3ca23021516b941f9dda800404d5","unit_id":"s024","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-021-s024-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s024","section_path":["Test Case 2: Increment by 1"],"section_title":"Test Case 2: Increment by 1","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":253,"source_line_start":253,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The testbench again checks the encoded game result.","text_sha256":"e229624a3f5aa75d2c6a7bc22765ffa492bb61ca3e34582d2c69b16bee188d3d","unit_id":"s024","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-021-s025-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s025","section_path":["Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary"],"section_title":"Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":257,"source_line_start":257,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The testbench initializes the counter near the upper boundary and repeatedly alternates decrement/increment operations so the count revisits the winning state.","text_sha256":"d08707968a7f544fe14488f2dc460b96f35ed6ab39a7c91f85a072e545e71dbf","unit_id":"s025","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-021-s025-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s025","section_path":["Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary"],"section_title":"Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":259,"source_line_start":259,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"After the sequence, it checks for `WINNER_WON`.","text_sha256":"37712f89b88c0fdb9fac11ceb6714575b46fa8abf98f31808894de0f02ad2ef4","unit_id":"s025","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-021-s025-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s025","section_path":["Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary"],"section_title":"Test Case 3: Alternating Around the Winner Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":261,"source_line_start":261,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This exercises score accumulation from a deliberately constructed trajectory rather than a single direct transition.","text_sha256":"156f29178513c952498de35efe418eda5ea4f991100cbfeece0abfbb51d02a15","unit_id":"s025","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-021-s026-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Test Case 4: Initialized Winner-Oriented Sequence"],"section_title":"Test Case 4: Initialized Winner-Oriented Sequence","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":265,"source_line_start":265,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The testbench asserts initialization and then runs a control mode intended to drive repeated winner events.","text_sha256":"d9e60d3e4f303506db0e6c2d5768d59ed33111270640ecb50fb64467af054f41","unit_id":"s026","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-021-s026-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Test Case 4: Initialized Winner-Oriented Sequence"],"section_title":"Test Case 4: Initialized Winner-Oriented Sequence","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":267,"source_line_start":267,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It checks the resulting winner identity after the simulation interval.","text_sha256":"667ec3af77b9aa967f77062750599498babe7f73053d76276c33ef392884e000","unit_id":"s026","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-021-s027-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s027","section_path":["Test Case 5: Mixed Increment Sequence"],"section_title":"Test Case 5: Mixed Increment Sequence","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":271,"source_line_start":271,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The stimulus alternates one-step and two-step increment modes across a long sequence.","text_sha256":"4ab2403d0467c54fa164da931ba70115d8cf7f35d12547325fe159fcf6d792c5","unit_id":"s027","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-021-s027-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s027","section_path":["Test Case 5: Mixed Increment Sequence"],"section_title":"Test Case 5: Mixed Increment Sequence","source_file":"repositories/repo-021-Multi-Mode-Counter-Winner-Loser-Game-SystemVerilog-Design-and-Verification/README.md","source_line_end":273,"source_line_start":273,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text