INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-022-rd004',22,'CPP_LIB',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3626,15,276,'Section: Technical Stack > C++

std::istringstream;

algorithms such as sorting;

integer arithmetic;

exception throwing;

loops and conditionals;

basic test/demo main functions.

Section: Technical Stack > Standard Library Text Processing

The irregular-string utility uses std::getline for multi-line collection and std::istringstream >> for whitespace-aware tokenization.

Section: Technical Stack > Standard Library Containers

std::vector is the primary collection structure for token lists, integer lists, and factor outputs.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Multi-Line Input Comparison

The largest utility reads arbitrary multi-line blocks until the sentinel STOP.

It then:

preserves the entered blocks;

tokenizes both;

records word counts;

compares every token from the first set with tokens in the second;

retains values present only in the first;

sorts those values;

converts each result into a SELECT * FROM ... line.

The repository README explicitly documents this tool as comparing first-input items against second-input items.

This is practical developer tooling for reconciling irregular text lists.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Prime Factorization

primeFactors(int n):

returns an empty factor list for 1;

throws std::invalid_argument for negative values;

repeatedly extracts factor 2;

searches odd factors up to sqrt(n);

appends a remaining prime factor.

The function demonstrates both input validation and a more efficient factor search than testing every integer through n.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Sieve-Based Prime Counting

_sieve(int n) initializes a boolean prime table, marks composite multiples beginning at p*p, and counts surviving primes below n.

This demonstrates the Sieve of Eratosthenes as a different prime-related strategy from direct divisor testing.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Direct Primality Check

is_prime(int n) tests candidate divisors only while i*i <= n.

The repository therefore preserves multiple number-theory approaches rather than one repeated implementation.','["sorting","technical","stack","standard","library","text","processing","containers","major","engineering","work","multi-line","input","comparison","prime","factorization","sieve-based","counting","primality","check"]','["Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-022-s011-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Technical Stack","C++"],"section_title":"C++","source_file":"repositories/repo-022-CPP_LIB/README.md","source_line_end":115,"source_line_start":115,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- `std::istringstream`;","text_sha256":"e56de54dfbe3756bc6fa8ec9f7d9b87afc7baeddeb93b2209abb8a63e25f164b","unit_id":"s011","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-022-s011-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Technical Stack","C++"],"section_title":"C++","source_file":"repositories/repo-022-CPP_LIB/README.md","source_line_end":116,"source_line_start":116,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- algorithms such as sorting;","text_sha256":"8b73d5f976b9ae4e1c7d2caab744ff11bc6ca33d018d97fae76433fcfbc4e9e7","unit_id":"s011","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-022-s011-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Technical Stack","C++"],"section_title":"C++","source_file":"repositories/repo-022-CPP_LIB/README.md","source_line_end":117,"source_line_start":117,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- integer arithmetic;","text_sha256":"60acc7bb0d09e8de2709e4bc043db377707305e7045c7db946d5026137fc7bb1","unit_id":"s011","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-022-s011-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","s