INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-022-rd005',22,'CPP_LIB',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','testing_quality','positive','repository_specific',0.4231,5,112,'Section: Major Engineering Work > String Trimming and Local Test Harness

Trim String.cpp includes a cleaner function that advances inward over leading/trailing blank characters and reconstructs the trimmed substring.

Its main function executes four concrete cases, increments a success counter, and prints the success ratio as a percentage.

That is direct evidence of small-scale expected-output verification inside a utility file.

Section: Verification > Embedded Expected-Output Checks

Trim String.cpp contains four explicit test cases for trimming behavior.

The program compares actual returned strings with expected strings and reports a success percentage.

Section: Verification > Console Demonstration

