INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-024-rd003',24,'CollisionGame',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3512,11,263,'Section: What This Project Is

CollisionGame is a single-page browser simulation containing 150 independently moving colored balls.

The result is an interactive particle/collision experiment implemented entirely in client-side browser code.

Section: Project Scope

The simulation includes:

dynamic DOM element creation;

150 moving entities;

random color generation;

random initial velocity;

absolute-position movement;

screen-boundary collision handling;

pairwise ball collision detection;

overlap separation;

angle-based velocity transformation;

cursor-proximity interaction;

fixed-timestep-style browser updates;

static deployment automation.

Section: Technical Stack > HTML

The page is a standalone HTML document with embedded style and script logic.

Section: Technical Stack > JavaScript

JavaScript implements:

element creation;

random generation;

movement state;

trigonometry;

Euclidean distance;

collision response;

mouse interaction;

periodic updates.

Section: Technical Stack > CSS

CSS defines circular ball geometry, absolute positioning, and visual transition behavior.

Section: Technical Stack > GitHub Actions

A workflow automatically deploys the repository to GitHub Pages on pushes to main.

Section: Technical Stack > GitHub Pages

The repository has Pages enabled and the workflow publishes the static site.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Dynamic Particle Creation

createBall() creates a new <div> element, assigns the ball class, chooses a random hexadecimal color, places the ball randomly inside the viewport, assigns random X/Y velocities, and appends it to the page.

A loop creates 150 such entities.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Continuous Motion Loop

setInterval(moveBalls, 16) updates the simulation approximately every 16 milliseconds.

moveBalls() applies each ball''s current velocity to its DOM position before handling boundaries and inter-ball collisions.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Boundary Collisions

When a ball reaches the left/right viewport boundary, its X velocity changes sign.','["html","javascript","trigonometry","scope","technical","stack","github","actions","pages","major","engineering","work","dynamic","particle","creation","continuous","motion","loop","boundary","collisions"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-024-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":34,"source_line_start":34,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`CollisionGame` is a single-page browser simulation containing 150 independently moving colored balls.","text_sha256":"0fdb8c837d14409d5c6f82717524c283facccfea7859398eb5160f15dab727f7","unit_id":"s004","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-024-s004-b011","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":48,"source_line_start":48,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The result is an interactive particle/collision experiment implemented entirely in client-side browser code.","text_sha256":"fb4f848cccb8ff2f9808cd37fba0a32dec9984e75d876ca276df539e1e086448","unit_id":"s004","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-024-s005-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s005","section_path":["Project Scope"],"section_title":"Project Scope","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":52,"source_line_start":52,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The simulati