INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-024-rd005',24,'CollisionGame',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','interpretive',0.3483,5,292,'Section: Major Engineering Work > Boundary Collisions

When it reaches the top/bottom boundary, its Y velocity changes sign.

This keeps the simulation bounded to the browser viewport.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Pairwise Collision Detection

handleCollisions() compares every ball with every other ball.

For each pair it computes:

center-to-center X difference;

center-to-center Y difference;

Euclidean distance through Math.hypot;

minimum non-overlapping distance from ball radii.

A collision is recognized when actual distance becomes smaller than the required minimum distance.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Overlap Resolution

The final implementation computes overlap distance and separates the two balls along the collision angle.

This is an important refinement over simply changing velocity while leaving visual elements interpenetrating.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Collision Velocity Adjustment

The final commit replaces an earlier simpler collision rule with angle-based calculations.

It derives:

movement angles;

velocity magnitudes;

velocity components relative to the collision axis;

resulting speed components;

transformed X/Y velocities.

The commit history therefore shows iterative refinement of collision behavior rather than one static upload.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Mouse Interaction

A mousemove handler computes cursor distance from each ball.

Balls inside a 40-pixel radius are displaced according to the mouse-relative angle while their new coordinates are clamped to viewport bounds.

This adds direct user interaction to the simulation.

Section: Engineering Practices > Incremental Refinement

Several focused commits modify the same collision logic during one development session.

Section: Engineering Practices > Explicit State Per Entity

Each generated DOM node carries speedX and speedY, keeping motion state associated with the rendered object.

Section: Engineering Practices > Boundary Clamping

Cursor-driven movement clamps new positions to valid viewport coordinates.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Algorithms and Mathematics

Euclidean distance — strong evidence.

Collision detection — strong evidence.

Overlap resolution — strong evidence.','["major","engineering","work","boundary","collisions","pairwise","collision","detection","overlap","resolution","velocity","adjustment","mouse","interaction","practices","incremental","refinement","state","entity","clamping","skills","demonstrated","algorithms","mathematics"]','["Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-024-s016-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Boundary Collisions"],"section_title":"Boundary Collisions","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":144,"source_line_start":144,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"When it reaches the top/bottom boundary, its Y velocity changes sign.","text_sha256":"4f10fda9baf820a7fc505b5da92f16470980d7423f664984fb7cf0b3634a249f","unit_id":"s016","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-024-s016-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Boundary Collisions"],"section_title":"Boundary Collisions","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":146,"source_line_start":146,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This keeps the simulation bounded to the browser viewport.","text_sha256":"31d2bc8b036f5909fdf1e656c24984a86b35096c17c08f505b44299adb72b478","unit_id":"s016","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-024-s017-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Pairwise Collision Detection"],"section_title":"Pairwise Collision Detection","source_file":"repositories/repo-024-CollisionGame/README.md","source_line_end":150,"source_line_start":150,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`han