INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-026-rd012',26,'Sensors',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','repository_specific',0.437,24,295,'Section: Skills Demonstrated > Languages and Tools

C++ — strong evidence.

Python — strong evidence.

NumPy — strong evidence.

Matplotlib — strong evidence.

Jupyter Notebook — strong evidence.

CMake — repository-level course infrastructure evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Engineering Practices

Processing-pipeline decomposition — strong evidence.

Parameter tuning — strong evidence.

Runtime timing — strong evidence.

Experiment result documentation — strong evidence.

Section: Capability Developed

Sensors broadens the portfolio from software and digital systems into autonomous-vehicle perception.

radar reduces electromagnetic/sampled-signal behavior into range and velocity estimates;
LIDAR turns spatial point returns into filtered road geometry and clustered obstacles.

Even with the course-infrastructure boundary, the hands-on technical surface is substantial and introduces several perception and signal-processing capabilities not previously present together.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

KD-tree-backed Euclidean point-cloud clustering;

LIDAR 3D obstacle bounding boxes;

radar maximum-range calculation;

beat-frequency-to-range calculation;

The earlier RADAR team repository already establishes radar/autonomous-vehicle collaboration; this repository adds concrete radar math exercises and detailed LIDAR point-cloud processing.

Section: Historical Significance

Sensors marks a major expansion of the autonomous-systems thread.

It records practical engagement with both radar signal concepts and LIDAR obstacle-processing pipelines, while also providing unusually explicit evidence of course-supplied infrastructure.

That makes it useful for later RAG queries about both technical capability and how coursework-based evidence should be weighted.

Section: Overall Repository Narrative

Sensors is a course-derived autonomous-vehicle sensing repository combining a radar notebook with a PCL-based LIDAR obstacle-detection project.

The radar work computes wavelength, radar range, chirp bandwidth, sweep time, beat-frequency range, Doppler velocity, and frequency-domain behavior of noisy sampled signals.

The LIDAR work filters point clouds through voxel grids and spatial crops, removes ego-vehicle points, segments road planes with PCL RANSAC, clusters obstacles with KD-tree-backed Euclidean extraction, generates bounding boxes, streams PCD frames, and records simulation results under changing sensor parameters.','["python","numpy","matplotlib","radar","lidar","beat-frequency","kd-tree","obstacle-detection","cmake","skills","demonstrated","languages","tools","engineering","practices","capability","developed","portfolio","evolution","context","historical","significance","narrative"]','["Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Repository Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-026-s060-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s060","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Languages and Tools"],"section_title":"Languages and Tools","source_file":"repositories/repo-026-Sensors/README.md","source_line_end":486,"source_line_start":486,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- **C++ — strong evidence.**","text_sha256":"3746ef4436ea4e73ba852f3f1b3ea4a447a43a816b2dd3ae7bda691e26539b95","unit_id":"s060","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-026-s060-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s060","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Languages and Tools"],"section_title":"Languages and Tools","source_file":"repositories/repo-026-Sensors/README.md","source_line_end":487,"source_line_start":487,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- **Python — strong evidence.**","text_sha256":"2d56f2fb71faa785c47f3fa33ecb1f76ebd3756933a8190a25aa8bb3de0a6cf9","unit_id":"s060","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-026-s060-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s060","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Language