INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-029-rd003',29,'Camera',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4045,20,231,'Section: What This Project Is

Camera is a collection of autonomous-driving perception experiments organized into three major areas:

lidar and object detection,

time-to-collision estimation.

camera-based TTC,
lidar-based TTC.

The repository combines Jupyter notebooks with binary .dat inputs and image artifacts.

This gives it the shape of a technical lab workspace rather than a single standalone application.

Section: Repository Structure

The checked-in tree includes:

This organization separates perception problems by sensing modality and analysis purpose.

Section: Technical Workflow

At a high level, the repository contains several perception workflows:

and:

The surrounding notebooks broaden the workspace toward feature tracking and lidar/object-detection experimentation.

Section: Camera-Based Time-to-Collision

TTC/Camera/CameraTTC.ipynb contains directly inspectable Python implementation.

The notebook loads binary keypoint and match data.

It reconstructs:

cv2.KeyPoint objects,
cv2.DMatch objects.

The binary reader uses Python’s struct module to unpack serialized records.

That means the notebook is not only performing TTC mathematics; it also bridges previously serialized native/OpenCV-style structures into Python objects.

Section: Binary Keypoint Parsing

The camera TTC notebook implements helpers for reading packed binary data.

Keypoint records are interpreted as:

x,

y,

size,

angle,

response,

octave,

class ID.

Match records are interpreted as:

query index,

train index,

image index,

distance.

Those values are then reconstructed into OpenCV objects.

This is concrete cross-representation data handling.

Section: Camera TTC Executed Result

The notebook executes the implementation against the checked-in keypoint and match data with a 10 FPS frame rate.','["python","opencv","autonomous-driving","lidar","time-to-collision","structure","technical","workflow","camera-based","binary","keypoint","parsing","camera","executed","result"]','["What This Project Is","Repository Structure","Technical Workflow","Camera-Based Time-to-Collision","Binary Keypoint Parsing","Camera TTC Executed Result"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-029-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-029-Camera/README.md","source_line_end":26,"source_line_start":26,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Camera` is a collection of autonomous-driving perception experiments organized into three major areas:","text_sha256":"7a72305a268029e9624f64c3d5eab6f06d801bf12e62c7e28bb27ba8048d2555","unit_id":"s003","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-029-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-029-Camera/README.md","source_line_end":29,"source_line_start":29,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"2. lidar and object detection,","text_sha256":"81bb30fbc88be90194a63c8d54e7c6907a57cbe86bb8036a9cea6ae43b506099","unit_id":"s003","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-029-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-029-Camera/README.md","source_line_end":30,"source_line_start":30,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"3. time-to-col