INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-032-rd003',32,'MachineLearning',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3469,20,227,'Section: What This Project Is

MachineLearning contains a single Jupyter notebook explicitly named:

FirstMLProject.ipynb

The notebook builds a regression workflow for predicting molecular aqueous solubility.

logS

MolLogP,

MolWt,

NumRotatableBonds,

AromaticProportion.

The preserved dataframe contains 1,144 rows and five columns including the target.

Section: Data Source and Preparation

The notebook loads a CSV dataset with pandas.

It uses:

pd.read_csv(...)

against a publicly hosted molecular-solubility dataset.

The target column logS is separated from the explanatory variables.

Conceptually:

Section: Dataset Shape

The preserved notebook output shows:

1,144 observations,

four input descriptors,

one logS target.

This provides direct data-scale evidence.

Section: Model Building

The model is scikit-learn LinearRegression.

The workflow is explicit:

Predictions are then produced for both:

training data,
test data.

This makes the notebook a complete supervised-regression workflow rather than only a dataset visualization.

Section: Evaluation Metrics

The notebook evaluates the regression model with:

mean squared error,
R² score.

It calculates both metrics independently for training and test partitions.

Preserved outputs include:

Section: Evaluation Metrics > Training

MSE: approximately 0.97397
R²: approximately 0.77658

Section: Generalization Comparison

Because the notebook records both train and test metrics, it supports basic generalization reasoning.

The test MSE is higher than training MSE.

The test R² is lower than training R².

The repository therefore demonstrates the practice of evaluating a model on unseen held-out data rather than judging it only on the training set.','["regression","pandas","scikit-learn","molecular-solubility","dataframe","data","source","preparation","dataset","shape","model","building","evaluation","metrics","training","generalization","comparison"]','["What This Project Is","Data Source and Preparation","Dataset Shape","Model Building","Evaluation Metrics","Generalization Comparison"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-032-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-032-MachineLearning/README.md","source_line_end":25,"source_line_start":25,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`MachineLearning` contains a single Jupyter notebook explicitly named:","text_sha256":"3f9c20560bf0e00e015d26f8398a201b901a38153a35f9b4654ce7910cd6a9ad","unit_id":"s003","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-032-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-032-MachineLearning/README.md","source_line_end":27,"source_line_start":27,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"`FirstMLProject.ipynb`","text_sha256":"c96abf0b9cecb4a7cd4afe9174bcb0704ef5fda36dd0cdea2ffd54fdaae747db","unit_id":"s003","word_count":1},{"block_id":"repo-032-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-032-MachineLearning/README.md","source_line_end":29,"source_line_start":29,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_fre