INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-033-rd003',33,'Port-AUTOSAR-ARM',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4196,21,199,'Section: What This Project Is

Port-AUTOSAR-ARM is a low-level embedded C codebase built around AUTOSAR-style driver organization for a TM4C123GH6PM microcontroller.

The repository also integrates:

GPT / SysTick,

The project therefore represents a layered embedded software stack rather than a single GPIO function.

Section: Repository Structure

Important files include:

The file layout follows the familiar embedded-driver separation between:

API headers,

implementation,

compile-time configuration,

post-build configuration,

register access,

upper-layer abstractions.

Section: AUTOSAR Versioning

Port.h explicitly declares:

software version 1.0.1,
AUTOSAR release 4.0.3.

The code also performs compile-time compatibility checks between modules.

For example, the Port header validates the AUTOSAR version of Std_Types.h.

It similarly checks the Port configuration header against the Port module version.

These checks use preprocessor #error directives.

This is concrete compile-time interface/version validation.

Section: Development Error Tracing

The Port API defines DET error codes for cases such as:

invalid pin ID,

unchangeable direction,

invalid configuration,

invalid mode,

unchangeable mode,

uninitialized module use,

null pointer input.

Port.c conditionally integrates Det_ReportError when development-error detection is enabled.

That is concrete defensive embedded-driver design.

Section: Configuration Model

The Port module uses typed configuration structures.

Pin configuration carries fields including:

direction,

mode,

resistor setting,

runtime changeability.

The module also exposes a Port_ConfigType.','["tm4c123","autosar","gpio","systick","structure","versioning","development","error","tracing","configuration","model"]','["What This Project Is","Repository Structure","AUTOSAR Versioning","Development Error Tracing","Configuration Model"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-033-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":4,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":42,"source_line_start":42,"specificity_score":0.72,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Port-AUTOSAR-ARM` is a low-level embedded C codebase built around AUTOSAR-style driver organization for a TM4C123GH6PM microcontroller.","text_sha256":"64e09b3051662f4df53c3b3d32bebb431809e26e7b284b2f74df7f79553f838f","unit_id":"s003","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-033-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":46,"source_line_start":46,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The repository also integrates:","text_sha256":"62a6e3d3a3303d1e9e05453491b01c5d3985a37fb453c6fe2d1aeef587c17e83","unit_id":"s003","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-033-s003-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":49,"source_line_start":49,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- GPT / SysTick,","text_sha256":"d29c512184346c26b02232f92360c381ede262834f8cc88fc349edefef824639","unit_id":"s003","