INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-033-rd004',33,'Port-AUTOSAR-ARM',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4089,17,222,'Section: Configuration Model

Port_PBcfg.c defines a concrete post-build configuration object.

Most channels use a default configuration, while named application configurations such as LED and SWITCH are inserted into the channel array.

Section: Post-Build Configuration

Port_PBcfg.c independently declares its software and AUTOSAR versions.

It validates those versions against the Port API header before defining Port_Configuration.

This separates generated/configuration-style data from driver logic.

The pattern is important because configuration becomes data passed into initialization rather than being buried entirely in imperative startup code.

Section: TM4C123 Register Mapping

Port_Regs.h defines memory-mapped base addresses for GPIO ports A through F.

It also defines register offsets including:

DATA,

DIR,

alternate-function selection,

pull-up,

pull-down,

digital enable,

lock,

commit,

analog mode,

port control.

Port.c computes register addresses by adding those offsets to the selected port base.

This is direct bare-metal memory-mapped I/O.

Section: Port Initialization

Port_Init receives a configuration pointer.

For each configured pin, the implementation:

selects the correct GPIO base address;

enables the corresponding port clock;

handles protected/special pins;

applies direction;

applies initial output value;

applies input pull-up or pull-down configuration;

configures the selected pin mode.

The initialization therefore turns declarative configuration data into actual hardware-register state.

Section: Pin Direction

Output pins cause the corresponding direction bit to be set.

Input pins clear the direction bit.

For inputs, resistor configuration determines whether pull-up or pull-down registers are enabled.','["bare-metal","tm4c123","autosar","gpio","configuration","model","post-build","mapping","port","initialization","direction"]','["Configuration Model","Post-Build Configuration","TM4C123 Register Mapping","Port Initialization","Pin Direction"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-033-s008-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Configuration Model"],"section_title":"Configuration Model","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":163,"source_line_start":163,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Port_PBcfg.c` defines a concrete post-build configuration object.","text_sha256":"62452598f627d236c60b3d851d80690cfecfeee229a9658db7519983755f1518","unit_id":"s008","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-033-s008-b009","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Configuration Model"],"section_title":"Configuration Model","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":165,"source_line_start":165,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Most channels use a default configuration, while named application configurations such as `LED` and `SWITCH` are inserted into the channel array.","text_sha256":"852c0df48e17c595d6e3be42df00e4df9e7c16d6193507bff7b43fa271e10f11","unit_id":"s008","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-033-s009-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Post-Build Configuration"],"section_title":"Post-Build Configuration","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":169,"source_line_start":169,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Port_PBcfg.c` independently 