rt Initialization"],"section_title":"Port Initialization","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":210,"source_line_start":210,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"7. configures the selected pin mode.","text_sha256":"baa7df493b9a554456da2a5c1c55c988b76d776cea7c21094154cf9516f3cade","unit_id":"s011","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-033-s011-b010","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Port Initialization"],"section_title":"Port Initialization","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":212,"source_line_start":212,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The initialization therefore turns declarative configuration data into actual hardware-register state.","text_sha256":"9e41fe6e19683c54d892fb3f2177afbac638bbb8f577d3aaf330cb6f71890520","unit_id":"s011","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-033-s012-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Pin Direction"],"section_title":"Pin Direction","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":216,"source_line_start":216,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Output pins cause the corresponding direction bit to be set.","text_sha256":"cff58603526a866552f48853dffd3b3c55180fea3f1601ceccf6682e51ba3598","unit_id":"s012","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-033-s012-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Pin Direction"],"section_title":"Pin Direction","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":218,"source_line_start":218,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Input pins clear the direction bit.","text_sha256":"8cb148c25d19dc233705b48c79daa55c0ad1dd15658bf3547403bc829bb70a3d","unit_id":"s012","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-033-s012-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Pin Direction"],"section_title":"Pin Direction","source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","source_line_end":220,"source_line_start":220,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"For inputs, resistor configuration determines whether pull-up or pull-down registers are enabled.","text_sha256":"049ec43a71e367e2b3606fe66bf22990edd2c6ade6006e08533f5f03c09af70f","unit_id":"s012","word_count":12}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-033-Port-AUTOSAR-ARM/README.md","document_text_sha256":"daf00202e68759e6871341d04e92927b563e1b85c10358e832286d2c9e3923a0","earliest_source_line":163,"embedding_text_sha256":"55901f8904eda72c1bc2dcfda2c2ba75b7df9f9debdcd3c256e932759ac5d694","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"6dd6f75e67a345006b20f763a9b234a7856badd614c9de9c55c203734ce207a5","repository_source_line_end":553,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-033-rd005',33,'Port-AUTOSAR-ARM',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','interpretive',0.3423,3,193,'Section: Pin Direction

Initial output level is also applied during setup.

Section: Pin Multiplexing

The Port driver contains explicit mode handling for multiple peripheral functions.

Positively evidenced modes include:

DIO,

UART,

ADC,

CAN,

SSI,

I²C,

PWM,

USB,

QEI,

GPT,

NMI,

analog comparator.

The driver manipulates:

alternate-function selection,

digital enable,

analog-mode selection,

port-control mux bits,

open-drain state where relevant.

This is a substantial pin-multiplexing implementation.

Section: DIO Mode

Digital I/O mode:

disables analog functionality,

disables alternate function,

clears the pin-control mux field,

enables digital functionality.

Section: UART Mode

UART configuration enables:

alternate function,

digital functionality,

appropriate port-control mux selection.

The implementation accounts for different mux values on specific pins.

Section: ADC Mode

ADC pin setup:

enables alternate function,

configures the pin as input,

disables digital mode,

enables analog mode.

Section: CAN Mode

CAN mode configures alternate function and chooses the correct mux values for different supported pins.

Section: SSI Mode

SSI setup enables alternate function and digital behavior and applies pin-control mux selection.

Section: I²C Mode

I²C configuration includes alternate-function and digital enable plus open-drain behavior.

Section: PWM, USB, QEI and GPT Modes

