INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-033-rd008',33,'Port-AUTOSAR-ARM',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3425,11,235,'Section: Engineering Practices > Compile-Time Compatibility Checks

Software and AUTOSAR versions are compared through preprocessor logic.

Section: Engineering Practices > Symbolic Hardware Access

Named base addresses and register offsets replace unexplained literals throughout core driver logic.

Section: Engineering Practices > Typed Configuration

Enums and structures model direction, resistance, changeability and pin mode.

Section: Engineering Practices > Error Detection

DET-compatible error IDs make invalid API use explicit.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > AUTOSAR-Style Engineering

AUTOSAR release metadata,

module/service IDs,

standard types,

DET error reporting,

pre-compile configuration,

post-build configuration,

version compatibility checks.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Microcontroller I/O

GPIO direction,

pull-up/pull-down,

digital enable,

analog mode,

alternate functions,

pin multiplexing.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Peripheral Configuration

UART,

ADC,

CAN,

SSI,

I²C,

PWM,

USB,

QEI,

GPT,

NMI.

Section: Capability Developed

It demonstrates moving from application-level embedded C to a configurable driver architecture with standardized interfaces, defensive checks and direct hardware register manipulation.

The broader repository also shows integration of that driver into a larger embedded software stack containing DIO, timer services, application abstractions and startup/platform support.

Section: Historical Portfolio Significance

This is the earliest processed repository with direct AUTOSAR 4.0.3-style MCAL conventions.

It is also the earliest processed repository with a substantial owner-attributed configurable Port driver for the TM4C123 platform.

The project introduces:

DET-style error reporting,

post-build driver configuration,

compile-time AUTOSAR version checks,

multi-peripheral GPIO pin multiplexing.

Section: Overall Project Narrative

