Repository: kirolossedra/Simple-Calculator','["identity"]','["Repository Identity"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-035-s001-b001","canonical_categories":["identity"],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s001","section_path":["Repository Identity"],"section_title":"Repository Identity","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":5,"source_line_start":5,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- **Repository:** `kirolossedra/Simple-Calculator`","text_sha256":"ba419aa9204076019641896d179b782a6fa917efd051e910fc3244a302bc5574","unit_id":"s001","word_count":3}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","document_text_sha256":"c04b598a505981e67021a26cebd636a4dad56cc1fb707c236de55d2c55aaa473","earliest_source_line":5,"embedding_text_sha256":"85ae25f2e8d59b63e85b911694ee86e4474d12e49fb0ed3922bfe25b301d5904","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"f6f6a31fa8a2aa7ecd8bafd82cb53fc30b932dfd6412997c031d04d28bb1cc8f","repository_source_line_end":169,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-035-rd002',35,'Simple-Calculator',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3541,13,303,'Section: What This Project Is

Simple-Calculator is an AVR calculator application that accepts one arithmetic expression from a matrix keypad and displays both input and result on an LCD.

The repository is layered into Calculator.c plus GPIO, keypad, LCD, shared type, and macro modules.

The main calculator source explicitly identifies kirol as its author.

Several supporting drivers, including GPIO and keypad, explicitly credit Mohamed Tarek. The corpus therefore treats the calculator parsing and application workflow as personally attributable while preserving the external provenance of those support modules.

Section: Functional Scope

The calculator supports one binary arithmetic operation between two non-negative integer operands.

Implemented operations are addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.

The user enters characters through the keypad until = is received, and the result is rendered on the LCD.

Section: Operator Detection

After input collection, the application scans the buffered expression.

A stored value greater than 9 is interpreted as the operator character, and its position is recorded as OpIndex.

That divides the expression into left digits, one operator, and right digits.

The design is intentionally narrow and targeted at one arithmetic operator per expression.

Section: Manual Decimal Parsing

The source manually reconstructs integer operands from individual keypad digits.

For each digit it builds the appropriate decimal place value by multiplying a temporary accumulator by 10 for every remaining digit position.

The right operand is reconstructed with the same technique.

The parser therefore does not depend on atoi, strtol, dynamic strings, or an expression library.

Section: Arithmetic Dispatch

The operator stored at RAM[OpIndex] drives a switch.

The application performs addition, subtraction, multiplication, or floating-point division.

Integer-style results are sent to LCD_longToString.

Division casts both operands to double and uses LCD_doubleToString.

Section: Interaction Reset

After displaying a result, the application waits for a particular keypad code before clearing the LCD and beginning another calculation.','["gpio","functional","scope","operator","detection","manual","decimal","parsing","arithmetic","dispatch","interaction","reset"]','["What This Project Is","Functional Scope","Operator Detection","Manual Decimal Parsing","Arithmetic Dispatch","Interaction Reset"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-035-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":15,"source_line_start":15,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Simple-Calculator` is an AVR calculator application that accepts one arithmetic expression from a matrix keypad and displays both input and result on an LCD.","text_sha256":"b9b9efeb2e49cb7fad402d90d24a55c518a236a8a539209888eb9024c0bc7382","unit_id":"s002","word_count":24},{"block_id":"repo-035-s002-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":17,"source_line_start":17,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository is layered into `Calculator.c` plus GPIO, keypad, LCD, shared type, and macro modules.","text_sha256":"bc65a00cf0942182774bb5c1c1874eb43dd9d5155b3665e273dc2bd3469083cc","unit_id":"s002","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-035-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end"