The application creates a fixed 30-byte RAM buffer.

The read() function performs the interaction cycle: displays a prompt, waits for keypad readiness, reads keys, echoes numbers or operators, stores keys into the buffer, and stops acquisition when = is pressed.

A counter records the amount of expression content captured.','["input","pipeline"]','["Input Pipeline"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-035-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Input Pipeline"],"section_title":"Input Pipeline","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":33,"source_line_start":33,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application creates a fixed 30-byte RAM buffer.","text_sha256":"d6e76470e3665d36656d9b9d1e093a7dee60ed23337ae86681c6a97e2a1bdfb2","unit_id":"s004","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-035-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Input Pipeline"],"section_title":"Input Pipeline","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":35,"source_line_start":35,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The `read()` function performs the interaction cycle: displays a prompt, waits for keypad readiness, reads keys, echoes numbers or operators, stores keys into the buffer, and stops acquisition when `=` is pressed.","text_sha256":"f1dc29414015042b6a7ac890efd9b111dcbbbd6a6bdecc6af07e5590ba88ebbc","unit_id":"s004","word_count":32},{"block_id":"repo-035-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Input Pipeline"],"section_title":"Input Pipeline","source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"A counter records the amount of expression content captured.","text_sha256":"45d01a970caf0be73db6d9bcffd506f5cd2544c9cb5578f94538beaed3e470e4","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-035-Simple-Calculator/README.md","document_text_sha256":"3744349b4784bc469a8ac85f4eb95cf66801edd1b4350ef362461febca1aa15c","earliest_source_line":33,"embedding_text_sha256":"192258cc034720059852292e00aef693fb6ae05d8d482859ab016c33915de40c","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"f6f6a31fa8a2aa7ecd8bafd82cb53fc30b932dfd6412997c031d04d28bb1cc8f","repository_source_line_end":169,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-035-rd004',35,'Simple-Calculator',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3733,30,283,'Section: Interaction Reset

main() initializes the LCD and repeatedly calls the application read/compute/display cycle.

Section: Hardware Abstraction Structure

The calculator does not manipulate all pins directly in the application source.

Instead, it consumes keypad and LCD interfaces built over GPIO.

This is an early layered embedded structure in which application semantics sit above lower-level peripheral handling.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Fixed-Buffer Processing

Input is captured into a bounded RAM buffer with explicit indices.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Numeric Parsing

Decimal integers are reconstructed manually from individual keypad digits.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Control Flow

A small parser identifies the operator and dispatches arithmetic through a switch.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Hardware Abstraction Consumption

The application sits above GPIO/keypad/LCD layers instead of putting all register logic in one source file.

Section: Capability Developed

Compared with a register-level exercise, the focus moves upward toward input semantics, parsing, application state, presentation, and reuse of device abstractions.

Section: Portfolio Evolution

Simple-Calculator follows the previous day''s AVR stopwatch.

The stopwatch emphasized interrupts and timer hardware.

The calculator emphasizes peripheral abstraction, interactive input, numeric parsing, and LCD presentation.

Together they show two distinct embedded application styles: asynchronous timing/control and user-driven input/compute/output.

Section: Overall Project Narrative

Simple-Calculator turns a keypad and LCD into a self-contained arithmetic interface.

The user enters a fixed-format expression, the application stores keypad values, locates the operator, reconstructs decimal operands manually, executes the chosen operation, and renders the result.

Source headers make it possible to distinguish personally authored application logic from externally attributed support drivers.

