Repository: kirolossedra/Fan-Controller','["identity"]','["Repository Identity"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-036-s001-b001","canonical_categories":["identity"],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s001","section_path":["Repository Identity"],"section_title":"Repository Identity","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":5,"source_line_start":5,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- **Repository:** `kirolossedra/Fan-Controller`","text_sha256":"7704fb7ca37641e01f0461a58bdfe328322f728a977106b9744caa45cbe31a3f","unit_id":"s001","word_count":3}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","document_text_sha256":"e6f9511aff38965dd18fe43ea108b4f90d2766dfdd6976fc2ec60d05878ab4fd","earliest_source_line":5,"embedding_text_sha256":"f75657add1e91eda52f58c7857e5c90b838f06a53fcff228ee37a66f4f2b1d87","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"bfd178ae9cc2fb03168baaf76d577be049e0cb84588267baa27a6dfa17a6fa03","repository_source_line_end":191,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-036-rd002',36,'Fan-Controller',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3398,13,290,'Section: What This Project Is

Fan-Controller is an embedded control application that reads temperature from an LM35 sensor and maps temperature ranges to fan operating state and speed.

The implementation combines ADC conversion, LM35 temperature acquisition, DC motor control, PWM duty-cycle generation, LCD status display, and GPIO support.

The ADC, DC motor, and PWM modules inspected in the repository also carry kirol authorship headers.

Section: System Behavior

The application continuously samples temperature.

Its implemented policy is:

Temperature; Fan state; Commanded speed

< 30 °C; OFF; stopped

30–59 °C; ON / clockwise; 25%

60–89 °C; ON / clockwise; 50%

90–119 °C; ON / clockwise; 75%

>= 120 °C; ON / clockwise; 100%

The LCD simultaneously displays whether the fan is ON or OFF and the current measured temperature.

Section: Control Strategy

The controller is threshold based rather than continuously proportional.

Temperature is quantized into four active speed regions plus an off region.

This makes every output condition explicit and inspectable.

Section: User Feedback

The LCD functions as operational telemetry.

At startup the application establishes fixed labels for fan state and temperature.

During the loop it updates those positions and writes a trailing space after shorter temperature values so stale digits are not left visible.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Sensor Integration

An LM35 sensor is translated into application-level temperature.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > PWM Motor Control

Timer0 PWM drives explicit motor-speed percentages.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Layered Drivers

Application policy, sensor logic, ADC, motor logic, PWM, LCD, and GPIO are separated.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Rule-Based Control

Temperature bands map deterministically to actuator commands.

Section: Engineering Skills Demonstrated > Runtime Telemetry

LCD output exposes current system state during execution.

Section: Portfolio Evolution

Chronologically, this project immediately follows Simple-Calculator.','["timer0","gpio","system","behavior","control","strategy","user","feedback","engineering","skills","demonstrated","sensor","integration","motor","layered","drivers","rule-based","runtime","telemetry","portfolio","evolution"]','["What This Project Is","System Behavior","Control Strategy","User Feedback","Engineering Skills Demonstrated","Portfolio Evolution"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-036-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":15,"source_line_start":15,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Fan-Controller` is an embedded control application that reads temperature from an LM35 sensor and maps temperature ranges to fan operating state and speed.","text_sha256":"1d911ff9531020a3c3be65828ccf1ac15621cb4aa0de598161a653e37eb59371","unit_id":"s002","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-036-s002-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":17,"source_line_start":17,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The implementation combines ADC conversion, LM35 temperature acquisition, DC motor control, PWM duty-cycle generation, LCD status display, and GPIO support.","text_sha256":"328e11995b17677d265852d1156ddf5f02f359202f676139774cc908bef17b8e","unit_id":"s002","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-036-s002-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project I