INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-036-rd003',36,'Fan-Controller',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','architecture_system_design','positive','repository_specific',0.4148,12,165,'Section: Layered Embedded Architecture > Application Layer

MINI_PROJECT_3.c owns the temperature-to-actuator policy and coordinates the sensor, motor, ADC, and display.

Section: Layered Embedded Architecture > Sensor Layer

The LM35 module supplies temperature to the application instead of exposing arbitrary raw ADC values directly to main().

Section: Layered Embedded Architecture > ADC Layer

adc.c configures the AVR ADC.

The owner-attributed implementation selects reference behavior through configuration, sets the prescaler, enables the ADC, selects a channel, starts conversion, polls conversion completion, and returns the ADC register value.

Section: Layered Embedded Architecture > Motor Layer

dcm.c abstracts DC motor state.

DcMotor_Rotate(state, speed) controls two direction pins and delegates speed generation to the PWM module.

The module supports stop, clockwise, and counter-clockwise states.

Section: Layered Embedded Architecture > PWM Layer

pwm.c configures AVR Timer0 for PWM output.

A percentage duty cycle is converted into an OCR0 compare value, and the timer drives the OC0 output pin.

Motor speed is therefore hardware-timer driven rather than produced by software delay loops.','["timer0","layered","embedded","architecture","application","layer","sensor","motor"]','["Layered Embedded Architecture"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-036-s005-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s005","section_path":["Layered Embedded Architecture","Application Layer"],"section_title":"Application Layer","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`MINI_PROJECT_3.c` owns the temperature-to-actuator policy and coordinates the sensor, motor, ADC, and display.","text_sha256":"0983042f1e1efc34d5697c00301c8b3b74e79a2bac82e61c03ae753a33ba414b","unit_id":"s005","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-036-s006-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Layered Embedded Architecture","Sensor Layer"],"section_title":"Sensor Layer","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":47,"source_line_start":47,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The LM35 module supplies temperature to the application instead of exposing arbitrary raw ADC values directly to `main()`.","text_sha256":"cdef3609871b09327e9474938859d695be49fff7b9922873e309507188d0436e","unit_id":"s006","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-036-s007-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Layered Embedded Architecture","ADC Layer"],"section_title":"ADC Layer","source_file":"repositories/repo-036-Fan-Controller/README.md","source_line_end":51,"source_line_start":51,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"`adc.c` configures the AVR ADC.","text_sha256":"206a45cf3176b2a17e7d58c61af8cd4a4b2a37a4449d41e8