INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-037-rd002',37,'Door-Lock-System',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3929,13,299,'Section: What This Repository Contains

Door-Lock-System contains a two-controller embedded access-control design split between MC1 and MC2.

The system integrates keypad input, LCD output, UART communication, external EEPROM, TWI/I²C, DC motor control, PWM, timers, and buzzer behavior.

Provenance is critical: both central application files explicitly state Author: Mohamed Tarek, date 25/4/2014, and identify themselves as challenge code. Repository ownership therefore does not support claiming original authorship of the core system.

Section: Password Creation

MC1 asks for a five-digit password and then requests the same password again.

When the two local entries agree, MC1 transmits the five bytes over UART.

MC2 receives them and writes each byte to external EEPROM.

Credential persistence therefore resides on the control MCU rather than only in volatile UI memory.

Section: Retry and Alarm Behavior

MC1 permits up to three verification attempts.

It displays remaining attempts after failures.

After the third failure it transmits a buzzer command.

MC2 reacts by enabling the buzzer and using timer/callback logic to terminate the alarm behavior.

Section: Door Actuation

A valid open-door path sends an OPEN_DOOR command to MC2.

MC2 installs a timer callback and drives the DC motor through a timed sequence.

The motor initially rotates in one direction, later stops, then rotates in the opposite direction before the timer sequence is deinitialized.

Door behavior is therefore represented as a temporal actuator workflow rather than a static GPIO state.

Section: Password Change

The password-change path first authenticates the current password.

Only after successful verification does MC1 trigger the password-entry workflow again and MC2 update EEPROM-backed credential data.

This reuses the same trust boundary as door opening.

Section: Inter-MCU Protocol

UART carries both commands and password data.

Defined control values include acceptance, open-door command, and buzzer command.

The system is therefore a small embedded distributed protocol across two processors.','["uart","buzzer","contains","password","creation","retry","alarm","behavior","door","actuation","change","inter-mcu","protocol"]','["What This Repository Contains","Password Creation","Retry and Alarm Behavior","Door Actuation","Password Change","Inter-MCU Protocol"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-037-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Contains"],"section_title":"What This Repository Contains","source_file":"repositories/repo-037-Door-Lock-System/README.md","source_line_end":15,"source_line_start":15,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Door-Lock-System` contains a two-controller embedded access-control design split between `MC1` and `MC2`.","text_sha256":"c92815968a3a9352d573a80945312b5172d18258e7921ff47f48bae35dd81bae","unit_id":"s002","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-037-s002-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":4,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Contains"],"section_title":"What This Repository Contains","source_file":"repositories/repo-037-Door-Lock-System/README.md","source_line_end":17,"source_line_start":17,"specificity_score":0.72,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The system integrates keypad input, LCD output, UART communication, external EEPROM, TWI/I²C, DC motor control, PWM, timers, and buzzer behavior.","text_sha256":"2ca71ead23d9dd302bc9818aa0620d2c842e282e52dd5d8ddf1a7648af1f49f7","unit_id":"s002","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-037-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Contains"],"section_title":"What This Repository Contains","source_file":"repositories/repo-037-Door-Lock-System/README.md","source_line_end":19,"source_line_start":19,"speci