INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-039-rd002',39,'Linux',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.437,33,262,'Section: What This Repository Is

Linux is a compact personal operational reference.

It records commands used around a Linux robotics/development environment rather than implementing a standalone application.

The material covers package installation, shell startup configuration, sudo/ownership operations, Git and GitHub CLI, PDF viewing, and RViz graphics troubleshooting.

Section: Development Environment Bootstrap

ImportantLibraries.bashrc records installation commands for:

Git,

g++,

CMake,

PCL development headers,

Eigen3 development headers.

These dependencies align directly with the contemporaneous C++, point-cloud, Kalman-filter, and robotics repositories.

Section: Shell Configuration

The SUDO notes include:

inspecting ~/.bashrc,

editing ~/.bashrc,

sourcing ~/.bashrc.

This preserves the practical cycle of changing shell initialization and reloading the environment.

Section: GitHub CLI

The same notes record installing gh, authenticating with gh auth login, and cloning through gh repo clone.

This is direct evidence of GitHub CLI use in the Linux workflow.

Section: Filesystem Permissions

A concrete command recursively changes ownership of:

/home/kiro/Robotics/src/

That ties the repository directly to a robotics workspace and documents resolution of a Linux ownership/permission problem.

Section: Git Workflow Notes

git.md records a basic change lifecycle:

git add,

git commit,

git push.

It also records a force-push command.

The repository therefore served as a working source-control cheat sheet.

Section: Graphics and Robotics Troubleshooting

media.md records PDF opening through evince, setting LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1, and starting rviz2.

The environment variable forces software rendering, which is a concrete workaround for graphics/runtime problems when launching RViz.

Section: Technical Context

The repository connects Linux package management with C++ compilation, CMake, Eigen, PCL, ROS/RViz, Git, and GitHub CLI.

It is best interpreted as operational knowledge accumulated while setting up robotics development.','["linux","bashrc","sudo","cmake","eigen","rviz","development","environment","bootstrap","shell","configuration","github","filesystem","permissions","workflow","notes","graphics","robotics","troubleshooting","technical","context"]','["What This Repository Is","Development Environment Bootstrap","Shell Configuration","GitHub CLI","Filesystem Permissions","Git Workflow Notes","Graphics and Robotics Troubleshooting","Technical Context"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-039-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-039-Linux/README.md","source_line_end":14,"source_line_start":14,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Linux` is a compact personal operational reference.","text_sha256":"a93d3813552f7d93aa9217fadefe99206aa33bb54ce49fded260b8dacddeb673","unit_id":"s002","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-039-s002-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-039-Linux/README.md","source_line_end":16,"source_line_start":16,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It records commands used around a Linux robotics/development environment rather than implementing a standalone application.","text_sha256":"13775fea58003c5759036e7d5bcf995adf8f4b261ac0965fdec920c19c8128dd","unit_id":"s002","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-039-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-039-Linux/README.md","sourc