INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-041-rd002',41,'Turtle-Hunter',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4471,28,249,'Section: What This Project Is

Turtle-Hunter is a small ROS 2 navigation exercise built around the standard turtlesim environment.

a turtle-control service that drives the primary turtle toward a requested target coordinate,
a random turtle spawner that periodically asks the turtlesim spawn service to create new turtles.

The repository README describes a broader two-stage idea in which generated turtle targets can be queued and passed to the navigator one by one.

The queue/removal orchestration described in the README is not visibly implemented in the two inspected Python files, so it is recorded as described intent rather than as completed behavior.

Section: Source Layout

The repository contains:

README.md,

turtlefinder.py,

turtlespawn.py.

This is a deliberately small repository with essentially no generated workspace noise.

Section: Turtle Navigation Service

turtlefinder.py defines TurtleControlService, a class derived from rclpy.node.Node.

Its constructor creates three ROS interfaces:

a service named control_turtle,

a publisher to /turtle1/cmd_vel,

a subscriber to /turtle1/pose.

This gives the node both observation and actuation channels.

Section: Pose Feedback

The node subscribes to turtlesim.msg.Pose.

Its pose callback stores the most recently received pose in self.current_pose.

The control service waits until a pose has been received before attempting navigation.

This provides current:

x position,

y position,

heading angle.

The code therefore uses live middleware state instead of assuming a fixed starting position.

Section: Target Geometry

The service request supplies target x and y coordinates.

The navigator computes:

delta_x,

delta_y,

desired heading with math.atan2(delta_y, delta_x).

This is a concrete geometric transformation from Cartesian target displacement to heading.','["python","rclpy","turtlesim","atan2","source","layout","turtle","navigation","service","pose","feedback","target","geometry"]','["What This Project Is","Source Layout","Turtle Navigation Service","Pose Feedback","Target Geometry"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-041-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":16,"source_line_start":16,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Turtle-Hunter` is a small ROS 2 navigation exercise built around the standard `turtlesim` environment.","text_sha256":"3704c37e201c625a694db9e20647257fc8b2f80c65dedb4db1868b2b52368654","unit_id":"s002","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-041-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":21,"source_line_start":20,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"1. a turtle-control service that drives the primary turtle toward a requested target coordinate,\n2. a random turtle spawner that periodically asks the `turtlesim` spawn service to create new turtles.","text_sha256":"6581814ad64af557182db6bfa71a4f8956a5c1ab6ace76df83e20d9fe0ed563e","unit_id":"s002","word_count":30},{"block_id":"repo-041-s002-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":23,"source_line_start":23,"specificity_score":0.24,