_line_end":71,"source_line_start":71,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The navigator computes:","text_sha256":"24c47af3737d4fe14b0ec1ea93019e551c78dab1cc14e094fbd30650e25bba9f","unit_id":"s006","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-041-s006-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Target Geometry"],"section_title":"Target Geometry","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":73,"source_line_start":73,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- `delta_x`,","text_sha256":"3b576a3152480e8dcce9a7910b8160fc6438928bfa98e889eaff881624bf7f13","unit_id":"s006","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-041-s006-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Target Geometry"],"section_title":"Target Geometry","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":74,"source_line_start":74,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- `delta_y`,","text_sha256":"0539b6ece3cb015417347da41e0bbda673be8543a51b62eb9bde0c6a123f51e2","unit_id":"s006","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-041-s006-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Target Geometry"],"section_title":"Target Geometry","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":75,"source_line_start":75,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- desired heading with `math.atan2(delta_y, delta_x)`.","text_sha256":"afb9b87891997af0efdce0a870e5ead886a98d014d4bfc5e0dfa150fbfbe4024","unit_id":"s006","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-041-s006-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Target Geometry"],"section_title":"Target Geometry","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":77,"source_line_start":77,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is a concrete geometric transformation from Cartesian target displacement to heading.","text_sha256":"1a0808559649b5d1c8cb6cb5895d26fd7e59f8f1f482c9e4b4ef626f8a1c71b6","unit_id":"s006","word_count":12}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","document_text_sha256":"683131ab068d798d0e6e4d2cfb0ac37917c2f436a32c0475ca31dce050def89d","earliest_source_line":16,"embedding_text_sha256":"1d387916ccd9855ace264d3fdfa631920bd8c16be8d99f2ee2cab96ebf852875","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"248a68b931b479654784e2d4ae408e6a71468a16126aa357829eb7f9359487a5","repository_source_line_end":314,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-041-rd003',41,'Turtle-Hunter',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3733,16,264,'Section: Target Geometry

The code then compares desired heading with the current turtle heading to choose clockwise or counter-clockwise angular motion.

Section: Angular Motion

A geometry_msgs.msg.Twist message is used for motion commands.

During orientation:

linear velocity is set to zero,
angular velocity is set to +2.0, -2.0, or 0.0.

The command is published to /turtle1/cmd_vel.

The code estimates rotation duration using the absolute heading difference divided by angular speed.

This is open-loop timed rotation rather than continuous closed-loop heading correction.

Section: Linear Motion

After rotation, the node computes Euclidean target distance:

sqrt((target_x-current_x)^2 + (target_y-current_y)^2).

It then commands a linear speed of 4.0.

The code repeatedly republishes the motion command for an estimated duration of distance / 4.0.

Finally it publishes a zero-velocity command to stop.

This is open-loop distance traversal driven by current-pose initialization and speed/time estimation.

Section: Service Interface Reuse

The navigator uses turtlesim.srv.Spawn as the service type for control_turtle.

The request''s x and y fields are reused as target coordinates.

The response''s name field is repurposed to return a success string.

That is a pragmatic learning-stage reuse of an existing service definition rather than a custom semantic service contract.

Section: Random Turtle Spawner

turtlespawn.py defines TurtleSpawner, another rclpy node.

It creates a client for the standard spawn service.

At startup it waits until the service becomes available.

It then schedules a timer every second.

Each timer callback builds a Spawn.Request.

Section: Randomized Spawn Generation

The spawner randomizes:

x coordinate from 0 to 11,

y coordinate from 0 to 11,

heading from 0 to approximately 2π,

turtle name using a random integer suffix.','["rclpy","turtlesim","target","geometry","angular","motion","linear","service","interface","reuse","random","turtle","spawner","randomized","spawn","generation"]','["Target Geometry","Angular Motion","Linear Motion","Service Interface Reuse","Random Turtle Spawner","Randomized Spawn Generation"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-041-s006-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Target Geometry"],"section_title":"Target Geometry","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":79,"source_line_start":79,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The code then compares desired heading with the current turtle heading to choose clockwise or counter-clockwise angular motion.","text_sha256":"9fcca1392ebd8f20017ad329f1093e364c52ac0db0f318f92a8d278bceb1d03c","unit_id":"s006","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-041-s007-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Angular Motion"],"section_title":"Angular Motion","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":83,"source_line_start":83,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"A `geometry_msgs.msg.Twist` message is used for motion commands.","text_sha256":"136e07e0025170e0b47a995d2352c540264551d69be68b43fdaab8ed4b0b95de","unit_id":"s007","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-041-s007-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Angular Motion"],"section_title":"Angular Motion","source_file":"repositories/repo-041-Turtle-Hunter/README.md","source_line_end":85,"source_line_start":85,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"During orientation:","text_sha256":"b32976302812f3eee24c48185042f51cf16000c70ee3db89347ea29f3cd2cf04","unit_id":"s007