INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-042-rd002',42,'RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4567,41,214,'Section: What This Project Is

RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF is a robotics-modeling repository focused on describing a robot structurally and making that description usable in ROS 2 visualization and Gazebo simulation.

small standalone URDF experiments,

command/reference notes for ROS 2, URDF, and Gazebo,

a ROS 2 workspace containing the sedrawybot_description package.

The repository also checks in generated build artifacts, which provide direct evidence that the ROS package was passed through the CMake/colcon build path.

Section: Repository Structure

At the root, the repository is organized into:

Command Cheat Sheet/,

basics/,

gazebo/.

The basics directory contains focused URDF models such as:

jointing.urdf,

nonfixedjoints.urdf,

simpleboxwithwheel.urdf.

The gazebo directory contains a ROS 2 workspace and repository documentation.

Section: Robot Description Package

Inside the workspace, the source package is:

gazebo/ros2_rviz_ws/src/sedrawybot_description.

Its visible source structure contains:

CMakeLists.txt,

package.xml,

config/,

launch/,

urdf/.

This is a conventional ROS 2 robot-description package organization.

Section: Xacro-Based Robot Model

The main model is:

urdf/sedrawybot.urdf.xacro.

It defines a robot named sedrawy.

The model uses Xacro features rather than duplicating every physical element by hand.

It imports a common Xacro file and defines reusable properties and macros.

Section: Xacro Properties and Macros

The model defines a body-length property.

It also defines a reusable wheel_link macro.

That macro creates wheel links with:

cylindrical visual geometry,

material assignment,

inertial properties,

collision geometry.','["ros2","robotics","urdf","xacro","rviz","gazebo","robot-description","cmake","simulation","structure","robot","description","package","xacro-based","model","properties","macros"]','["What This Project Is","Repository Structure","Robot Description Package","Xacro-Based Robot Model","Xacro Properties and Macros"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-042-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":16,"source_line_start":16,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF` is a robotics-modeling repository focused on describing a robot structurally and making that description usable in ROS 2 visualization and Gazebo simulation.","text_sha256":"cf72462552713637f3a0caf8e5652a772998ce0a32d5827e7e8d45743fc7a51c","unit_id":"s002","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-042-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":20,"source_line_start":20,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- small standalone URDF experiments,","text_sha256":"cbe617d77eb5fd74f430393fe000dc0a1d5907a20d1ac9627af4d84b7ed50fb8","unit_id":"s002","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-042-s002-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":21,"source_line_start":21,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- command/reference notes for 