robot link composition,

fixed and continuous joints,

collision geometry,

inertial modeling,

ROS 2 package structure,

CMake-based package configuration,

launch-file integration,

Gazebo plugin integration,

differential-drive configuration,

odometry topic configuration,

build-tool execution.

Section: Engineering Discipline

The source package separates:

model definition,

configuration,

launch behavior,

package metadata.

Xacro macros reduce duplication.

Physics properties are explicitly represented.

The repository preserves incremental learning artifacts instead of only the final robot model.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Robot Modeling

URDF

Xacro

robot links

joint definitions

collision geometry

inertial properties

reusable model macros

Section: Skills Demonstrated > ROS 2 Packaging

CMake

package.xml

launch assets

description package layout

build workspace structure

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Simulation

Gazebo

differential-drive plugin

odometry configuration

wheel geometry

physics-facing robot parameters

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Visualization

RViz-oriented description workflow
robot state/model inspection

Section: Capability Developed

The repository develops the ability to convert a conceptual mobile robot into a ROS-compatible model with:

That is a meaningful systems-integration skill because correctness spans XML structure, physics semantics, ROS packaging, and simulator expectations.

Section: Portfolio Evolution

This follows Turtle-Hunter.

The earlier repository controlled an already-provided simulated turtle.','["urdf","xacro","rviz","gazebo","differential-drive","odometry","cmake","simulation","engineering","work","evidenced","discipline","skills","demonstrated","robot","modeling","packaging","visualization","capability","developed","portfolio","evolution"]','["Engineering Work Evidenced","Engineering Discipline","Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-042-s019-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Engineering Work Evidenced"],"section_title":"Engineering Work Evidenced","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":258,"source_line_start":258,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- robot link composition,","text_sha256":"67809dfd44dfe9cb8ab317f5db32847566b5accfa9336de5b36e665574cfa4da","unit_id":"s019","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-042-s019-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Engineering Work Evidenced"],"section_title":"Engineering Work Evidenced","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":259,"source_line_start":259,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- fixed and continuous joints,","text_sha256":"a0d84da7a1ca46f4aded6b699bec612c2d85422fa03d357ecb5167ecb3a98fbe","unit_id":"s019","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-042-s019-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Engineering Work Evidenced"],"section_title":"Engineering Work Evidenced","source_file":"repositories/repo-042-RVIZ-GAZEBO-URDF/README.md","source_line_end":260,"source_line_start":260,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- collision geometry,","text_sha256":"c0af316a71c0a5f7516332