Section: Capability Developed

This repository develops framework-level deep-learning fluency.

expressing architectures with Keras,

Section: Portfolio Evolution

Tensor-Flow-Basics appears directly after StudyTree.

The roadmap artifact listed AI/Machine Learning as one of the current learning branches.

This repository immediately expands that branch with practical TensorFlow work.

That provides unusually clear chronology between a learning plan and an implementation repository.

Section: Historical Significance

Within the processed corpus, this is the earliest observed repository centered specifically on TensorFlow/Keras.

Section: Overall Narrative

Tensor-Flow-Basics records the transition from general machine-learning study into hands-on deep-learning framework usage.

The repository''s strongest evidence is the sequence of actual notebooks: dense classifiers, CNN recognition, image classification, training, and validation.

It should be read as concentrated deep-learning practice—not as a production ML system and not as proof that all instructional notebook scaffolding originated in the repository.

