INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-048-rd004',48,'RNN-and-Sequence-Models--Training',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.351,7,262,'Section: Character Vocabulary

sequential targets,

recurrent hidden-state reuse,

probabilistic next-character prediction.

Section: Gradient Clipping

The character-model notebook contains a graded clip function.

Gradient clipping is used to constrain gradient magnitude during recurrent training.

This addresses exploding-gradient behavior directly.

The presence of dedicated generated test cases for clip provides explicit validation scaffolding.

Section: Sampling

The character language-model exercise also includes a sampling stage.

The model repeatedly predicts a probability distribution over the next character and selects from that distribution to construct generated text.

This introduces autoregressive generation rather than classification only.

Section: Character-Model Optimization Loop

The exercise connects:

forward propagation,

sequence loss,

backward propagation,

gradient clipping,

parameter updates.

This makes it a full small recurrent training loop rather than just a forward-pass demonstration.

Section: Cosine Similarity

Cosine similarity compares vector direction independent of raw magnitude.

Within this repository it is used as a primitive for semantic comparison between embeddings.

This expands the portfolio from manually created feature vectors into pretrained semantic representation use.

Section: Word Analogies

The analogy exercise applies vector arithmetic and similarity search to relationships of the form:

a : b :: c : ?

That develops intuition for geometric structure in embedding spaces.

Section: Emojify

Emojifi/Emojifi.ipynb contains sentence classification work using word vectors.

A visible sentence_to_avg function converts words in a sentence into an averaged embedding representation.

That representation is then usable for downstream classification.

The notebook includes unit-test-style checks for the sentence averaging operation.

Section: Representation Aggregation

The sentence-average approach demonstrates a simple but important NLP architecture:

raw sentence
→ tokens
→ word vectors
→ aggregate representation
→ classifier.','["hidden-state","character","vocabulary","gradient","clipping","sampling","character-model","optimization","loop","cosine","similarity","word","analogies","emojify","representation","aggregation"]','["Character Vocabulary","Gradient Clipping","Sampling","Character-Model Optimization Loop","Cosine Similarity","Word Analogies","Emojify","Representation Aggregation"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-048-s009-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Character Vocabulary"],"section_title":"Character Vocabulary","source_file":"repositories/repo-048-RNN-and-Sequence-Models--Training/README.md","source_line_end":152,"source_line_start":152,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- sequential targets,","text_sha256":"a305cbea51a3ecb8bd47a936d25d0f472190523fa222a0e370f5eb149a24955b","unit_id":"s009","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-048-s009-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Character Vocabulary"],"section_title":"Character Vocabulary","source_file":"repositories/repo-048-RNN-and-Sequence-Models--Training/README.md","source_line_end":153,"source_line_start":153,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- recurrent hidden-state reuse,","text_sha256":"c55a789320920a14c16731c95a80a5fa0a24de0c98a22e276cf32218d7381a64","unit_id":"s009","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-048-s009-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Character Vocabulary"],"section_title":"Character Vocabulary","source_file":"repositories/repo-048-RNN-and-Sequence-Models--Training/README.md","source_line_end":154,"source_line_start":154,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- probabilistic next-character prediction.","text_sha256":"17ee2c5f34c769f2303597f9fcd06bd0adcf628e26c11f5d64ccbfc85