INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-050-rd003',50,'SQL-Problems',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','mixed','repository_limitation',0.3584,14,251,'Section: Friend Requests: Most Friends

The solution:

groups accepted relationships by accepter_id,

groups them again by requester_id,

normalizes both roles to a shared id,

combines them with UNION ALL,

aggregates the combined counts,

selects the maximum.

Section: Symmetric Relationship Normalization

This is a useful relational-design insight.

A friendship count cannot be computed correctly by considering only one endpoint column.

The solution first converts both endpoint roles into one logical participant dimension.

That demonstrates reasoning about schema semantics, not just SQL syntax.

Section: Customers Who Never Order

The repository contains a dedicated problem for finding customers without orders.

That problem class exercises missing-relationship logic.

Depending on the checked-in query, this family is typically solved through:

anti-join,

NOT IN,

NOT EXISTS,

or null filtering after outer join.

The repository therefore records practice with negative relational conditions.

Section: Managers With Direct Reports

The managers-with-at-least-5-direct-reports problem exercises employee-to-manager self-relationships.

This requires grouping or joining a table against its own managerial references.

It adds hierarchical relational reasoning to the corpus.

Section: Employee Bonus

The employee-bonus problem requires joining employee records with optional bonus records and filtering based on nullable/threshold conditions.

This reinforces outer-join/null semantics.

Section: Customer Referee

The customer-referee problem exercises SQL three-valued logic around nullable foreign-key-like values.

This is useful evidence of practical null-handling awareness.

Section: Largest Number of Orders

The repository contains an aggregation problem for identifying the customer with the largest order count.

That class combines:

COUNT,

grouping,

ordering or maximum selection.

Section: Big Countries

The big-countries problem is a simpler predicate/filter exercise.','["null-handling","friend","requests","most","friends","symmetric","relationship","normalization","customers","never","order","managers","reports","employee","bonus","customer","referee","largest","number","orders","countries"]','["Friend Requests: Most Friends","Symmetric Relationship Normalization","Customers Who Never Order","Managers With Direct Reports","Employee Bonus","Customer Referee","Largest Number of Orders","Big Countries"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-050-s007-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Friend Requests: Most Friends"],"section_title":"Friend Requests: Most Friends","source_file":"repositories/repo-050-SQL-Problems/README.md","source_line_end":81,"source_line_start":81,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The solution:","text_sha256":"cc5d92808bc620bcc326a4c810b5b1a1a5d97c556e1cb4692adf402158b9d4c6","unit_id":"s007","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-050-s007-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Friend Requests: Most Friends"],"section_title":"Friend Requests: Most Friends","source_file":"repositories/repo-050-SQL-Problems/README.md","source_line_end":83,"source_line_start":83,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- groups accepted relationships by `accepter_id`,","text_sha256":"329855012087140ca18ea89eb7546fc5a80a35926f4a325af2a3398ce82dfb78","unit_id":"s007","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-050-s007-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Friend Requests: Most Friends"],"section_title":"Friend Requests: Most Friends","source_file":"repositories/repo-050-SQL-Problems/README.md","source_line_end":84,"source_line_start":84,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"tex