INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-061-rd003',61,'Postgress-for-Data-Engineering',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3895,26,259,'Section: Environment Setup > Python Version Compatibility

The README records a Python compatibility problem encountered during setup.

The documented response includes adding the Deadsnakes PPA and refreshing package metadata:

This is evidence of Linux package/environment troubleshooting around the database toolchain.

Section: Shell Configuration

The repository documents editing:

~/.bashrc for Bash;
~/.zshrc for Zsh.

It then adds a shell alias:

alias pgadmin4=''/usr/pgadmin4/bin/pgadmin4''

This shows persistent shell-environment configuration rather than one-off command execution.

Section: pgAdmin Server Configuration

The README walks through registering a local PostgreSQL server in pgAdmin with:

localhost / 127.0.0.1;

default port 5432;

postgres user credentials.

Section: CSV Import Troubleshooting

The README records a CSV import failure caused by an unexpected extra row/formatting issue.

Instead of abandoning the load, the workflow switches to explicit SQL.

Section: COPY-Based Import

fix.sql contains:

This demonstrates PostgreSQL''s server-side bulk-import syntax with:

explicit target columns;

filesystem input;

delimiter declaration;

CSV header handling.

Section: Engineering Practices > Environment Troubleshooting

The repository captures dependency/runtime compatibility work around Python and pgAdmin.

Section: Engineering Practices > Persistent Developer Environment

Shell aliases are stored in shell startup configuration.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > PostgreSQL

local server configuration;

default port/user concepts;

database creation;

password management;

COPY bulk import;

CSV handling.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Linux

APT/PPA package management;

shell startup files;

aliases;

sudo-based PostgreSQL administration.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Data Engineering

relational data ingestion;

CSV-to-table loading;

operational troubleshooting.

Section: Capability Developed

