INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-063-rd006',63,'phpmyadmin',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3446,28,197,'Section: Transactional System Shape

This is much more significant than the repository title alone suggests.

Section: Technical Stack > SQL Features

DDL;

CREATE TABLE;

INSERT;

UPDATE;

primary keys;

CHECK;

stored procedures;

transactions;

exception handlers;

rollback;

commit;

RESIGNAL.

Section: Technical Stack > Environment

Linux;

APT;

dpkg;

Apache/phpMyAdmin setup.

Section: Engineering Discipline > Integrity Constraints

Invalid financial state is constrained at the schema level:

CHECK(Balance>=0)

rather than relying only on application convention.

Section: Engineering Discipline > Atomicity

Related financial and inventory changes are grouped into one transaction.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > MySQL

schema creation;

constrained columns;

data insertion;

table updates;

stored procedures.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Transaction Management

START TRANSACTION;

COMMIT;

ROLLBACK;

exception-triggered recovery.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Data Integrity

primary keys;

NOT NULL;

CHECK;

non-negative financial balance.

Section: Capability Developed

The key lesson is not merely how to issue SQL updates.

It is how to coordinate dependent updates so a partially completed business transaction does not corrupt state.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

SQL query practice;

phpmyadmin adds a stronger transaction/recovery dimension.

a SQL stored procedure;

SQL exception handling;

rollback-on-failure.

Section: Historical Significance

