INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-068-rd003',68,'GCP',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','repository_specific',0.3913,29,254,'Section: Original Problem

The user was working in Google Cloud Shell inside a directory named after a storage bucket.

The shell showed:

dags

but:

cd dags

failed with:

-bash: cd: dags: Not a directory

This is the key technical clue.

Section: Filesystem vs Object Storage

The troubleshooting distinguishes two different abstractions:

Section: Filesystem vs Object Storage > Local POSIX Filesystem

Normal commands such as:

cd
ls

operate on local filesystem objects.

Section: Failed Copy Attempt

The recorded command was:

The destination is written like a local path rather than an explicit Cloud Storage URI.

Section: Alternative Storage Command

The troubleshooting proposes:

The important difference is the destination:

gs://...

That makes the target unambiguously a Cloud Storage bucket/object prefix.

Section: Storage Inspection

The notes also discuss using:

gsutil ls gs://<bucket>/

and:

gsutil ls gs://<bucket>/dags/

to inspect Cloud Storage directly.

Section: Technical Stack > CLI

gcloud storage

gsutil

Bash shell

Section: Engineering Discipline > Read the Error Literally

The key diagnostic message is:

Not a directory

rather than simply assuming an authorization failure.

Section: Engineering Discipline > Distinguish Abstractions

The repository captures an important cloud-operations principle:

a cloud object-storage namespace is not the same thing as a local filesystem hierarchy.

Section: Engineering Discipline > Separate Hypothesis From Root Cause

IAM is considered, but the evidence does not justify declaring it the confirmed cause.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > GCP CLI

gcloud storage cp;

gsutil ls;

gsutil cp.

Section: Capability Developed

The key lesson is that cloud resources often expose abstractions that resemble local resources without behaving identically.','["gsutil","bash","object-storage","bucket","original","problem","filesystem","object","storage","local","posix","failed","copy","attempt","alternative","command","inspection","technical","stack","engineering","discipline","read","error","literally"]','["Original Problem","Filesystem vs Object Storage","Failed Copy Attempt","Alternative Storage Command","Storage Inspection","Technical Stack","Engineering Discipline","Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-068-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["Original Problem"],"section_title":"Original Problem","source_file":"repositories/repo-068-GCP/README.md","source_line_end":35,"source_line_start":35,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The user was working in Google Cloud Shell inside a directory named after a storage bucket.","text_sha256":"d7fa0350b6fa68d78d3745dbc0d4d9f81120ff0f24def11d01225bb03295e443","unit_id":"s003","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-068-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["Original Problem"],"section_title":"Original Problem","source_file":"repositories/repo-068-GCP/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The shell showed:","text_sha256":"ea7aca0a2c03fa57cfe51fbb706cda6e010927f9b546cc6d64f477f248f38783","unit_id":"s003","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-068-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["Original Problem"],"section_title":"Original Problem","source_file":"repositories/repo-068-GCP/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":39,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_re