INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-068-rd004',68,'GCP',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','deployment_operations','positive','repository_specific',0.3794,27,203,'Section: Filesystem vs Object Storage > Google Cloud Storage

Cloud Storage uses buckets and objects referenced with URIs such as:

gs://bucket-name/object-prefix/

A storage "folder" is commonly represented by object-name prefixes rather than a true POSIX directory.

That explains why seeing dags in one context does not automatically mean it is a local directory that cd can enter.

Section: Cloud Composer Context

The README says the issue occurred during a lab called:

An Introduction to Cloud Composer

This establishes Cloud Composer as learning context.

The repository does not contain:

a Composer environment definition;

an Airflow DAG;

Terraform;

deployment configuration.

Cloud Composer therefore remains a context tag rather than an implemented system capability.

Section: Technical Stack > Google Cloud

Google Cloud Platform

