INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-069-rd005',69,'Portfolio-V2',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','deployment_operations','positive','repository_specific',0.3808,6,150,'Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline

The browser preprocessing code demonstrates the model-input preparation needed to bridge arbitrary user images and an MNIST-style model.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Grayscale Tensor Creation

Image pixels are converted with:

tf.browser.fromPixels(image, 1)

The single channel matches a grayscale digit-model workflow.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Resize

Input is resized to 28×28 when required through TensorFlow.js image operations.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Numeric Normalization

Pixel values are converted to floating point and scaled by 255.0.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Background Inversion

The mean pixel value is examined.

For predominantly light backgrounds, the image is inverted so digit/background polarity better matches the model representation.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Contrast Normalization

The tensor is shifted by its minimum and divided by its range, producing a normalized intensity span.

Section: Image Preprocessing Pipeline > Batch Dimension

The processed tensor is expanded into a batch before prediction.','["javascript","image","preprocessing","pipeline","grayscale","tensor","creation","resize","numeric","normalization","background","inversion","contrast","batch","dimension"]','["Image Preprocessing Pipeline"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-069-s013-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Image Preprocessing Pipeline"],"section_title":"Image Preprocessing Pipeline","source_file":"repositories/repo-069-Portfolio-V2/README.md","source_line_end":156,"source_line_start":156,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The browser preprocessing code demonstrates the model-input preparation needed to bridge arbitrary user images and an MNIST-style model.","text_sha256":"af66fd945cfde1e700d70a9b3c8fd38eadb55eee91f1d27083bf6becf9079cd1","unit_id":"s013","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-069-s014-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Image Preprocessing Pipeline","Grayscale Tensor Creation"],"section_title":"Grayscale Tensor Creation","source_file":"repositories/repo-069-Portfolio-V2/README.md","source_line_end":160,"source_line_start":160,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Image pixels are converted with:","text_sha256":"b9e335d59a1a129fd901a2b69a3093753af0747d380f8b05a77d92b12508156d","unit_id":"s014","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-069-s014-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Image Preprocessing Pipeline","Grayscale Tensor Creation"],"section_title":"Grayscale Tensor Creation","source_file":"repositories/repo-069-Portfolio-V2/README.md","source_line_end":164,"source_line_start":162,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":96,"text":"```javascript\ntf.browser.fromPixels(image, 1)\n```","text_sha25