INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-074-rd004',74,'Habit-Tracker',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3483,7,227,'Section: Long-Press Interaction > Trigger Threshold

After 500 milliseconds, the custom context menu is shown.

Section: Long-Press Interaction > Cancellation

The timer is cleared on:

touchend;
touchmove.

This prevents a movement gesture from unintentionally triggering the menu.

Section: Custom Context Menu

The context menu offers:

Edit;
Delete.

Its position is calculated relative to the selected activity.

This is a nontrivial mobile interaction pattern implemented directly with DOM events and geometry.

Section: Edit Workflow

Selecting Edit:

stores the current item as editingActivity;

extracts its name and type;

fills the modal fields;

changes the modal title;

opens the modal.

Confirming the modal updates the existing card rather than creating a new one.

Section: Delete Workflow

Selecting Delete removes the active list item from the DOM.

The context menu is then dismissed.

Section: Overlay and Modal State

The modal and overlay are toggled together through CSS classes.

Closing the modal resets:

input text;

activity type;

selected emoji;

editing state;

modal title.

This keeps add and edit workflows inside one reusable component.

Section: Touch Behavior Control

The page deliberately suppresses browser defaults on activity items.

It uses:

touch-action: none;

preventDefault;

non-passive touch listeners.

That gives the application control over long-press behavior.

Section: Engineering Practices > Reusable Add/Edit Workflow

One modal supports both creation and editing.

Section: Engineering Practices > Explicit Interaction State

JavaScript tracks:

selected emoji;

