INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-076-rd006',76,'LeetCodeJava',NULL,NULL,'direct_evidence','implementation_skills','positive','implemented_or_concrete',0.4219,5,106,'Section: Representative Implementation — Stone Game III

The latest Java solution is a compact dynamic-programming implementation.

The key state is:

Instead of tracking both players'' absolute scores, the solution tracks score difference.

For each index:

consider taking one, two, or three stones,

accumulate the score taken immediately,

subtract the opponent''s optimal future advantage,

retain the maximum resulting advantage.

The transition is conceptually:

The table is filled backward because dp[i] depends on later suffix states.

The result is classified from dp[0]:

positive → Alice,

negative → Bob,

zero → Tie.

