INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-078-rd003',78,'Reinforcement-Learning',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.371,10,191,'Section: What the Project Is

The repository begins with a hand-built Pygame basketball simulation.

It then repeatedly augments that environment with tabular Q-learning.

The learning task is to select a projectile arc that can cause the ball to enter the basket.

Across the variants, the state representation and learning strategy become progressively richer.

The project therefore combines:

game-loop programming,

projectile physics,

reward-driven control,

discrete state construction,

epsilon-greedy exploration,

Q-value updates,

experience replay in the final version.

It is not a neural-network reinforcement-learning project.

No DQN is implemented.

The learning mechanism remains tabular Q-learning.

Section: Experimental Progression

The repository structure itself communicates the experiment:

Each later file carries forward the game while modifying the agent.

That gives unusually clear evidence of iterative model design.

Section: Baseline Environment — basicgame.py

The baseline file implements a Pygame application called BasketBallfellow.

It creates:

a player,

a basketball,

a basket,

a scoreboard,

a court,

celebration effects.

The player can:

move horizontally,

jump,

shoot.

The projectile arc is adjustable.

The ball follows simple discrete-time projectile motion with:

horizontal velocity,

vertical velocity,

gravity.

The game detects whether the ball enters the basket-rim region.

It also handles missed/out-of-bounds shots.','["reinforcement-learning","q-learning","epsilon-greedy","pygame","experimental","progression","baseline","environment","basicgame.py"]','["What the Project Is","Experimental Progression","Baseline Environment — `basicgame.py`"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-078-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-078-Reinforcement-Learning/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository begins with a hand-built Pygame basketball simulation.","text_sha256":"1f51b71ce9d8db20cdb073506a1887f1c73bf67661af78a702c436d11c24e611","unit_id":"s003","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-078-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-078-Reinforcement-Learning/README.md","source_line_end":39,"source_line_start":39,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It then repeatedly augments that environment with tabular Q-learning.","text_sha256":"6717ab426deb647bea3444a04fe3ee940316b2da1bc4b3d39a09bfc9a4089bad","unit_id":"s003","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-078-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-078-Reinforcement-Learning/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":41,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The learning task is to select a projectile arc that can cause the ball to enter the basket.","text_sha256":"df025be91d24316fd3b22bf0ad8e7bc16c79471f08ed8832aefeea2c85150197","u