INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-079-rd003',79,'SDR',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3532,5,230,'Section: What the Project Is

This repository develops tooling around a wireless networking experiment in which application-level UDP traffic is generated and received over real network interfaces.

The checked-in Python tools:

send broadcast UDP traffic,

receive traffic across one or more threads,

measure bytes/packets,

estimate throughput,

expose network configuration,

collect burst statistics,

present results through a desktop GUI.

The repository also preserves hardware/environment notes and experiment logs.

The root README later evolves into a conference-paper revision checklist.

That shows the code and experiments were being organized toward research communication rather than only as a utility.

Section: Repository Shape

The current tree includes a structure broadly like:

Several intermediate READMEs are empty placeholders.

The active evidence lives in source and experiment files.

Section: UDP Sender

The multithreaded experiment includes a Python UDP sender.

It:

opens a datagram socket,

enables socket broadcast,

increases the socket send buffer,

sends fixed-size payloads to a subnet broadcast address,

runs for a fixed duration,

throttles each iteration with a small send delay,

catches socket send failures,

computes total MiB and approximate Mbps.

This is direct real-network traffic generation.

It is separate from the earlier ns-3 simulation repository.

Section: Send-Rate Control

The sender includes an explicit sub-millisecond delay between sends.

The code comment explains this as protection against buffer overflow.

On send failure, it also pauses briefly before retrying.

This demonstrates awareness of practical sender-side resource constraints.','["python","shape","sender","send-rate","control"]','["What the Project Is","Repository Shape","UDP Sender","Send-Rate Control"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-079-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-079-SDR/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":41,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This repository develops tooling around a wireless networking experiment in which application-level UDP traffic is generated and received over real network interfaces.","text_sha256":"ba0a048be43b51c34fff3833a10a006d648707fce95dd956479135a12d2b7917","unit_id":"s003","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-079-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-079-SDR/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The checked-in Python tools:","text_sha256":"1ac14ca5a5510e5786b35ad5eae929d53daea5143f44509970182843003a6883","unit_id":"s003","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-079-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-079-SDR/README.md","source_line_end":45,"source_line_start":45,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- send broadcast UDP traffic,","text_sha256":"a429afbb02d8f7e713d1783ba6314c5ef7441835ead3035614d66f9aeba516c0","unit_id":"s003","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-079-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"inter