INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-081-rd004',81,'Milestone',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','mixed','repository_specific',0.4063,15,246,'Section: Registration Workflow

email format,

minimum password length,

password confirmation match,

birth date in the past,

username uniqueness,

email uniqueness.

This is a meaningful validation flow for a prototype.

Section: Password Handling

The browser uses the Web Crypto API to compute a SHA-256 hash of the password before storing the user record.

Login recomputes the hash and compares it against the stored value.

This demonstrates awareness that plaintext passwords should not be stored directly.

However, a raw unsalted SHA-256 password hash is not equivalent to a dedicated password-hashing scheme such as Argon2/bcrypt/scrypt.

The corpus therefore tags browser-side hashing, not production-grade authentication security.

Section: Authority Model

The code stores an authority value with each user.

The first user receives one authority value and subsequent users another.

After login, the application routes the permitted authority to kilostone.html.

Other authority values receive an ineligible state.

This is a simple prototype authorization mechanism.

It is not a full role/permission system.

The README itself lists multi-user hierarchy and broader authority behavior as future work.

Section: Implemented vs Planned Scope

The README marks deleting milestones as complete.

It leaves several items explicitly unchecked, including:

multiple users and email behavior as a broader product concept,

categories based on logged-user authority,

visual redesign,

a global multi-user hierarchy.

Those unchecked items are not treated as implemented features.

The actual source provides a simpler user/authority mechanism.

Section: Track Model

kilostone.html stores tracks in Firebase.

The application can load track records and render them into the UI.','["html","firebase","sha-256","registration","workflow","password","handling","authority","model","implemented","planned","scope","track"]','["Registration Workflow","Password Handling","Authority Model","Implemented vs Planned Scope","Track Model"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-081-s007-b010","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Registration Workflow"],"section_title":"Registration Workflow","source_file":"repositories/repo-081-Milestone/README.md","source_line_end":110,"source_line_start":110,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- email format,","text_sha256":"84b18ed85bcb0958a184224c8859ab458a8f6a40eb7d7d1efcbf3cbc6673dd65","unit_id":"s007","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-081-s007-b011","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Registration Workflow"],"section_title":"Registration Workflow","source_file":"repositories/repo-081-Milestone/README.md","source_line_end":111,"source_line_start":111,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- minimum password length,","text_sha256":"afea54543dd86fd06a764e847b4e401c313ca687f89e21da78fa75a0a2239e76","unit_id":"s007","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-081-s007-b012","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Registration Workflow"],"section_title":"Registration Workflow","source_file":"repositories/repo-081-Milestone/README.md","source_line_end":112,"source_line_start":112,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- password confirmation match,","text_sha256":"2231a5a42124e3fea0c97c5e6f35a72def7783bb42e68dcf6f851fea450bf403","unit_id":"s007","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-081-s007-b013","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","s