INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-082-rd004',82,'FlashWare',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3499,8,240,'Section: Subnet Host Generation

It then yields candidate IPs across the host range.

This allows the same scanner to adapt to the selected interface''s subnet size.

The design assumes a conventional host range and is most naturally suited to ordinary LAN subnets.

Section: Concurrent Host Scanning

The scanner uses a queue plus a fixed worker pool.

The configured worker count is:

100

Each worker:

receives an IP from the queue,

invokes the platform ping command,

records a responding host,

increments shared progress.

A lock protects shared counters and active-device state.

This is a practical concurrency design for reducing sequential scan latency.

Section: Cross-Platform Ping Handling

The worker distinguishes Windows from other platforms.

It selects different command-line flags for:

packet count,
timeout.

That is evidence of cross-platform intent at the host-discovery layer.

The packaged .exe provides direct Windows distribution evidence.

The README also contains macOS-oriented Miniforge/Tkinter packaging preparation.

Section: Scan Progress

The NetworkScanner accepts a progress callback.

After each processed IP, it reports:

processed count,
total count.

The GUI converts that state into:

a determinate progress bar,

a textual percentage,

a loader animation.

A commit specifically records adding download/transfer progress and GUI improvements.

That is product-level feedback rather than background-only scanning.

Section: File-Transfer Server

FileTransferServer starts a notification listener in a daemon thread.

It listens on a dedicated TCP notification port.

For each incoming connection it launches a request-handler thread.

The request protocol begins with a TRANSFER_REQUEST message containing file metadata.','["tkinter","subnet","host","generation","concurrent","scanning","cross-platform","ping","handling","scan","progress","file-transfer","server"]','["Subnet Host Generation","Concurrent Host Scanning","Cross-Platform Ping Handling","Scan Progress","File-Transfer Server"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-082-s007-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Subnet Host Generation"],"section_title":"Subnet Host Generation","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":100,"source_line_start":100,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It then yields candidate IPs across the host range.","text_sha256":"1019cb46b544e50b2ceb8f20231ad58813ad653ccc2cdf37a5d00edfcedd0868","unit_id":"s007","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-082-s007-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Subnet Host Generation"],"section_title":"Subnet Host Generation","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":102,"source_line_start":102,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This allows the same scanner to adapt to the selected interface''s subnet size.","text_sha256":"8074f19094b38905b82ed15ac49aeacf4421dcf9be95ce2e48cf4a99adee982a","unit_id":"s007","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-082-s007-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Subnet Host Generation"],"section_title":"Subnet Host Generation","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":104,"source_line_start":104,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The design assumes a conventional host range and is most naturally suited to ordinary LAN subnets.","text_sha256":"6820c92e