INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-082-rd005',82,'FlashWare',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3464,3,221,'Section: File-Transfer Server

The receiver can respond:

ACCEPT,
decline behavior.

Accepted requests trigger the data-receive phase.

Section: Two-Port Protocol

The application uses two fixed TCP ports:

one for notification/negotiation,
one for file data.

This separates control-plane-like transfer negotiation from the actual data stream.

Conceptually:

This is a simple custom application protocol.

Section: Incoming Transfer Flow

On an accepted incoming transfer:

the receiver marks a transfer as active,

opens a listening TCP socket for data,

accepts the sender connection,

writes received byte chunks to a file,

updates transfer progress on the GUI thread,

checks received size against expected size,

displays success or incomplete-transfer feedback.

The implementation therefore includes explicit completeness checking based on byte count.

Section: Outgoing Transfer Flow

The sender path:

connects to the target notification port,

sends filename and size metadata,

waits for receiver response,

if accepted, starts transfer UI state,

connects to the data port,

streams the file,

updates progress.

This is a complete request/accept/send workflow.

Section: User-Controlled Acceptance

Incoming files are not written automatically merely because a peer connects.

The server calls back into the GUI to display a transfer prompt.

This is a meaningful product/safety control for a LAN utility.

The user participates in the decision to receive a file.

Section: Drag-and-Drop

The GUI inherits from TkinterDnD.Tk.

It registers a file-drop target and binds a drop event.','["tkinter","drag-and-drop","file-transfer","server","two-port","protocol","incoming","transfer","flow","outgoing","user-controlled","acceptance"]','["File-Transfer Server","Two-Port Protocol","Incoming Transfer Flow","Outgoing Transfer Flow","User-Controlled Acceptance","Drag-and-Drop"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-082-s011-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["File-Transfer Server"],"section_title":"File-Transfer Server","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":171,"source_line_start":171,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The receiver can respond:","text_sha256":"34a5addd7e8eaa426ce3ec0d158bcf3718b1728a1f3cb05feaa9b3d60c9d8bf9","unit_id":"s011","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-082-s011-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["File-Transfer Server"],"section_title":"File-Transfer Server","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":174,"source_line_start":173,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- `ACCEPT`,\n- decline behavior.","text_sha256":"09b8957e61daa7dfc67ccbfbc80d71b1e064bf311060edc38bbc0d5a68bf1550","unit_id":"s011","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-082-s011-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["File-Transfer Server"],"section_title":"File-Transfer Server","source_file":"repositories/repo-082-FlashWare/README.md","source_line_end":176,"source_line_start":176,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Accepted requests trigger the data-receive phase.","text_sha256":"0700c65cb5ae1e5c381afd73869e6e0c4e86952f8848773156551c0a37cce787","unit_id":"s011","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-082-s012-b001","canonical_categories"