INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-083-rd014',83,'LanguageStudy',NULL,NULL,'direct_evidence','identity_access_security','positive','repository_specific',0.4835,6,74,'Section: Security and Data Boundaries

The Firebase web configuration is embedded client-side.

That is normal for many Firebase browser applications and is not equivalent to a server secret by itself.

Actual protection would depend on Firebase security rules.

Those rules are not present in the inspected repository.

Therefore the corpus must not claim authenticated or authorization-protected data.

The application does not show a login flow.

