INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-084-rd003',84,'assignment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3989,18,214,'Section: What the Project Is

This project is a numerical robotics experiment for iterative inverse kinematics of a spatial anthropomorphic manipulator.

The source models a revolute-joint serial robot.

It computes end-effector pose through forward kinematics.

It then iteratively drives the robot toward a desired pose using Jacobian-based update laws.

The implementation compares three main methods:

Jacobian pseudoinverse using SVD;

damped least-squares pseudoinverse;

Jacobian transpose.

It records trajectories and errors for analysis.

It produces multiple comparative plots.

This is not a generic Python assignment.

It is a focused robotics/control/numerical-methods implementation.

Section: Project Scope

The implemented scope is a numerical comparison of Jacobian-based inverse-kinematics techniques on a spatial serial manipulator model.

The repository does not attempt dynamics, torque control, path planning, collision avoidance, hardware control, or a complete robotics application.

Its focus is task-space convergence and algorithm comparison.

Section: Manipulator Model

The source constructs a DHRobot.

The link model uses revolute DH joints.

The comments describe the intended physical interpretation as:

base/shoulder yaw;

shoulder pitch;

elbow pitch;

wrist joint.

The code defines:

link lengths;

base height offset;

DH d;

DH a;

DH alpha.

A target pose is defined numerically.

An initial joint-angle guess is also defined.

Section: Pose Representations

The code provides two pose functions.

Section: Pose Representations > Full Pose

ee_pose_spatial computes:

x;

y;

z;','["python","robotics","dhrobot","inverse-kinematics","jacobian","numerical-methods","scope","manipulator","model","pose","representations","full"]','["What the Project Is","Project Scope","Manipulator Model","Pose Representations"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-084-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This project is a numerical robotics experiment for iterative inverse kinematics of a spatial anthropomorphic manipulator.","text_sha256":"186ce583b8ef074cdbd00d5507410db00eab3524a3a63f6dafb5312498f40798","unit_id":"s003","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-084-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":42,"source_line_start":42,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The source models a revolute-joint serial robot.","text_sha256":"fe597fdf3deaf4579e4856371404ea7f33c30168f1b9a93bd9d79329ca990d36","unit_id":"s003","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-084-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":44,"source_line_start":44,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It computes end-effector pose through forward kinematics.","text_sha256":"f381d5ac4b8e36fc33983f2f17db4457932aa3d4aeb118ae187ca5d008230814","unit_id":"s003","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-084-s003-b004","canonical_categori