INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-084-rd004',84,'assignment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3739,14,200,'Section: Pose Representations > Full Pose

roll;

pitch;

yaw.

It obtains position and rotation from fkine.

Euler angles are extracted from the rotation matrix.

The code explicitly handles a singular branch in the Euler conversion.

Section: Pose Representations > Simplified Pose

ee_pose_simplified returns:

x;

y;

z;

summed joint angle.

This creates a reduced orientation representation for comparative iteration.

The main comparison path uses the simplified target.

Section: Inverse-Kinematics Algorithms > SVD Pseudoinverse

JacobianPseudoinverse_SVD:

computes an SVD;

thresholds singular values;

reciprocates values above the threshold;

reconstructs a pseudoinverse.

This explicitly handles small singular values.

Section: Inverse-Kinematics Algorithms > Damped Least Squares

JacobianPseudoinverse computes a damped inverse based on:

(JᵀJ + λI)^-1 Jᵀ

The damping term is intended to improve numerical stability.

This provides a second treatment of singular or ill-conditioned Jacobian behavior.

Section: Inverse-Kinematics Algorithms > Jacobian Transpose

JacobianTranspose returns a scaled transpose.

An additional adaptive transpose function adjusts its scaling using the current error magnitude.

The three main comparison algorithms stored in the run dictionary are:

SVD pseudoinverse;

damped least squares;

Jacobian transpose.

Section: Iterative Solver

IK_Jacobian_Spatial implements the reusable iterative solve loop.

Its inputs include:

IK algorithm;

manipulator;

target pose;

initial guess;

pose function;

step size;

maximum iterations;

