INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-084-rd009',84,'assignment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3618,7,183,'Section: Major Engineering Work > 5. Instrumentation

It does not only return a final joint configuration.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 6. Comparative Visualization

The project builds several views of the same experiment:

task-space geometry;

component-level error;

component-level pose;

joint trajectories;

aggregate convergence.

This is useful engineering-analysis discipline.

Section: Engineering Discipline

Strong aspects visible in source:

algorithms isolated as functions;

solver parameterization;

consistent result schema;

explicit numerical tolerances;

singular-value thresholding;

damped inverse option;

iteration cap;

trajectory capture;

shared comparison conditions.

Constraints:

one large source file;

no dependency manifest;

no environment lock;

no unit tests;

no CI;

no saved benchmark output in the repository;

no reproducibility document beyond code constants;

joint limits are present only as commented optional logic;

the model description says RRR while the implementation constructs four revolute joints.

That last inconsistency matters.

The source variable is called spatial_rrr, but the DHRobot list contains four RevoluteDH entries.

The corpus should therefore describe the actual implementation as four revolute joints rather than blindly repeating the RRR label.

Section: Skills Demonstrated

Evidence supports:

Python;

NumPy;

numerical linear algebra;

robotics kinematics;

Denavit-Hartenberg modeling;

forward kinematics;','["python","numpy","robotics","denavit-hartenberg","dhrobot","major","engineering","work","instrumentation","comparative","visualization","discipline","skills","demonstrated"]','["Major Engineering Work","Engineering Discipline","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-084-s030-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s030","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","5. Instrumentation"],"section_title":"5. Instrumentation","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":379,"source_line_start":379,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It does not only return a final joint configuration.","text_sha256":"2a72ad00e675cd5699996745ddc32584e62d4a39d381e689f4b57f6a9cc3c923","unit_id":"s030","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-084-s031-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","6. Comparative Visualization"],"section_title":"6. Comparative Visualization","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":383,"source_line_start":383,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The project builds several views of the same experiment:","text_sha256":"2ed3f698ba3869781fa6f35e041b2b6a3b98573fda5927660856345b6771b696","unit_id":"s031","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-084-s031-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","6. Comparative Visualization"],"section_title":"6. Comparative Visualization","source_file":"repositories/repo-084-assignment/README.md","source_line_end":385,"source_line_start":385,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- task-space geometry;","text_sha256":"53a2b4b6ce6c1ac979f2988053dfd56421a805894899852f2aa7d7b3a8f9bbd1","unit_id":"s031","word_count":3