INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-085-rd006',85,'BroadcastInAndroid',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3778,15,215,'Section: Port Validation

status feedback;
a shake animation.

The port control is disabled while actively listening.

Section: UI Engineering

The application is more styled than a bare Android networking proof.

It implements:

status-color transitions;

button-state transitions;

mode-specific color treatment;

scroll-to-latest behavior;

message-entry animation;

shake feedback;

readable monospaced log text.

The unified variant uses GradientDrawable to build button visuals programmatically.

The screen state communicates whether the receiver is:

ready;

listening;

stopped;

failed to bind.

Section: Technical Stack

Kotlin

Android SDK

Android Activity

Kotlin coroutines

Java networking APIs

UDP

DatagramSocket

DatagramPacket

NetworkInterface

Handler / Looper

programmatic Android UI

Section: Android Manifest Concerns

The repository includes manifest files for the variants.

The presence of separate manifests supports standalone Android experiments.

The inspected application behavior requires network access.

The corpus should treat manifest configuration as application integration evidence.

It should not infer Play Store packaging or signed-release distribution.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 1. Native UDP Receiver

The source implements direct socket receiving on Android rather than relying on a web view or external library.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 2. Off-Main-Thread Networking

Blocking receive behavior is moved to an IO coroutine.

This avoids performing network work directly on the UI thread.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 3. Thread-Safe UI Updates

Main-thread UI updates are routed through a Handler.','["kotlin","android","port","validation","engineering","technical","stack","manifest","concerns","major","work","native","receiver","off-main-thread","networking","thread-safe","updates"]','["Port Validation","UI Engineering","Technical Stack","Android Manifest Concerns","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-085-s013-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Port Validation"],"section_title":"Port Validation","source_file":"repositories/repo-085-BroadcastInAndroid/README.md","source_line_end":201,"source_line_start":200,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- status feedback;\n- a shake animation.","text_sha256":"3aa1a243d35e7c611823f5d2e1f0b5c6af1882cf054a75a0efeef0e44d0ee5b1","unit_id":"s013","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-085-s013-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Port Validation"],"section_title":"Port Validation","source_file":"repositories/repo-085-BroadcastInAndroid/README.md","source_line_end":203,"source_line_start":203,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The port control is disabled while actively listening.","text_sha256":"0219654c5b9631f529026df84f5d2d542f15e72c1e84945c8d1a00a759367bd3","unit_id":"s013","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-085-s015-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["UI Engineering"],"section_title":"UI Engineering","source_file":"repositories/repo-085-BroadcastInAndroid/README.md","source_line_end":232,"source_line_start":232,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application is more styled than a bare Android networking proof.","text_sha256":"44a54edfdea41d396358f28e75e6d6701ab0baaa1dc0f1194d8074310e77a2cd","unit_id":"s015","word_count":1