INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-085-rd007',85,'BroadcastInAndroid',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','positive','interpretive',0.3372,3,108,'Section: Throughput Measurement

The larger broadcast-capable variant adds throughput state.

It tracks:

received bytes;

packet count;

burst start time;

pending throughput state.

The UI includes formatted throughput output in Mbps.

The throughput message also exposes:

packet count;

approximate kilobytes;

burst duration.

This turns the app from only a text receiver into a lightweight traffic-observation tool.

The code measures application-observed receive volume.

It should not be treated as a full wireless PHY benchmark.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 6. Throughput Instrumentation

The later version collects burst-level receive metrics.

This connects application-level network traffic with a simple performance observation.

Section: Scale and Complexity

The Broadcast/MainActivity.kt file is substantial.

