INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-088-rd008',88,'Quizedra',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4014,20,239,'Section: Technical Stack

Firebase

Firebase Realtime Database

QRCode.js

Web Audio API

responsive browser UI

realtime event subscription

Section: Major Engineering Work > 2. Frictionless Join Flow

QR onboarding turns a shared screen into a multi-device interaction entry point.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 3. Real-Time Data Propagation

Participant submissions reach the master through Firebase subscriptions.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 5. Duplicate Render Prevention

Message IDs already displayed are tracked.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 6. Participant and Message Metrics

The UI exposes basic session statistics.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 7. Spatial Bubble Layout

The application implements a collision-avoidance heuristic for feedback placement.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 8. Audio Feedback

The app generates a sound in-browser for new messages.

Section: Major Engineering Work > 9. Input Guardrails

Submission fields have explicit validation and visual character feedback.

Section: Engineering Discipline

Positive evidence:

clear separation of master vs participant role;

asynchronous submission handling;

input validation;

realtime subscription;

session-time filtering;

deduplication of rendered IDs;

responsive participant form;

graceful audio fallback;

URL-relative QR construction;

user-visible error states.

Constraints:

Firebase browser configuration embedded in source;

no authentication;

no database security rules in repo;

no explicit session ID;

session defined only by master-open timestamp;

participant identity based only on name;

user-provided strings inserted into innerHTML on the master page;

no sanitization visible before that HTML interpolation;

no moderation workflow;

no rate limiting;

no automated tests.

