INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-091-rd003',91,'RogersExperiment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3685,11,193,'Section: What the Project Is

RogersExperiment is a focused simulation that studies how application throughput changes as a Wi-Fi station moves progressively farther from an access point.

The experiment repeatedly runs a simple AP/STA scenario.

For each run, it changes the station''s distance from the AP.

The station follows waypoint mobility at a configured velocity.

UDP traffic is generated toward the AP.

FlowMonitor statistics are used to derive throughput.

The distance and throughput pair is written to a CSV file.

The result is a small measurement-generation experiment rather than a full network simulator framework.

Section: Project Scope

The implemented scope includes:

ns-3 Wi-Fi node creation;

one AP and one station;

802.11ac/VHT PHY/MAC configuration;

fixed MCS selection;

wide-channel configuration;

waypoint mobility;

increasing separation distance;

UDP OnOff traffic;

IPv4 addressing;

FlowMonitor statistics;

throughput computation;

CSV export.

The repository does not establish cellular simulation, real-world modem interaction, or Rogers infrastructure access.

Section: Technical Stack

C++

ns-3

Wi-Fi module

mobility module

internet stack

applications module

FlowMonitor

IPv4

UDP

CSV output

Section: Wi-Fi Configuration

The source configures an 802.11ac/VHT-oriented Wi-Fi scenario.

A constant-rate Wi-Fi manager is used.

The configured data mode is VhtMcs5.

The control mode is VhtMcs0.','["station","ipv4","scope","technical","stack","wi-fi","configuration"]','["What the Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack","Wi-Fi Configuration"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-091-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":35,"source_line_start":35,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"RogersExperiment is a focused simulation that studies how application throughput changes as a Wi-Fi station moves progressively farther from an access point.","text_sha256":"a10e000ff8b4fcd49626fb51f90b3c0235fcb14a7374aee4e72c77bff39a1582","unit_id":"s003","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-091-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The experiment repeatedly runs a simple AP/STA scenario.","text_sha256":"3ada34a1c9a10d67f0f566fdcc0b5638b7b69c7ec7eea66b6cf8e1b5c8318f77","unit_id":"s003","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-091-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":39,"source_line_start":39,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"For each run, it changes the station''s distance from the AP.","text_sha256":"db5a541365111386859226355c20b9d35de8c0df784485acda78952f9af9fbce","unit_id":"s003","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-091-s003-b004","cano