INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-091-rd005',91,'RogersExperiment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3534,9,261,'Section: Wi-Fi Configuration

The source sets a 160 MHz channel width.

These are deliberate PHY/MAC assumptions in the simulation.

They should not be generalized into claims about all Wi-Fi deployments.

The use of fixed MCS is particularly important when interpreting the distance curve.

The experiment is not evaluating adaptive rate control.

Section: Network Topology

The network consists of two nodes:

one access point;
one station.

The internet stack is installed.

IPv4 addresses are assigned.

The topology is deliberately minimal so that mobility/distance remains the main manipulated condition.

This reduces topology complexity but does not isolate all wireless-channel variables in a real-world sense.

Section: Mobility Model

The station uses WaypointMobilityModel.

The experiment specifies station motion rather than teleporting between arbitrary points inside a single run.

The configured velocity is 1 m/s.

Distance is incremented by 0.01 m between the repeated experiment configurations until the defined upper range.

That gives the simulation a fine-grained distance sweep.

The resulting large number of potential distance points is computationally more demanding than a handful of manually chosen distances.

Section: Traffic Generation

Traffic uses an ns-3 OnOff application.

The transport is UDP.

The offered data rate is configured at 10 Mbps.

The packet size is 1024 bytes.

The application sends traffic toward the access point.

This provides a stable offered-load configuration for comparing runs.

It is not a congestion-heavy multi-flow workload.

Section: FlowMonitor Use

FlowMonitor is installed to retrieve per-flow packet/byte/timing statistics.

The experiment uses received-byte and timing information to derive throughput.

This is application-layer/flow-oriented simulation measurement.

It avoids estimating throughput merely from the configured sender rate.','["station","ipv4","wi-fi","configuration","network","topology","mobility","model","traffic","generation","flowmonitor"]','["Wi-Fi Configuration","Network Topology","Mobility Model","Traffic Generation","FlowMonitor Use"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-091-s007-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Wi-Fi Configuration"],"section_title":"Wi-Fi Configuration","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":121,"source_line_start":121,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The source sets a 160 MHz channel width.","text_sha256":"3f7df3b8e8c10ae1255be422f7ebc389ce7a26e0644a373c96907394cbb31021","unit_id":"s007","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-091-s007-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Wi-Fi Configuration"],"section_title":"Wi-Fi Configuration","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":123,"source_line_start":123,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"These are deliberate PHY/MAC assumptions in the simulation.","text_sha256":"d5205b902f600d000b49d37b54d272a351b77789c3f14a8caba565c9d91b68cb","unit_id":"s007","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-091-s007-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s007","section_path":["Wi-Fi Configuration"],"section_title":"Wi-Fi Configuration","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":125,"source_line_start":125,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"They should not be generalized into claims about all Wi-Fi deployments.","text_sha256":"200315d6c0ba37e2c3129e9c1024400ea140884a24d11bd389735c7974dcf370","unit_id":"s007","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-091-s007