INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-091-rd007',91,'RogersExperiment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','positive','interpretive',0.3498,3,126,'Section: Throughput Calculation

Throughput is converted to Mbps from the flow statistics.

The resulting value is paired with the distance used for that run.

These pairs form the output series.

The experiment is therefore designed around a simple explanatory relationship:

The repository does not add confidence intervals, repeated random seeds, or statistical uncertainty analysis around each distance point.

The output is best understood as a deterministic/configured simulation sweep in the retained snapshot.

Section: Scale / Complexity

The node topology is intentionally small.

The complexity lies in the cross-layer simulation configuration and repeated measurement sweep.

A two-node scenario still requires coordination of:

wireless standard configuration;

rate configuration;

mobility;

addressing;

application traffic;

flow instrumentation;

experiment iteration;

result export.

It is a narrow experiment, not a large network topology.','["throughput","calculation","scale","complexity"]','["Throughput Calculation","Scale / Complexity"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-091-s012-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Throughput Calculation"],"section_title":"Throughput Calculation","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":190,"source_line_start":190,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Throughput is converted to Mbps from the flow statistics.","text_sha256":"8f226eb540f0b0f7af3d4676e647d94e3d0e34446cec8925b9b49906b49fd192","unit_id":"s012","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-091-s012-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Throughput Calculation"],"section_title":"Throughput Calculation","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":192,"source_line_start":192,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The resulting value is paired with the distance used for that run.","text_sha256":"a4e9f7da9ad73a07be9a39a3f73dd7559dfaff4cf66a6d58a34cfcc71d8a54a7","unit_id":"s012","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-091-s012-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Throughput Calculation"],"section_title":"Throughput Calculation","source_file":"repositories/repo-091-RogersExperiment/README.md","source_line_end":194,"source_line_start":194,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"These pairs form the output series.","text_sha256":"3e4cf0b1f3adabd011dca2d0ae68404091f27f47d8e161b33a44688c5afedb67","unit_id":"s012","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-091-s012-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Throughput