INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-092-rd010',92,'Coptic',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4096,24,287,'Section: Skills Demonstrated > Language/Data Engineering

one-to-many lexical mapping

dialect/form mapping

Bohairic normalization

Unicode-aware source data

domain-data curation

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Software

JavaScript object lookup

browser UI integration

Python dictionary representation

static application design

data-driven frontend behavior

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Data-Quality Awareness

The repository also surfaces practical schema lessons around duplicate keys and multi-valued lexical data.

Section: What Was Learned / Capability Developed

The project reinforces that language software is often constrained by data modeling more than by interface code.

Representing several valid forms requires schemas that preserve alternatives.

Dialect conversion requires explicit normalization rules.

Large hand-maintained mappings also expose why validation tooling and provenance become increasingly important as a corpus grows.

Those lessons are directly relevant to later RAG/corpus-building work in the portfolio.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

Coptic script had appeared earlier in repository 006 Egypt.

This repository should therefore not be tagged as the first Coptic-script use in the portfolio.

The earlier project mixed Ancient Egyptian transliteration, calendars, numbers, names, and Coptic representations inside a broader historical-language utility.

Repository 092 narrows the focus to Coptic lexical tooling and Bohairic mapping.

Section: Historical Significance

Within the processed corpus, this is the earliest observed repository centered primarily on Coptic lexicography and Bohairic-oriented form mapping.

The repository shows that specialized linguistic data remained a recurring technical domain several years after the earliest Egyptinator work.

Section: Overall Narrative

Coptic is a specialized language-data project that combines a browser Coptic lookup tool with large Python/JavaScript lexicons and an explicit Bohairic form-mapping layer.

Its engineering value lies in domain corpus construction, Unicode script handling, one-to-many lexical representation, and dialect normalization.

It continues one of the oldest themes in the portfolio while making the work more linguistically focused and data-structured.','["coptic","coptic-script","bohairic","lexicography","lexicon","dictionary","unicode","domain-data","javascript","python","skills","demonstrated","language/data","engineering","software","data-quality","awareness","learned","capability","developed","portfolio","evolution","context","historical"]','["Skills Demonstrated","What Was Learned / Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-092-s026-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Language/Data Engineering"],"section_title":"Language/Data Engineering","source_file":"repositories/repo-092-Coptic/README.md","source_line_end":309,"source_line_start":309,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- one-to-many lexical mapping","text_sha256":"91f269afc1e3274c9c8dcfa1be70c6125bf4b4f3846f96ce64ef656ac8b1cebe","unit_id":"s026","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-092-s026-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Language/Data Engineering"],"section_title":"Language/Data Engineering","source_file":"repositories/repo-092-Coptic/README.md","source_line_end":310,"source_line_start":310,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- dialect/form mapping","text_sha256":"b371e6cace805c7e30b17f2f14de1f116f2d8576828a6f6a8161df512ef35a57","unit_id":"s026","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-092-s026-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s026","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Language/Data Engineering"],"section_title":"Language/Data Engineering","source_file":"repositories/repo-092-Coptic/README.md","source_line_end":311,"source_