INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-094-rd007',94,'Fast-FTP',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','positive','interpretive',0.3522,2,109,'Section: Throughput Measurement

The controller records transfer timing.

It converts payload size and elapsed time into Mbps.

This ties the file-transfer experiment to a performance-measurement concern that becomes much larger in repository 095.

The metric is an application-observed transfer rate.

It is not a physical-layer throughput measurement.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Performance Observation

Transfer duration and Mbps are calculated directly in the client.

Section: Scale / Complexity

The source footprint is modest.

Protocol complexity is meaningful because FTP requires coordination of two TCP connections and stateful responses.

The implementation covers more than a trivial socket send:

control greeting;

authentication;

transfer mode;

passive negotiation;

data stream;

completion responses;

