INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-094-rd008',94,'Fast-FTP',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','repository_specific',0.4006,15,254,'Section: Language Classification Boundary

MainController.m has an Objective-C-style filename extension.

Its contents are Swift.

My.swift contains the same implementation blob.

The repository therefore has inconsistent file naming/history.

For retrieval, the implementation should be tagged swift rather than inferred as Objective-C from the filename or GitHub primary-language metadata.

This is exactly the kind of corpus-cleaning correction that raw repository metadata cannot provide reliably.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Manual Protocol Sequencing

The controller maps numeric FTP replies into the next protocol action.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Passive Data-Channel Negotiation

The implementation parses a PASV response and creates a second connection.

Section: Major Engineering Work > File Upload

It sends a binary file through the data stream after issuing STOR.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Native Stream Integration

Foundation stream callbacks and run-loop scheduling are used instead of a browser/networking abstraction.

Section: Engineering Discipline

Useful discipline choices include:

explicit protocol reply-code handling;

binary transfer mode;

passive-address parsing;

separate control/data streams;

cleanup/state transitions;

performance timing.

Repository hygiene is weaker around duplicated content and mismatched .m/Swift naming.

That is captured as a corpus fact because it affects automated language classification.

Section: Skills Demonstrated

Swift networking

Foundation streams

event-driven stream handling

FTP protocol understanding

FTP reply-code parsing

passive FTP

binary transfers

dual-channel protocol coordination

file I/O

transfer timing

throughput calculation

protocol-state management

corpus metadata correction

Section: What Was Learned / Capability Developed

The repository develops understanding of how an application protocol sits on top of TCP.

FTP makes that especially visible because control and data are separate connections.','["swift","foundation","pasv","stor","data-channel","language","classification","boundary","major","engineering","work","manual","protocol","sequencing","passive","negotiation","file","upload","native","stream","integration","discipline","skills","demonstrated"]','["Language Classification Boundary","Major Engineering Work","Engineering Discipline","Skills Demonstrated","What Was Learned / Capability Developed"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-094-s014-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Language Classification Boundary"],"section_title":"Language Classification Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-094-Fast-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":192,"source_line_start":192,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"`MainController.m` has an Objective-C-style filename extension.","text_sha256":"973856ec9eb0683cb74adb40c3bf64a4829065247f2e9108ce1cf6d094f549fd","unit_id":"s014","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-094-s014-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Language Classification Boundary"],"section_title":"Language Classification Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-094-Fast-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":194,"source_line_start":194,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Its contents are Swift.","text_sha256":"1089ad5adc653c868903f4b31763dc282c5261c9633e7e5e971fc6ff13ab0e35","unit_id":"s014","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-094-s014-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Language Classification Boundary"],"section_title":"Language Classification Boundary","source_file":"repositories/repo-094-Fast-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":196,"source_line_start":196,"specificity_score":0.58,"