INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-095-rd008',95,'Private-FTP',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3525,6,239,'Section: Serial Instrument Discovery

The GUI can work with serial ports.

It includes connection/disconnection behavior and terminal-oriented command exchange.

This bridges desktop application code with physical test equipment.

The tool is not merely plotting synthetic arrays.

Its design is centered around controlling and collecting from an external instrument.

Section: SCPI Command Workflow

SCPI is a command language commonly used by measurement instruments.

The GUI exposes custom command entry and structured sweep controls.

This gives the user both:

low-level terminal access;
higher-level form controls for common measurement tasks.

That is a useful instrumentation UX pattern because advanced users can escape the fixed UI when needed.

Section: Sweep Configuration

The GUI contains controls around parameters including:

center frequency;

frequency span;

resolution bandwidth (RBW);

dwell behavior;

reference level;

attenuation;

units;

sweep-point count;

sweep count.

These are domain-specific RF measurement settings.

Their presence is stronger evidence of spectrum-analyzer understanding than a generic serial terminal would provide.

Section: Multi-Sweep Recording

The tool supports repeated sweeps rather than only one instantaneous trace.

Multiple sweeps allow temporal comparison and max-hold accumulation.

This is especially useful when intermittent emissions need to be captured across time.

The commit history explicitly includes iterative changes around sweep behavior, RBW handling, and GUI quality.

That history supports meaningful owner iteration on this subsystem.

Section: Max Hold

Max hold retains the maximum observed amplitude at each frequency bin across multiple sweeps.

The GUI implements max-hold-oriented behavior.

This is a domain-specific signal-analysis feature.','["scpi","spectrum-analyzer","multi-sweep","max-hold","serial","instrument","discovery","command","workflow","sweep","configuration","recording","hold"]','["Serial Instrument Discovery","SCPI Command Workflow","Sweep Configuration","Multi-Sweep Recording","Max Hold"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-095-s028-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s028","section_path":["Serial Instrument Discovery"],"section_title":"Serial Instrument Discovery","source_file":"repositories/repo-095-Private-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":343,"source_line_start":343,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The GUI can work with serial ports.","text_sha256":"ac82304d796eb21cdd8ebac813fcd52b79918a23c6f4cc508441aaf6a7ff7182","unit_id":"s028","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-095-s028-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s028","section_path":["Serial Instrument Discovery"],"section_title":"Serial Instrument Discovery","source_file":"repositories/repo-095-Private-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":345,"source_line_start":345,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It includes connection/disconnection behavior and terminal-oriented command exchange.","text_sha256":"4ce9dc0c9335b7a20e2ed2ab17f6e343b04a0f50c576f46e40ab535e479ad83c","unit_id":"s028","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-095-s028-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s028","section_path":["Serial Instrument Discovery"],"section_title":"Serial Instrument Discovery","source_file":"repositories/repo-095-Private-FTP/README.md","source_line_end":347,"source_line_start":347,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This bridges desktop application code with physical test equipment.","text_sha256":"5dd8c39a1dc67da92650cb8124a34fffbeeadaaac2e4b1a66a9