INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-096-rd003',96,'SocketLib',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4192,28,170,'Section: What the Project Is

SocketLib is a hand-built Python DHCP server experiment.

The program binds to DHCP server UDP port 67.

It receives broadcast/client packets, parses BOOTP/DHCP fields, identifies message type, allocates an address from an in-memory pool, and constructs DHCP OFFER, ACK, or NAK replies.

Replies are broadcast toward DHCP client port 68 where appropriate.

The source therefore demonstrates protocol implementation below the level of ordinary HTTP/TCP application programming.

Section: Project Scope

The retained server supports key DHCP mechanics including:

UDP server binding;

socket broadcast mode;

BOOTP header parsing;

transaction ID extraction;

client hardware/MAC address extraction;

DHCP option parsing;

DHCP magic cookie handling;

DHCP DISCOVER recognition;

address offer allocation;

DHCP OFFER construction;

DHCP REQUEST recognition;

requested-IP extraction;

ACK generation;

NAK generation;

subnet mask option;

router option;

DNS option;

lease-time option;

server-identifier option;

lease expiration/reuse;

in-memory MAC-to-IP lease tracking.

The implementation intentionally covers a core subset rather than every DHCP message/state.

Section: Technical Stack

Python

socket

UDP

broadcast sockets

DHCP

BOOTP

binary packet parsing

struct.pack

struct.unpack

IPv4 address packing','["python","broadcast","dhcp","bootp","ipv4","server-identifier","scope","technical","stack"]','["What the Project Is","Project Scope","Technical Stack"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-096-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":4,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-096-SocketLib/README.md","source_line_end":33,"source_line_start":33,"specificity_score":0.72,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"SocketLib is a hand-built Python DHCP server experiment.","text_sha256":"0982f954b302f4017fac15548f1dfb14fd99d81dc1195e0a5453e0b9ee402ed1","unit_id":"s003","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-096-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-096-SocketLib/README.md","source_line_end":35,"source_line_start":35,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The program binds to DHCP server UDP port 67.","text_sha256":"458ca0e7dbe13b547315f67bbd76278a26dbb41c2f3eb49c7b87b0c46a6bb617","unit_id":"s003","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-096-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What the Project Is"],"section_title":"What the Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-096-SocketLib/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It receives broadcast/client packets, parses BOOTP/DHCP fields, identifies message type, allocates an address from an in-memory pool, and constructs DHCP OFFER, ACK, or NAK replies.","text_sha256":"26d40a28bae76abc4fd1c39a160e3df56fd0f570f44b03c029d1ace6c6b0c360","unit_id":"s003","word_count":25},{"block_id":"repo-096-s003-b004","canonical_ca