INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-097-rd003',97,'Thesis-Scripts',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3685,20,188,'Section: What This Project Is

Thesis-Scripts is a research-support repository for collecting and interpreting network measurements around wireless experiments.

The Aruba tools transform controller or station telemetry logs into focused views of one client device.

The DHCP component provides local address-allocation behavior through a directly implemented BOOTP/DHCP server.

Section: Project Scope

The retained code covers:

Aruba station-log filtering;

target-MAC extraction;

BSSID history;

BSSID transition detection;

Wi-Fi channel history;

channel transition detection;

RSSI extraction;

SNR extraction;

simple signal statistics;

timeline plotting;

filtered text-report generation;

timestamped continuous ping logging;

long-running iperf3 acquisition;

real-time iperf3 log tailing;

Windows/Linux ping-command selection;

DHCP request parsing;

DHCP response construction;

address-pool management;

static MAC-to-IP reservations;

lease tracking;

DHCP RELEASE handling;

broadcast UDP replies.

Section: System Shape

The repository can be understood as three independent but complementary tool paths.

Section: Technical Stack > Python

All substantive source in the repository is Python.

The language is used for:

regular-expression log parsing;

file scanning;

plotting;

subprocess control;

timestamping;

socket programming;

binary protocol parsing;

stateful lease management.

Section: Technical Stack > Regular Expressions

The Aruba utilities use regular expressions to recover timestamps and station fields from semi-structured controller output.','["python","bssid","rssi","ping","iperf3","subprocess","dhcp","bootp","address-pool","broadcast","scope","system","shape","technical","stack","regular","expressions"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope","System Shape","Technical Stack"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-097-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-097-Thesis-Scripts/README.md","source_line_end":36,"source_line_start":36,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Thesis-Scripts` is a research-support repository for collecting and interpreting network measurements around wireless experiments.","text_sha256":"c0b20b41282d3a2a034283543f8d73e386f6f272bcc0817d4cd101eb7e3be130","unit_id":"s003","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-097-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-097-Thesis-Scripts/README.md","source_line_end":38,"source_line_start":38,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The Aruba tools transform controller or station telemetry logs into focused views of one client device.","text_sha256":"778b32c7e9e8f26f2eeef642c32c911a4dff35870faa05c5cdc92fe6aea3421b","unit_id":"s003","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-097-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-097-Thesis-Scripts/README.md","source_line_end":42,"source_line_start":42,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repo