INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-098-rd003',98,'Rogers-Experiment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','neutral','repository_specific',0.3559,21,211,'Section: What This Project Is

Rogers-Experiment is a multi-part research workspace for measuring and analyzing wireless-network behavior around a mobile-robot experiment environment.

Aruba access-point logs;

ping latency;

iperf3 throughput;

BSSID;

noise-floor information;

ns-3 Wi-Fi broadcast simulations.

The source therefore represents both physical-experiment support and simulation-oriented network research.

Section: Research Context

The root README documents a Husky robot setup.

It records practical steps for:

placing a host on the robot''s Ethernet subnet;

checking connectivity with ping;

connecting to the robot through SSH;

using the joystick controller.

The experiment task list explicitly references:

two-access-point tests;

single-access-point tests;

uplink;

downlink;

noise-floor measurement;

5G tests.

The retained improvement list shows deliberate iteration in the experiment design.

Section: Experiment Improvements Recorded in the Repository

Completed improvements in the root README include:

unified timestamps across files, logs, latency, and iperf workflows;

use of two Linux laptops for a lighter measurement system;

generating a single main log per experiment rather than separate logs per AP;

moving RF equipment onto a plastic shelf instead of directly on concrete;

reducing transmit power to make roaming occur in the two-AP experiment;

preparing uplink and downlink scripts;

including retransmission information;

adding noise-floor logging commands.

The latest commit adds an additional task to move from Unix-based timestamp handling toward fully unified actual timestamps.','["aruba","bssid","noise-floor","uplink","downlink","ping","iperf3","latency","throughput","linux","ns-3","simulation","research","context","experiment","improvements","recorded"]','["What This Project Is","Research Context","Experiment Improvements Recorded in the Repository"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-098-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-098-Rogers-Experiment/README.md","source_line_end":46,"source_line_start":46,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Rogers-Experiment` is a multi-part research workspace for measuring and analyzing wireless-network behavior around a mobile-robot experiment environment.","text_sha256":"3b18e3cb29c9599df1f61d3bf74cec947a0649d4107a44b0f9a9dbbd3e5885b0","unit_id":"s003","word_count":17},{"block_id":"repo-098-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-098-Rogers-Experiment/README.md","source_line_end":52,"source_line_start":52,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- Aruba access-point logs;","text_sha256":"a2dd9ca057cd8534895a5ebc9a9617db4f97a36555f15d2fb015d6ac7de04c66","unit_id":"s003","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-098-s003-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-098-Rogers-Experiment/README.md","source_line_end":53,"source_line_start":53,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_fre