INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-098-rd011',98,'Rogers-Experiment',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3867,11,239,'Section: Broadcast Research Track > Threaded UDP Broadcast Receiver

receiverGUI.py provides a Tkinter desktop application for receiving UDP broadcast traffic.

The GUI exposes:

port configuration;

thread count;

DHCP/static-IP mode selection;

static IP, subnet, and gateway fields;

start/stop controls;

activity logs;

statistics display.

Section: Broadcast Research Track > Socket Configuration

Each receiver thread creates a UDP socket with:

address reuse;

broadcast capability;

a larger receive buffer;

timeout behavior.

The socket binds to the selected port and receives broadcast datagrams.

Section: Broadcast Research Track > Multi-Threaded Reception

The number of listener threads is configurable.

Python threading.Thread is used to start daemon receiver workers.

A shared stop event coordinates shutdown.

Section: Broadcast Research Track > Thread-Safe Statistics

The receiver uses:

a shared deque;

a lock;

a queue for log messages.

This separates background receive activity from GUI updates.

Section: Broadcast Research Track > Burst Measurement

The receiver groups packets into bursts separated by idle timeout.

For a completed burst it calculates:

packet count;

total bytes;

MiB;

elapsed time;

Mbps.

The statistics are then surfaced in the desktop UI.

Section: Broadcast Research Track > Packaged Executable

The hybrid-approach directory includes a packaged GUI executable.

That is evidence that the receiver tool was packaged for direct execution, while the Python source remains the basis for implementation analysis.

Section: ns-3 Broadcast Simulation

The broadcast simulation is implemented with ns-3 C++ APIs.

Section: ns-3 Broadcast Simulation > Wi-Fi Topology

