INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-102-rd015',102,'George-Sedra-Website',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3726,24,314,'Section: Skills Demonstrated > Data

Schema migration design — strong evidence.

Foreign keys and relational normalization — strong evidence.

Indexes and database constraints — strong evidence.

Repository-layer SQL access — strong evidence.

Lifecycle/history modeling — strong evidence.

Base64 file persistence — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Delivery and Quality

Vite — strong evidence.

ESLint — strong evidence.

TypeScript build/typecheck workflows — strong evidence.

Wrangler — strong evidence.

D1 migration/seeding commands — strong evidence.

Section: Capability Developed

Earlier personal sites established browser and portfolio capabilities; this project turns a company website into a structured business system with:

typed frontend routes;

The engineering object is no longer only a page or utility. It is a product architecture that connects public interactions to persistent business operations.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

React/TypeScript SPA work;

Hono backend development;

Cloudflare Workers conventions;

Cloudflare D1 relational persistence;

It also demonstrates later-stage defensive thinking around constraints, validation, file-size limits, protected downloads, environment secrets, request tracing, and operational lifecycle states.

Section: Historical Significance

George-Sedra-Website marks a transition from frontend company presentation toward full-stack business software.

Its chronology is particularly useful because the repository begins as a website and later gains a serverless backend and persistence architecture without discarding the original product surface.

The September 2026 commit sequence provides strong evidence of deliberate backend decomposition and business-domain modeling.

Section: Overall Repository Narrative

George-Sedra-Website is a full-stack consulting-company platform built from a React/TypeScript frontend and a Hono/Cloudflare backend.

The frontend gives engineering, environmental, real-estate, careers, contact, and company content dedicated routes. The backend models the operational data behind jobs, applications, resumes, contacts, and project inquiries.

Cloudflare D1 provides normalized relational persistence with strict constraints and indexes. Public endpoints accept business inputs; admin endpoints provide protected review and lifecycle operations. Dedicated validation, error handling, middleware, repository modules, request IDs, and Base64 resume persistence demonstrate a materially more structured engineering style than a simple brochure site.','["typescript","react","vite","hono","middleware","wrangler","eslint","skills","demonstrated","data","delivery","quality","capability","developed","portfolio","evolution","context","historical","significance","narrative"]','["Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Repository Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-102-s061-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s061","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Data"],"section_title":"Data","source_file":"repositories/repo-102-George-Sedra-Website/README.md","source_line_end":502,"source_line_start":502,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- **Schema migration design — strong evidence.**","text_sha256":"cf92db4697345cf2150de60156a03ae042508edb634ffa725408274e1c704481","unit_id":"s061","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-102-s061-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s061","section_path":["Skills Demonstrated","Data"],"section_title":"Data","source_file":"repositories/repo-102-George-Sedra-Website/README.md","source_line_end":503,"source_line_start":503,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- **Foreign keys and relational normalization — strong evidence.**","text_sha256":"b0d801f034d62e8faa0c70b11af775838b96356169363cb2594a86cb61a2590e","unit_id":"s061","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-102-s061-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s