The grading harness uses Bash for:

lifecycle orchestration;

Mininet process discovery;

interface inspection;

connectivity tests;

process execution;

sequential/concurrent test coordination;

CSV aggregation.

Section: Technical Stack > Mininet

Mininet supplies virtual hosts, switches, interfaces, links, namespaces, and the network CLI.

Section: Technical Stack > TCP Sockets

The sample load balancer and endpoint programs use direct TCP sockets.

Section: Technical Stack > JSON

Requests/responses use JSON fields to preserve request IDs, client identity, graph input, backend identity, and computed results.

Section: Technical Stack > tmux / mnexec

The grader uses detached tmux sessions and mnexec to run programs inside Mininet host namespaces.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Dual-Subnet Topology Construction

The topology creates two client/backend networks and a load-balancer host with one interface in each subnet.

This exercises explicit interface addressing rather than relying on automatic topology defaults.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Thread-Safe Round-Robin Selection

The load balancer maintains a global backend index and protects selection/update with a threading.Lock.

This is the central concurrency requirement of the assignment.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Client Request Framing

The handler accumulates bytes and splits on newline boundaries, allowing multiple framed requests to travel over one client connection.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Per-Client Concurrency

Every accepted client connection is handled by a daemon thread, allowing the grader to exercise multiple clients concurrently.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Request Correlation

The JSON communication contract carries request IDs through client, load balancer, backend, and response paths.

The verifier checks that received IDs match original IDs.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Automated Interface Validation

The grading script enters Mininet namespaces and inspects expected IP addresses on:

six endpoint interfaces;
both load-balancer interfaces.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Automated Connectivity Matrix

The grader computes expected reachability between client, backend, and load-balancer endpoints, runs pings, and compares observed packet-loss values to expected behavior.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Sequential Request Evaluation

The script runs multiple client rounds one at a time and grades each generated output set independently.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Concurrent Request Evaluation

Three client workloads are launched concurrently, then their combined results are sliced by client IP and graded independently.','["bash","mininet","tmux","mnexec","technical","stack","sockets","json","major","engineering","work","dual-subnet","topology","construction","thread-safe","round-robin","selection","client","request","framing","per-client","concurrency","correlation","automated"]','["Technical Stack","Major Engineering Work"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-103-s013-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Technical Stack","Bash"],"section_title":"Bash","source_file":"repositories/repo-103-test3/README.md","source_line_end":147,"source_line_start":147,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The grading harness uses Bash for:","text_sha256":"631c9f69e53839f6972399d03ce1b2e6ba568efe2702d1cabfd37ce7544d36bd","unit_id":"s013","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-103-s013-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Technical Stack","Bash"],"section_title":"Bash","source_file":"repositories/repo-103-test3/README.md","source_line_end":149,"source_line_start":149,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- lifecycle orchestration;","text_sha256":"e181d02917a6817b9734f7e0360816b6afe7d3c659e677118e3ce2d91d4becf7","unit_id":"s013","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-103-s013-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Technical Stack","Bash"],"section_title":"Bash","source_file":"repositories/repo-103-test3/README.md","source_line_end":150,"source_line_start":150,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- Mininet process discovery;","text_sha256":"f8d9b518aae5250b27fab1f6970c51a638f0de757aeb4b5833bdd4ba0d8f46d8","unit_id":"s013","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-103-s013-b004",