INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-105-rd003',105,'RF-Power-Logging',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3886,9,222,'Section: What This Project Is

RF-Power-Logging is a Python RF measurement toolkit for repeatedly sweeping a tinySA spectrum analyzer and converting raw scan output into structured experiment artifacts.

Section: What This Project Is > Acquisition

The sweep tools:

locate the tinySA USB serial device;

configure resolution bandwidth;

request raw scans;

decode the instrument payload;

convert raw values to dBm;

schedule repeated sweeps;

record timing metadata;

export plots and tables.

Section: What This Project Is > Post-Processing

The processing tool:

discovers per-sweep CSV files;

validates consistent frequency axes;

stacks sweeps into a two-dimensional power matrix;

exports the matrix;

renders waterfall plots by sweep index and by physical frequency.

Section: Project Scope > Instrument Discovery

The code scans serial ports for a fixed USB vendor/product identity:

VID 0x0483;
PID 0x5740.

Section: Project Scope > Spectrum Configuration

Default measurement configuration includes:

start frequency: 2.3 GHz;

end frequency: 2.5 GHz;

401 points;

automatically derived RBW unless explicitly provided.

Section: Project Scope > Automatic Acquisition

Automatic mode supports:

configurable sweep count;

fixed scheduled start period;

high-resolution timing;

stop signaling;

per-sweep start/end/duration metadata;

start-offset measurement;

output directories based on timestamps.

Section: Project Scope > Live Acquisition

A live mode repeatedly performs scans until stop is requested.

Section: Project Scope > Artifact Generation

The repository generates:

one CSV per sweep;

one PNG per sweep;

summary CSV;

PDF run report;','["python","tinysa","rf-power","acquisition","post-processing","scope","instrument","discovery","spectrum","configuration","automatic","live","artifact","generation"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-105-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":4,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-105-RF-Power-Logging/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.72,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`RF-Power-Logging` is a Python RF measurement toolkit for repeatedly sweeping a tinySA spectrum analyzer and converting raw scan output into structured experiment artifacts.","text_sha256":"49dda84e089c405891ca8797683b3760ab17f39e8310d0d65ec934058f498400","unit_id":"s004","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-105-s005-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s005","section_path":["What This Project Is","Acquisition"],"section_title":"Acquisition","source_file":"repositories/repo-105-RF-Power-Logging/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The sweep tools:","text_sha256":"d9ccb9be40f54855db348b4c156a8ed5e2633152a0716d6212e45c12591c3f8d","unit_id":"s005","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-105-s005-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s005","section_path":["What This Project Is","Acquisition"],"section_title":"Acquisition","source_file":"repositories/repo-105-RF-Power-Logging/README.md","source_line_end":45,"source_line_start":45,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- locate the tinySA USB serial device;","text_sha256":"fe677d42c12e04f58bf79f27d710e9dc5d034388d7bca1740202e96614f8bb40","unit_id":"s005","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-10