INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-105-rd005',105,'RF-Power-Logging',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3611,3,287,'Section: Major Engineering Work > Fixed-Period Sweep Scheduling

The remote-oriented acquisition code schedules sweeps against target start times rather than simply sleeping a fixed duration after each completed sweep.

The recorded metadata distinguishes:

scheduled start;

actual start;

end time;

duration;

start offset;

automatically available buffer time.

This directly supports experiment timing analysis.

Section: Major Engineering Work > In-Memory Acquisition Before Export

The later acquisition variant stores automatic-mode sweep data in memory first and performs export after acquisition ends.

That design separates time-sensitive measurement from potentially slower plot/file generation.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Signal-Based Stop Control

A shared stop event coordinates termination behavior.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Per-Sweep CSV Export

Each CSV includes:

frequency;

power in dBm;

export timestamp;

scan count;

sweep index.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Per-Sweep PNG Export

Every sweep can be rendered as a frequency-versus-power plot.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Summary CSV

Run-level summary tables record sweep timing and artifact names.

Section: Major Engineering Work > PDF Reporting

A PDF report contains:

run metadata;

frequency range;

sweep count;

timing summary;

a page for each captured sweep.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Waterfall Matrix Construction

Remote/process.py loads all per-sweep CSVs and stacks power vectors into an N sweeps × M frequency points matrix.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Frequency-Axis Consistency Validation

Before stacking, the processor verifies that every sweep:

has the same point count;
uses the same frequency values.

This prevents combining incompatible measurements into one heatmap.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Waterfall Visualization

The matrix is rendered in two views:

x-axis as bin index;
x-axis as actual frequency.

Color encodes power in dBm.

Section: Engineering Practices > Separation of Acquisition and Analysis

