INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-107-rd003',107,'MyCV',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3472,4,225,'Section: What This Project Is

MyCV is a LaTeX-based curriculum-vitae repository paired with a written strategy for repositioning a technically specialized profile toward broader systems-oriented engineering roles.

First, main.tex provides a reproducible source artifact for a professional CV.

Second, the README records the reasoning used to change how the underlying experience is communicated: wireless work is reframed as one specialization within a wider systems, integration, validation, infrastructure, and debugging profile.

Section: Project Scope > Structured CV Source

The CV is maintained as source text rather than only as an opaque PDF.

LaTeX is used to control:

page geometry;

typography;

headings;

itemized experience bullets;

section composition;

spacing;

hyperlinks;

consistent visual structure.

The source can therefore be revised, diffed, and reproduced through version control.

Section: Project Scope > Career Positioning Strategy

The README explicitly broadens the target role vocabulary beyond narrow RF/RAN research.

The documented target families include:

systems engineering and analysis;

systems integration;

validation / QA engineering;

technical support engineering;

deployment engineering;

telecom systems;

infrastructure and networking;

IoT systems;

platform / operations engineering.

The strategy identifies a recurring engineering pattern across past work:

complex systems debugging;

integration;

validation;

automation;

infrastructure troubleshooting;

performance analysis;

hardware/software/network interaction.

Section: Project Scope > Jargon Translation

The repository contains an explicit communication rule: preserve technical depth while translating niche terminology into language understandable to recruiters, applicant-tracking systems, and non-specialist engineering managers.','["latex","scope","structured","source","career","positioning","strategy","jargon","translation"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-107-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-107-MyCV/README.md","source_line_end":34,"source_line_start":34,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`MyCV` is a LaTeX-based curriculum-vitae repository paired with a written strategy for repositioning a technically specialized profile toward broader systems-oriented engineering roles.","text_sha256":"71720a7e804a1e1d2b5b68c30c40971f3bdc7df250bb38dcb4f080cc97752871","unit_id":"s004","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-107-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-107-MyCV/README.md","source_line_end":38,"source_line_start":38,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"First, `main.tex` provides a reproducible source artifact for a professional CV.","text_sha256":"6d92f5279f20a33f60125312e7cc8b562ffe2102970b566e0fdee0a5ac09cb42","unit_id":"s004","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-107-s004-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-107-MyCV/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_