INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-107-rd007',107,'MyCV',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.2917,6,320,'Section: Engineering Practices > Abstraction Control

Highly specialized terminology is retained where useful but translated into broader system-level outcomes when communicating to general audiences.

Section: Engineering Practices > Evidence Prioritization

The strategy emphasizes concrete engineering activities—debugging, validation, automation, analysis, and integration—over generic motivational language.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Technical Communication

Engineering experience summarization — strong evidence.

Audience-aware terminology selection — strong evidence.

Technical jargon translation — strong evidence.

Concise professional positioning — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Document Engineering

LaTeX authoring — strong evidence.

Structured document composition — strong evidence.

Source-controlled professional documents — strong evidence.

Reproducible typesetting — strong evidence.

Section: Capability Developed

MyCV shows an explicit shift from merely listing technical work toward engineering the communication layer around that work.

The repository recognizes that a technically accurate document can still fail if its abstraction level is mismatched to its reader. The documented solution is to surface systems-level value first, then retain specialist wireless detail as supporting evidence.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

MyCV adds a different kind of engineering evidence: deliberate curation of the portfolio into a career-facing systems narrative.

The repository therefore acts as a bridge between accumulated technical work and how that work is made legible to external decision-makers.

Section: Historical Significance

Within the processed corpus so far, this is the clearest explicit artifact dedicated to reframing a specialist technical profile into a broader systems/integration/validation engineering identity while preserving the underlying technical evidence.

Section: Overall Repository Narrative

MyCV is a small but purposeful source-controlled career-document repository.

Its LaTeX file provides a reproducible professional CV, while its README records a concrete repositioning strategy: broaden the target role set, reduce unnecessary niche terminology, lead with systems/integration/validation value, and keep wireless expertise as a specialization rather than the only identity.

The strongest evidence is therefore in technical communication and information architecture. The repository demonstrates how accumulated engineering work is selected, abstracted, organized, and rendered into a maintainable professional artifact.','["career-document","latex","engineering","practices","abstraction","control","prioritization","skills","demonstrated","technical","communication","document","capability","developed","portfolio","evolution","context","historical","significance","narrative"]','["Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Repository Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-107-s023-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s023","section_path":["Engineering Practices","Abstraction Control"],"section_title":"Abstraction Control","source_file":"repositories/repo-107-MyCV/README.md","source_line_end":183,"source_line_start":183,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Highly specialized terminology is retained where useful but translated into broader system-level outcomes when communicating to general audiences.","text_sha256":"8fdb9431f28b5e6347b035ac1819609031eb4186ba4ce661f9290bd0e75bd1c0","unit_id":"s023","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-107-s024-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s024","section_path":["Engineering Practices","Evidence Prioritization"],"section_title":"Evidence Prioritization","source_file":"repositories/repo-107-MyCV/README.md","source_line_end":187,"source_line_start":187,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The strategy emphasizes concrete engineering activities—debugging, validation, automation, analysis, and integration—over generic motivational language.","text_sha256":"f1ef865a32b6198f0196c3d6bcd18eec0a00464bf43f14c857fdffae22cf1d65","unit_id":"s024","word_count"