INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-108-rd003',108,'Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3953,19,218,'Section: What This Project Is

Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit is a collection of engineering utilities for provisioning, simulating, and observing AquaSensing gateway/sensor behavior.

registering and auditing gateway-build metadata in Azure SQL;

simulating hardware telemetry into Azure IoT Hub over MQTT;

simulating periodic sensor power events from an ESP32 into Firebase;

This creates a practical test ecosystem around devices that have firmware, cellular/SIM attributes, BLE build modes, cloud telemetry, and quality-control state.

Section: Project Scope > Gateway Registration Manager

Gateway-Registerar.py implements a CustomTkinter desktop application backed by Azure SQL.

Its declared workflow includes:

password-based database login;

Azure SQL connection testing;

automatic table creation;

gateway-record insertion;

record updates;

searching and viewing records;

loading an existing record back into the form;

deleting records.

The application therefore acts as an operational CRUD tool around gateway provisioning history.

Section: Project Scope > Gateway Addition Data Model

The Azure SQL table stores concrete gateway-build and validation fields including:

gateway ID;

programmer/operator name;

ICCID;

BLE build mode;

LTE firmware status;

quality-check result;

LTE modem firmware version;

SIM provider;

data-limit enforcement;

in-force date;

deployment/testing purpose;

internal/external usage scope;

intended user;

creation/update timestamps.

Several columns contain SQL CHECK constraints so allowed workflow states are enforced by the database schema.

Section: Project Scope > Azure SQL Bootstrap

The desktop tool checks INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES and creates dbo.GatewayAdditionLogs when it does not already exist.','["tkinter","customtkinter","mqtt","esp32","scope","gateway","registration","manager","addition","data","model","azure","bootstrap"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-108-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit/README.md","source_line_end":36,"source_line_start":36,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit` is a collection of engineering utilities for provisioning, simulating, and observing AquaSensing gateway/sensor behavior.","text_sha256":"6c2bd1762815037d644554cacc8056b1a4de072e3be348fb5c0bb51bd25997d0","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-108-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- registering and auditing gateway-build metadata in Azure SQL;","text_sha256":"1e18c93137119312cd7a03fdf450168e0fc9ec3275324bbe1e7e0c77bfb032ec","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-108-s004-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":41,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- simulating hardware telemetry into