INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-108-rd008',108,'Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4002,16,327,'Section: Major Engineering Work > Operational Gateway Data Modeling

The Azure SQL schema captures both identity and lifecycle/quality metadata for gateways.

It is not a generic key/value table: typed columns and CHECK constraints encode allowed build and deployment states.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Parameterized CRUD Layer

Database operations are centralized in DatabaseManager and use parameters for user data.

The GUI is therefore separated from direct cursor-management details.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Simulated IoT Telemetry

The MQTT publisher creates a controllable stand-in for hardware telemetry.

This allows a tester to vary beacon identity and credentials while holding the rest of the test payload stable.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Background Network Work

MQTT connection/publish operations run on a daemon thread and use Tkinter''s event loop to apply UI updates safely afterward.

This avoids freezing the desktop interface during connection waits.

Section: Major Engineering Work > Publish Completion Signaling

Threading events are used to wait for MQTT connection and publish callbacks with bounded timeouts.

The application distinguishes broker rejection, timeout, publish-call failure, and successful publish completion.

Section: Major Engineering Work > End-to-End Alert Visibility

The repository pairs event generation with a browser monitoring surface, making simulated hardware activity inspectable outside the device serial console.

Section: Engineering Practices > Separation of Concerns

The repository separates:

provisioning data management;

cloud telemetry simulation;

embedded hardware simulation;

browser observation.

Section: Engineering Practices > Secure Transport Configuration

Azure SQL enables encryption and certificate validation, while MQTT uses TLS with insecure mode disabled.

Section: Engineering Practices > Structured Operational Data

Gateway build metadata is persisted in explicit relational columns rather than free-form notes alone.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Python and Desktop Tooling

Python application development — strong evidence.

Tkinter / CustomTkinter UI development — strong evidence.

Background-threaded network operations — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Databases

Azure SQL integration — strong evidence.

PyODBC — strong evidence.

Relational schema design — strong evidence.

Parameterized CRUD — strong evidence.

SQL constraints — strong evidence.','["python","tkinter","customtkinter","pyodbc","mqtt","major","engineering","work","operational","gateway","data","modeling","parameterized","crud","layer","simulated","telemetry","background","network","publish","completion","signaling","end-to-end","alert"]','["Major Engineering Work","Engineering Practices","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-108-s029-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s029","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Operational Gateway Data Modeling"],"section_title":"Operational Gateway Data Modeling","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit/README.md","source_line_end":280,"source_line_start":280,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The Azure SQL schema captures both identity and lifecycle/quality metadata for gateways.","text_sha256":"4f62f3c26a0b92b7a503458843da016c6c3ae17bca8376ac08feaa9031951525","unit_id":"s029","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-108-s029-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s029","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Operational Gateway Data Modeling"],"section_title":"Operational Gateway Data Modeling","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-Auto-Test-Kit/README.md","source_line_end":282,"source_line_start":282,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It is not a generic key/value table: typed columns and `CHECK` constraints encode allowed build and deployment states.","text_sha256":"418be724bfb26046583a8fe541010bf66ffc4d95c155e413eef780d90dd1a8f1","unit_id":"s029","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-108-s031-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Parameterized CRUD Layer"],"section_title":"Parameterized CRUD Layer","source_file":"repositories/repo-108-Aquaseninsg-