INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-109-rd010',109,'RobohubDemo',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','testing_quality','mixed','repository_specific',0.3704,5,162,'Section: Major Engineering Work > Defensive Stream Grouping

Explicit stream identity prevents two logically distinct tests on the same interface from being merged accidentally.

Missing identities are isolated rather than guessed.

Section: Testing and Verification > Firebase Route Test

The GUI provides a dedicated POST test through the selected sending interface before a measurement run.

The test creates a distinct stream code and reports HTTP success/failure.

Section: Testing and Verification > Configuration Validation

Before starting, the application validates items such as:

Firebase URL form;

stream code presence;

selected interfaces;

target IPv4 address;

port range;

protocol;

timing and stream configuration.

Section: Testing and Verification > iperf3 Availability Check

The application checks whether iperf3 is available before launching a run.

Section: Testing and Verification > Runtime Diagnostics

Parsed counts, successful posts, failures, routes, raw lines, stream-code grouping, and timestamp sources are surfaced during operation.

Section: Engineering Practices > Defensive Compatibility

The browser normalizes multiple field aliases but avoids unsafe guesses for missing stream identity.','["iperf3","major","engineering","work","defensive","stream","grouping","testing","verification","firebase","route","test","configuration","validation","availability","check","runtime","diagnostics","practices","compatibility"]','["Major Engineering Work","Testing and Verification","Engineering Practices"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-109-s045-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s045","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Defensive Stream Grouping"],"section_title":"Defensive Stream Grouping","source_file":"repositories/repo-109-RobohubDemo/README.md","source_line_end":404,"source_line_start":404,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Explicit stream identity prevents two logically distinct tests on the same interface from being merged accidentally.","text_sha256":"694e610c1f3aa1d3adb2b5707dff69f6891571db8e09340bd470c48125c4cabe","unit_id":"s045","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-109-s045-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"repository_limitation","section_id":"s045","section_path":["Major Engineering Work","Defensive Stream Grouping"],"section_title":"Defensive Stream Grouping","source_file":"repositories/repo-109-RobohubDemo/README.md","source_line_end":406,"source_line_start":406,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Missing identities are isolated rather than guessed.","text_sha256":"201f1c77266e36cb987f532bf480169bc18f7cdc5be1ccd3adb6e7a414787274","unit_id":"s045","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-109-s047-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s047","section_path":["Testing and Verification","Firebase Route Test"],"section_title":"Firebase Route Test","source_file":"repositories/repo-109-RobohubDemo/README.md","source_line_end":412,"source_line_start":412,"