2","word_count":25},{"block_id":"repo-110-s012-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Automated PDF Build Pipeline","Generated Artifact Commit"],"section_title":"Generated Artifact Commit","source_file":"repositories/repo-110-CV-Highly-Organized/README.md","source_line_end":126,"source_line_start":126,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"When changes exist, it configures the GitHub Actions bot identity, commits the generated PDFs, and pushes them back to the repository.","text_sha256":"619fc920bac09bfcbcc9d0686b7070f273458cbbffb53a6f946c901ea6a18b03","unit_id":"s012","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-110-s012-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Automated PDF Build Pipeline","Generated Artifact Commit"],"section_title":"Generated Artifact Commit","source_file":"repositories/repo-110-CV-Highly-Organized/README.md","source_line_end":128,"source_line_start":128,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This creates a source-plus-built-artifact workflow in which users can retrieve a current PDF without compiling LaTeX locally.","text_sha256":"48ff668d0c811bdccb41a6fde6ed90974058ba9e5e5288756cb6406ebaac90ec","unit_id":"s012","word_count":17}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-110-CV-Highly-Organized/README.md","document_text_sha256":"b5efe4256f19357a413cfca8431f86efad5bce3e5c9487ba7529e9668a9c5ac1","earliest_source_line":102,"embedding_text_sha256":"5af46b6c69b0e377f64cee091634f0ffacea1bf82a24af38eb09803fff378de1","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"8bdf14302810255026e5d34a9c2e17349bd907693751cbdebe02d14d1fb57b4e","repository_source_line_end":601,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-110-rd005',110,'CV-Highly-Organized',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.365,10,260,'Section: Authenticated Career CV Manager > Browser Application

search;

grid/list views;

dark/light theme;

repository refresh;

CV/folder statistics;

built-PDF download actions;

status toasts and error states.

Section: Authenticated Career CV Manager > Fixed Repository Boundary

The browser is intentionally scoped to one fixed GitHub repository:

kirolossedra/CV-Highly-Organized.

The application does not ask the user to supply arbitrary owner/repository names.

This gives the UI a narrow operational purpose: browse and retrieve this particular CV library.

Section: Authenticated Career CV Manager > Recursive GitHub Tree Loading

The application calls the GitHub repository tree endpoint with recursive traversal enabled.

The returned paths are converted into an in-memory folder structure.

The builder:

filters hidden/build/dependency paths;

creates folder nodes from path segments;

recognizes built main.pdf blobs;

associates each PDF with a sibling main.tex source path;

sorts folders and files;

counts descendant PDFs;

produces flat folder/file lists for search and statistics.

Section: Authenticated Career CV Manager > Dynamic Hierarchy

The frontend does not maintain a hard-coded JavaScript list of every CV category.

It derives the navigation tree from the GitHub repository itself.

New qualifying folders/PDFs can therefore appear in the browser without manually changing a second category registry in the frontend.

Section: Authenticated Career CV Manager > Repository Cache

The recursive tree response is cached in localStorage.

The application:

namespaces the cache by owner/repository/branch;

records synchronization time;

accepts cached data only within a bounded age;

renders cached data quickly;

then performs a forced background refresh.

This balances responsiveness with repository freshness.

