INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-110-rd011',110,'CV-Highly-Organized',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.4813,29,338,'Section: Auxiliary nRF RSSI Measurement Utility > Cutoff Events

gap at the transition.

This is direct evidence of turning two-board signal observations into structured events.

Section: Auxiliary Technical Stack > Python

Python implements serial discovery, run management, event modeling, and GUI orchestration.

Section: Auxiliary Technical Stack > PySerial

PySerial enumerates and reads J-Link/nRF serial interfaces.

Section: Auxiliary Technical Stack > PySide6

PySide6 implements the desktop application UI and worker-thread signaling.

Section: Auxiliary Technical Stack > pyqtgraph

pyqtgraph renders live RSSI data.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Document Engineering

LaTeX — strong evidence.

Multi-document information architecture — strong evidence.

Role-specific document variants — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > CI / Delivery

GitHub Actions — strong evidence.

Automated LaTeX compilation — strong evidence.

Generated artifact commits — strong evidence.

Path-filtered workflow triggers — strong evidence.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Auxiliary Hardware Tooling

nRF/J-Link serial discovery — strong evidence.

Physical-device/interface disambiguation — strong evidence.

PySide6 — strong evidence.

pyqtgraph — strong evidence.

Live RSSI visualization — strong evidence.

Section: Capability Developed

Role variants are structured as source, reproducibly compiled, versioned together, exposed through a derived repository hierarchy, authenticated, cached, searchable, and downloadable as built artifacts.

Section: Portfolio Evolution Context

Repository 107 established the explicit career-repositioning strategy in a single LaTeX CV repository.

CV-Highly-Organized expands that approach into a managed family of variants with automated compilation and an application interface over the resulting artifact library.

The progression is therefore from one source-controlled CV to a reusable career-document platform organized around multiple positioning strategies.

Section: Historical Significance

a nested multi-CV LaTeX library;

Section: Overall Repository Narrative

CV-Highly-Organized is a structured career-document repository that applies software-engineering practices to a growing set of LaTeX CV variants.

The repository taxonomy keeps multiple role-positioned documents on one branch. GitHub Actions compiles every main.tex, commits changed PDFs, and turns the repository into a source-plus-artifact store. An authenticated standalone web application then reads the recursive GitHub tree, reconstructs the hierarchy, caches it locally, supports search and responsive navigation, and downloads the current CI-built PDF with a useful timestamped filename.','["latex","python","search","j-link","pyserial","pyside6","pyqtgraph","rssi","auxiliary","measurement","utility","cutoff","events","technical","stack","skills","demonstrated","document","engineering","delivery","hardware","tooling","capability","developed"]','["Auxiliary nRF RSSI Measurement Utility","Auxiliary Technical Stack","Skills Demonstrated","Capability Developed","Portfolio Evolution Context","Historical Significance","Overall Repository Narrative"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-110-s057-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s057","section_path":["Auxiliary nRF RSSI Measurement Utility","Cutoff Events"],"section_title":"Cutoff Events","source_file":"repositories/repo-110-CV-Highly-Organized/README.md","source_line_end":424,"source_line_start":424,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- gap at the transition.","text_sha256":"b179921875f2dc468b54361a27092a42eb4a65513d2066ea42762fd5a62dc05e","unit_id":"s057","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-110-s057-b009","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s057","section_path":["Auxiliary nRF RSSI Measurement Utility","Cutoff Events"],"section_title":"Cutoff Events","source_file":"repositories/repo-110-CV-Highly-Organized/README.md","source_line_end":426,"source_line_start":426,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is direct evidence of turning two-board signal observations into structured events.","text_sha256":"8d