INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-111-rd006',111,'MegaRepo',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3836,13,235,'Section: Ruby Library Manager > Collection Service

book addition/removal;

lookup;

search;

available/borrowed subsets;

sorted books;

aggregate statistics.

Section: Ruby Library Manager > Borrowing Workflow

The application protects state transitions:

a borrowed book cannot be borrowed again;

a return applies only to a borrowed book;

borrower identity is stored while the book is checked out.

Section: Ruby Library Manager > JSON Persistence

library_data.json stores the library.

Like the Go implementation, Ruby writes pretty-printed JSON through a temporary file before rename replacement.

Section: Ruby Library Manager > Publication-Year Validation

Book creation validates the year against a range based on the current calendar year.

Section: Ruby Library Manager > Search and Statistics

Search covers title, author, and year text.

Statistics report total, available, and borrowed books.

Section: PHP Inventory Manager > Strictly Typed PHP

inv.php begins with declare(strict_types=1) and uses typed properties, parameter types, and return types throughout the domain model.

Section: PHP Inventory Manager > Inventory Service

Inventory owns the product collection and provides:

load/save;

addition;

sorted listing;

ID lookup;

removal;

search;

low-stock filtering;

total inventory-value calculation;

item count.

Section: PHP Inventory Manager > JSON Persistence

Inventory state is stored in inventory_data.json.

The persistence path:

JSON-encodes structured state;

writes a temporary file;

renames it to the canonical file;

raises runtime exceptions on invalid or failed persistence operations.

Section: PHP Inventory Manager > Inventory Workflow

The menu-driven application supports:

adding products;

listing products;

searching;

quantity updates;

product removal;','["ruby","json","library","manager","collection","service","borrowing","workflow","persistence","publication-year","validation","search","statistics","inventory","strictly","typed"]','["Ruby Library Manager","PHP Inventory Manager"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-111-s014-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Ruby Library Manager","Collection Service"],"section_title":"Collection Service","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":148,"source_line_start":148,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- book addition/removal;","text_sha256":"d0ebffa9ae724e78fe8ac721d19870d5cea9aa772f162f7a9ec8488fc8597cbd","unit_id":"s014","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-111-s014-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Ruby Library Manager","Collection Service"],"section_title":"Collection Service","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":149,"source_line_start":149,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- lookup;","text_sha256":"c008bf7dc46099d18501a7b68e6be0be3f08d148c1733c7c880af794bec01282","unit_id":"s014","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-111-s014-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Ruby Library Manager","Collection Service"],"section_title":"Collection Service","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":150,"source_line_start":150,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- search;","text_sha256":"06640997c06cc280e39006d84e63d02ebe75f69df77d35e6ca9b9cfb539bd590","unit_id":"s014","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-111-s014-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["Ruby Library M