atterns expose how comparable concerns—domain objects, state mutation, persistence, validation, and CLI interaction—are expressed differently in Go, Ruby, PHP, and Rust.","text_sha256":"50e5eb98d3a1fcec0092aca830ff970d6b857124bddbd87ebff5ee9f0b23eebc","unit_id":"s053","word_count":24},{"block_id":"repo-111-s054-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s054","section_path":["Portfolio Evolution Context"],"section_title":"Portfolio Evolution Context","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":403,"source_line_start":403,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The processed corpus already contains extensive C/C++, Java, Python, JavaScript, and other language experience.","text_sha256":"ff6572404758a2c5b0e6926229802394faf6c25754bd2394b9832d08bcf60d7c","unit_id":"s054","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-111-s054-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s054","section_path":["Portfolio Evolution Context"],"section_title":"Portfolio Evolution Context","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":405,"source_line_start":405,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This repository adds direct implementation evidence for Go, Ruby, PHP, and Rust within one focused practice workspace, with substantially more depth in Go/Ruby/PHP than in the Rust file.","text_sha256":"a4c5af7ffe656197d609e20fac3179136fcd4da378f1a7d3d439347b0496f208","unit_id":"s054","word_count":28},{"block_id":"repo-111-s055-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s055","section_path":["Historical Significance"],"section_title":"Historical Significance","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":409,"source_line_start":409,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Within the processed corpus so far, `MegaRepo` is the clearest single repository explicitly practicing several server/general-purpose languages side by side through small stateful applications.","text_sha256":"78e72979a5d53d2a9303bf7f4de0cbfe3939fcdfc2949c8fef207693928958c8","unit_id":"s055","word_count":24},{"block_id":"repo-111-s056-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s056","section_path":["Overall Repository Narrative"],"section_title":"Overall Repository Narrative","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":413,"source_line_start":413,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`MegaRepo` is a multi-language practice workspace containing a Go task manager, Ruby library manager, PHP inventory manager, and small Rust console exercise.","text_sha256":"1f3729b66edb2a242e25258b1a1047f069ed7fc156865b739c372fe25a4123b1","unit_id":"s056","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-111-s056-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s056","section_path":["Overall Repository Narrative"],"section_title":"Overall Repository Narrative","source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","source_line_end":415,"source_line_start":415,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The Go, Ruby, and PHP programs all implement persistent local state, domain rules, search/filtering, input validation, and menu-driven interaction while using the idioms of their respective languages. Their repeated temporary-file-plus-rename persistence pattern also shows attention to safer state replacement rather than direct destructive overwrites.","text_sha256":"1758bcd287da167b7099d541ab66151b07d2cad7415ef70799b36cdd864afb2e","unit_id":"s056","word_count":44}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-111-MegaRepo/README.md","document_text_sha256":"e3eb507a523f0bfd4dd86e611677