INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-112-rd003',112,'WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3318,4,244,'Section: What This Project Is

WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking is an authenticated web application for managing physical laboratory equipment across projects while preserving serial-level location, lending, note, and activity history.

The application also supports item-level notes and photos, generates reporting/export structures, and records user-attributed activity events when operational state changes.

Section: Project Scope > Equipment Records

Equipment is represented under a dedicated Firebase root and contains fields such as:

project;

item type;

name;

comment;

quantity;

registered serial count;

optional Base64 photo;

creation/update timestamps;

creating/updating user identity.

The implemented project categories include named research/engineering contexts plus a generic category.

The item-type vocabulary distinguishes devices and components.

Section: Project Scope > Serial-Level Inventory

Serial numbers are stored separately under their parent equipment item.

Each serial record contains:

serial number;

current location;

lending state;

borrower when lent;

lending timestamp;

creation/update metadata;

creating/updating user identity.

This allows multiple physical instances of one catalog item to be tracked independently.

Section: Project Scope > Quantity / Serial Invariant

The application enforces consistency between declared quantity and registered physical serials.

When adding serials, the service refuses an operation that would make the number of serial records exceed the equipment quantity.

When editing equipment quantity, the quantity cannot be reduced below the number of already registered serial numbers.

This is a concrete domain invariant rather than a UI-only convention.

Section: Project Scope > Duplicate Serial Protection

Incoming serial numbers are normalized for comparison and checked against:

existing serials;
other entries in the same incoming batch.','["scope","equipment","records","serial-level","inventory","quantity","serial","invariant","duplicate","protection"]','["What This Project Is","Project Scope"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-112-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-112-WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking/README.md","source_line_end":37,"source_line_start":37,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking` is an authenticated web application for managing physical laboratory equipment across projects while preserving serial-level location, lending, note, and activity history.","text_sha256":"ca050bcf5e9a64b7a1a9f9a572188971b6a805dba9534f77b386bdc927a49644","unit_id":"s004","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-112-s004-b009","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-112-WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking/README.md","source_line_end":49,"source_line_start":49,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application also supports item-level notes and photos, generates reporting/export structures, and records user-attributed activity events when operational state changes.","text_sha256":"0a62318af51214cec9cceb3500f01179aa15b77685ed2c22c7878a906893b20e","unit_id":"s004","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-112-s006-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s006","section_path":["Project Scope","Equipment Records"],"section_title":"Equipment Records","source_file":"repositories/repo-112-WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking/README.md","source_line_end":57,"source_line_start":57,"sp