INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-112-rd008',112,'WSDL-Inter-project-Item-Tracking',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','architecture_system_design','neutral','repository_specific',0.4151,18,169,'Section: Authentication and Authorization Context > Authenticated Database Boundary

The documented Realtime Database rules isolate tracker data under labEquipmentTracker and require an authenticated user for tracker reads and writes.

The tracker therefore has a clear application-data boundary inside the reused Firebase project.

Section: Realtime Data Architecture > Equipment Subscription

The application subscribes to the equipment branch with onValue and sorts records by update time.

Section: Realtime Data Architecture > Serial Subscription

Serials are subscribed per equipment item and sorted by serial number using numeric-aware comparison.

Section: Realtime Data Architecture > Notes Subscription

Notes are subscribed per item and sorted by note/update time.

Section: Realtime Data Architecture > Activity Subscription

Activity events are queried by occurredAt, limited to a bounded recent set, and streamed live.

The browser therefore receives operational changes without requiring manual page refreshes for each data category.

Section: Technical Stack > Firebase Realtime Database

Realtime Database stores inventory, serials, notes, and activity history while supplying live subscriptions.

