19-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["D1 Image Storage","Architectural Migration Away from R2"],"section_title":"Architectural Migration Away from R2","source_file":"repositories/repo-113-my-portfolio/README.md","source_line_end":239,"source_line_start":239,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"A later migration explicitly renames the legacy image table, recreates it with Base64 image columns, migrates the schema boundary, and removes the old R2 table.","text_sha256":"75f8da2c2d921257abbca6d4a101f766b36e6d5295b11931adf3a719ca03f6d3","unit_id":"s019","word_count":25}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-113-my-portfolio/README.md","document_text_sha256":"8c4dc4df38fe902deeffd85488412fcd9c75e79e0f6a2ccbd3580573c05ec401","earliest_source_line":70,"embedding_text_sha256":"c9fea08f8840c5845d73a3b3675f817dd6b891349367a5610acd817f6c9223d7","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"c810ad7a8b5f56454bb2fbdbf6ee906314b32aa8271c9da3e7180df11d24b307","repository_source_line_end":2019,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-113-rd004',113,'my-portfolio',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','implementation_skills','positive','repository_specific',0.3707,10,296,'Section: Frontend Application > React 19 Application

The current frontend uses React 19.1.1 and React DOM 19.1.1 with TypeScript and Vite.

The application routes among public portfolio surfaces and private owner surfaces without introducing a heavy routing framework.

The route set includes:

the public timeline;

milestone detail views;

skills;

opinions;

Kiro RAG;

admin;

OAuth callback handling.

Section: Frontend Application > Timeline as a Narrative Interface

The main portfolio is modeled as a chronological sequence of milestones rather than a flat list of cards.

Milestones are loaded from the Worker and contain structured date, title, summary, expanded context, images, and optional long-form sections.

The interface supports reversible reveal behavior as the reader moves through the timeline.

The implementation also supports vertical and horizontal timeline presentation.

This makes chronology an interaction model rather than merely a metadata field.

Section: Frontend Application > Seasonal Presentation

The timeline includes season-aware visual transitions tied to the active milestone period.

The implementation uses restrained seasonal effects rather than placing unrelated animations on every navigation event.

Reduced-motion preferences are considered so decorative motion does not become a required interaction dependency.

Section: Frontend Application > Skills Surface

The skills page presents capability evidence associated with source projects rather than reducing skills to an unsupported technology-name list.

The current skills data is versioned in frontend source and supports a visual evidence panel alongside a scrolling capability presentation.

This is an early example inside the product of the same evidence-first philosophy later formalized in the RAG subsystem.

Section: Frontend Application > Responsive Behavior

The application contains separate layout handling for desktop and smaller screens.

Interactive views such as the skills feed, timeline, opinions, and Kiro chat adapt their layout rather than assuming one fixed viewport.

Section: Frontend Application > Reduced-Motion Support

