INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-113-rd016',113,'my-portfolio',NULL,NULL,'direct_evidence','deployment_operations','positive','implemented_or_concrete',0.4498,30,199,'Section: RAG Publishing Pipeline > Bounded Table Ownership

The generated import replaces only the dedicated RAG runtime tables.

It does not mutate:

milestones;

opinions;

authentication handoff state;

Vectorize vectors;

historical Pinecone artifacts.

This is an important operational boundary: publishing evidence is not allowed to rewrite unrelated portfolio content.

Section: CI/CD Deployment Ordering > Worker Deployment

On an eligible main-branch push after the quality gate:

Cloudflare deployment secrets are checked;

dependencies are installed;

remote D1 migrations are applied;

the Worker is deployed.

Section: CI/CD Deployment Ordering > Frontend Deployment

The Netlify deployment job depends on successful Worker deployment.

It then:

validates Netlify credentials;

installs dependencies;

builds the production frontend;

deploys the prebuilt dist directory to production.

This ordering reduces the chance that a newly deployed frontend expects backend/schema behavior that has not yet been deployed.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > CI/CD and Operations

GitHub Actions CI/CD — strong evidence.

quality-gated deployment — strong evidence.

remote schema migration before backend deployment — strong evidence.

backend-before-frontend deployment ordering — strong evidence.

Worker dry-run verification — strong evidence.

architecture regression guards — strong evidence.

Netlify deployment — strong evidence.

