INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-113-rd027',113,'my-portfolio',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3712,9,257,'Section: Historical RAG Migration > Why the Historical Files Matter

The current Worker, package scripts, deployment configuration, and production acceptance evidence establish the active architecture.

Section: Kiro Avatar Evolution

Repository history shows multiple avatar approaches rather than one final model appearing immediately.

The sequence includes:

2D avatar foundation;

articulated React rig;

continuous 2D deformation model;

Three.js GLB runtime and controlled-animation backbone;

Mixamo-ready FBX runtime;

lifecycle-driven procedural motion.

This demonstrates iterative replacement of presentation architecture while preserving the broader Kiro product concept.

Section: Three.js / FBX Runtime > Current Asset Contract

The active avatar asset is:

public/models/kiro/kiro.fbx.

The runtime loads it through Three.js FBXLoader.

The historical component filename kiro-glb-avatar.tsx is retained for compatibility even though the active loader now targets FBX.

Section: Three.js / FBX Runtime > Skeleton Resolution

The 3D subsystem contains model contracts, skeleton/bone alias resolution, diagnostics, inspection utilities, and an animation controller.

The runtime can address meaningful body regions such as:

head;

spine;

upper arms;

forearms.

Section: Three.js / FBX Runtime > Controlled Animation Boundary

The language model is not given arbitrary direct control of skeleton joints.

Application lifecycle state chooses animation semantics.

This creates a strong boundary between generated language and physical/visual character behavior.

Section: Three.js / FBX Runtime > Procedural Motion

The supplied FBX is treated primarily as a rigged master pose rather than a complete conversational animation library.

The controller therefore implements bounded procedural movement including:

calmer standing arm posture from the rig''s base pose;

subtle idle breathing;

attentive retrieval behavior;

alternating arm/head motion while answering;

pointer-follow gaze;

success reaction;

error reaction.','["fbxloader","historical","migration","files","matter","kiro","avatar","evolution","three.js","runtime","asset","contract","skeleton","resolution","controlled","animation","boundary","procedural","motion"]','["Historical RAG Migration","Kiro Avatar Evolution","Three.js / FBX Runtime"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-113-s134-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s134","section_path":["Historical RAG Migration","Why the Historical Files Matter"],"section_title":"Why the Historical Files Matter","source_file":"repositories/repo-113-my-portfolio/README.md","source_line_end":1305,"source_line_start":1305,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The current Worker, package scripts, deployment configuration, and production acceptance evidence establish the active architecture.","text_sha256":"bb214be8b6f3d369ac64e23711c03935f8c565fcf827ebe8eb52cee501e3a1b3","unit_id":"s134","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-113-s135-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s135","section_path":["Kiro Avatar Evolution"],"section_title":"Kiro Avatar Evolution","source_file":"repositories/repo-113-my-portfolio/README.md","source_line_end":1309,"source_line_start":1309,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Repository history shows multiple avatar approaches rather than one final model appearing immediately.","text_sha256":"6576779b2b02eb222184c0f2c6274d419ec9944450290681b5c61941d7803fa7","unit_id":"s135","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-113-s135-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s135","section_path":["Kiro Avatar Evolution"],"section_title":"Kiro Avatar Evolution","source_file":"repositories/repo-113-my-portfolio/README.md","source_line_end":1311,"source_line_start":1311,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The sequence in