-b014","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["Evidence Basis"],"section_title":"Evidence Basis","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":57,"source_line_start":57,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The current Wrangler configuration still contains a placeholder D1 database ID, so this corpus records concrete deployment plumbing without elevating it to verified production deployment.","text_sha256":"1ebf91089a45c768ca0aa6c392b210ce00005382f2f5cc226c8dd0d669bda8b1","unit_id":"s003","word_count":25}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","document_text_sha256":"7d10962f90858c692d3d963fb508d9c0449ed8d77c8341ca83067ba48cb54e14","earliest_source_line":23,"embedding_text_sha256":"42cf23c70db20e7d5b408a08ed825e33730af9a73426064bf4a492648267d33c","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"0ae4e6ed0fd72882e2c4121ba4d8fd8beeac7e87930ca8e9dc1efe5e5acbfb25","repository_source_line_end":1181,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-114-rd003',114,'KiroQuestionsBank',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3515,20,249,'Section: What This Project Is

KiroQuestionsBank is a small full-stack application for creating, organizing, exporting, and importing reusable question banks.

Its most important design choice is conceptual rather than visual: the persistent model deliberately avoids treating one learning source type as the schema.

Chapter 4 Questions is simply a subcategory name.

The backend does not encode chapter number, chapter metadata, or book semantics into its data model.

Section: Question Types

The type contract supports two question kinds:

mcq;
multi_select.

The same shared TypeScript union is used by the client and Worker-side validation contract.

Section: Question Types > MCQ Invariant

An MCQ must contain:

at least two options;
exactly one correct option.

Section: Question Types > Multi-Select Invariant

A multi-select question must contain:

at least two options;
at least two correct options.

The validator rejects invalid correct-answer cardinality before persistence.

Section: Shared TypeScript Contract

src/shared/contracts.ts defines both transport shapes and persisted API view shapes.

Portable types include:

PortableOption;

PortableQuestion;

PortableSubcategory;

PortableCategory;

CategoryExportFile.

Runtime/API view types include:

CategorySummary;

QuestionOption;

Question;

Subcategory;

CategoryDetail.

This keeps browser and Worker code aligned around one domain vocabulary.

Section: Markdown as Stored Content

Question bodies are stored in body_markdown.

Explanations are stored in explanation_markdown.

Option bodies are also represented as Markdown text in the portable contract.

The design therefore keeps source content as portable plain text with lightweight formatting semantics rather than persisting rendered HTML.

The current React question display places the stored string directly into the page rather than passing it through a Markdown renderer.','["typescript","question","types","invariant","multi-select","shared","contract","markdown","stored","content"]','["What This Project Is","Question Types","Shared TypeScript Contract","Markdown as Stored Content"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-114-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":61,"source_line_start":61,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`KiroQuestionsBank` is a small full-stack application for creating, organizing, exporting, and importing reusable question banks.","text_sha256":"380c187c0a29a7ba06d284b9c8bf6c66019446a60c9d3f4ad75820bc6b00377e","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-114-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":63,"source_line_start":63,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Its most important design choice is conceptual rather than visual: the persistent model deliberately avoids treating one learning source type as the schema.","text_sha256":"fd68f7dd73cdb82623505d83b4ca9896f6744debff3fa64a19a16a499edf00a3","unit_id":"s004","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-114-s004-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":88,"source_line_