INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-114-rd007',114,'KiroQuestionsBank',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3857,9,255,'Section: Import Validation > Reuse of Question Validation

This prevents import from becoming a lower-validation bypass around interactive authoring rules.

Section: Import Persistence Strategy

After validation, the Worker creates fresh IDs for the entire imported hierarchy.

It collects three flat row arrays:

subcategory rows;

question rows;

option rows.

The import then builds a D1 batch containing:

category insert;

optional bulk subcategory insert;

optional bulk question insert;

optional bulk option insert.

Section: Import Persistence Strategy > JSON-to-SQL Bulk Expansion

Instead of issuing one prepared statement per imported entity, the Worker serializes each row collection to JSON and uses SQLite/D1 json_each() plus json_extract() to expand it into relational insert rows.

This is a compact bulk-import technique especially appropriate for a portable JSON source format.

Section: Import Persistence Strategy > Unit-Oriented Batch

The category and all of its nested content are submitted through one D1 batch.

The design aims to treat a category package as one import operation rather than exposing a partially imported hierarchy to the application.

Section: Export Logic

GET /api/categories/:id/export first reconstructs the full category hierarchy from D1.

It then maps the runtime objects into the portable representation.

IDs and installation timestamps are omitted from the nested domain data.

The route sets:

JSON content type;

attachment Content-Disposition;

sanitized lowercase file name;

.kiroq.json suffix.

This makes export usable directly from the browser as a category package.

Section: Category Reconstruction

readCategory() rebuilds a nested category from relational tables.

It performs parallel queries for:

subcategories;

questions;

options.

It then groups:

options by question ID;
questions by subcategory ID.','["import","validation","reuse","question","persistence","strategy","json-to-sql","bulk","expansion","unit-oriented","batch","export","logic","category","reconstruction"]','["Import Validation","Import Persistence Strategy","Export Logic","Category Reconstruction"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-114-s031-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Import Validation","Reuse of Question Validation"],"section_title":"Reuse of Question Validation","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":384,"source_line_start":384,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This prevents import from becoming a lower-validation bypass around interactive authoring rules.","text_sha256":"4903c371e2958c154f238d764036bad70b10a4a360930b0fc0e0e7bc709b4f3d","unit_id":"s031","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-114-s032-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s032","section_path":["Import Persistence Strategy"],"section_title":"Import Persistence Strategy","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":388,"source_line_start":388,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"After validation, the Worker creates fresh IDs for the entire imported hierarchy.","text_sha256":"4e9b711ca1f170d1e31093cf7a439acce9f25e63cae0445a9db914d4096dd292","unit_id":"s032","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-114-s032-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s032","section_path":["Import Persistence Strategy"],"section_title":"Import Persistence Strategy","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":390,"source_line_start":390,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"It collects three flat row arrays:","text_sha256":"24954d2c8