INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-114-rd011',114,'KiroQuestionsBank',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3561,11,243,'Section: Question Editor > Correctness UI Behavior

Clicking an MCQ option makes that option the sole selected answer in frontend state.

Multi-select controls toggle answers independently.

Backend validation remains the authority that checks final correctness cardinality.

Section: Question Editor > Dynamic Option Count

The editor begins with four answer options.

Users can add more options.

Options can be removed while at least two remain.

This aligns the UI floor with the domain validator''s minimum option count.

Section: Question Editor > Optional Explanation

The question editor provides an optional explanation field.

The browser sends empty explanation input as null.

Section: Question Editor > Post-Save Reset

After successful question creation, the editor resets:

body;

explanation;

type to MCQ;

default option list;

default first correct option.

It then reloads the selected category.

Section: Import UI

The browser uses a hidden file input triggered by the Import category button.

Accepted file hints include:

.json;

.kiroq.json;

application/json.

The browser:

reads the selected file as text;

parses JSON locally;

posts the parsed object to /api/import;

refreshes category summaries;

selects the imported category.

The browser-level JSON parse gives fast syntax failure, while the Worker still performs authoritative schema/domain validation.

Section: Export UI

The selected category exposes a direct browser link to:

/api/categories/:id/export.

The Worker responds as an attachment, so export requires no extra client-side transformation logic.

Section: Delete UX

Before deleting a category, the React client shows a confirmation dialog that states the category and its questions will be deleted.','["question","editor","correctness","behavior","dynamic","option","count","optional","explanation","post-save","reset","import","export","delete"]','["Question Editor","Import UI","Export UI","Delete UX"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-114-s053-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s053","section_path":["Question Editor","Correctness UI Behavior"],"section_title":"Correctness UI Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":624,"source_line_start":624,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Clicking an MCQ option makes that option the sole selected answer in frontend state.","text_sha256":"459553e111de0e518b5ea1126bcaea961b1fe402341ab7124118107965c98acd","unit_id":"s053","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-114-s053-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s053","section_path":["Question Editor","Correctness UI Behavior"],"section_title":"Correctness UI Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":626,"source_line_start":626,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Multi-select controls toggle answers independently.","text_sha256":"8a2facf7ce74d0c5786f8bba5afc4c27baaf2122e698439186d00aaaeee32869","unit_id":"s053","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-114-s053-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s053","section_path":["Question Editor","Correctness UI Behavior"],"section_title":"Correctness UI Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":628,"source_line_start":628,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Backend validation remains the authority that checks