INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-114-rd017',114,'KiroQuestionsBank',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','engineering_judgment','positive','interpretive',0.3462,3,242,'Section: Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book

The strongest product-modeling decision is the refusal to create a permanent chapter entity merely because one intended use case is book study.

The application instead models the stable relationship:

Book/chapter terminology is kept at the user-authored naming layer.

This reduces schema connascence between:

one content-source type;

persistent backend entities;

import/export format;

frontend workflows.

A future non-book category can use the same API and schema without requiring a backend migration just to remove chapter assumptions.

Section: Architectural Decision: Relational Persistence, JSON Transport

The project deliberately gives persistence and portability different representations.

D1 uses normalized tables because the application needs entity-level editing, counts, ordering, and cascade behavior.

Export uses nested JSON because a portable category package benefits from:

readability;

easy scripting;

easy AI/tool generation;

independence from database IDs;

explicit format versioning.

This is a clean separation of storage model and interchange model.

Section: Architectural Decision: Shared Validation

Question validation lives in the shared contract module rather than being implemented differently for interactive creation and file import.

Both paths enforce the same answer-cardinality semantics.

That prevents a common import feature failure mode where bulk input bypasses the rules used by the normal product UI.

Section: Architectural Decision: Explicit Ordering

Position is persisted at every ordered level below category.

The exported JSON naturally preserves array order.

The importer converts that array order into persistent relational positions.

This prevents data ordering from depending on incidental UUID or timestamp order.','["architectural","decision","encode","book","relational","persistence","json","transport","shared","validation","ordering"]','["Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book","Architectural Decision: Relational Persistence, JSON Transport","Architectural Decision: Shared Validation","Architectural Decision: Explicit Ordering"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-114-s071-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s071","section_path":["Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book"],"section_title":"Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":822,"source_line_start":822,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The strongest product-modeling decision is the refusal to create a permanent chapter entity merely because one intended use case is book study.","text_sha256":"618702228f1d9f0959c6d24921155ffe138927a6fb3bb459e475609da20d2a06","unit_id":"s071","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-114-s071-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s071","section_path":["Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book"],"section_title":"Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book","source_file":"repositories/repo-114-KiroQuestionsBank/README.md","source_line_end":824,"source_line_start":824,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application instead models the stable relationship:","text_sha256":"10dc645437b7f4d2e634ddb6c305c4130931bf28bb39da968ab6ea450eafcb43","unit_id":"s071","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-114-s071-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s071","section_path":["Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book"],"section_title":"Architectural Decision: Do Not Encode the Book","source_f