INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-115-rd003',115,'TransAct',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3114,10,310,'Section: What This Project Is

Participants use an internal accounting unit named Brain Coins to represent transactional exchanges associated with project work, direct transfers, recurring payments, and loans.

The system separates economic accounting from a second concept named T-score.

T-score is designed as a bounded measure of observed transactional reliability inside TransAct.

Its code-level inputs are completed project commitments, overdue accepted work, disputes, repaid loans, and defaulted loans.

The score therefore captures behavioral evidence produced by TransAct workflows instead of attempting to represent technical competence, intelligence, employability, or personal value.

A user can participate in financial-style workflows while the application independently explains how observed commitments affect a reliability score.

The project also explores a loan-approval workflow in which automated review is intentionally subordinate to deterministic domain services and a human administrator.

The administrator must wait through a configured review period before approving or rejecting the application.

The review provider itself cannot directly change balances, approve a loan, reject a loan, or alter T-score.

That boundary makes the application a useful example of separating advisory computation from authoritative state transition logic.

Section: Architectural Shape

The repository is organized as a conventional full-stack application with explicit backend, frontend, database, and operational layers.

Docker Compose supplies a local three-service topology.

The PostgreSQL container has a health check.

The backend waits for the database to become healthy before starting.

The frontend is configured with the backend API URL at image-build time.

This provides a reproducible local environment for exercising the complete application rather than requiring separately provisioned services.

Section: Brain Coin Ledger > Ledger as the Balance Authority

The application does not model a user balance as an independently mutable field.

Balance is calculated from ledger postings associated with an account.

LedgerService.balanceForUser obtains the user''s account and asks the posting repository for the account balance.

The resulting amount is normalized to two decimal places.','["postgresql","docker","t-score","architectural","shape","brain","coin","balance","authority"]','["What This Project Is","Architectural Shape","Brain Coin Ledger"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-115-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":41,"source_line_start":41,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Participants use an internal accounting unit named Brain Coins to represent transactional exchanges associated with project work, direct transfers, recurring payments, and loans.","text_sha256":"f12a45fc45ab5ea2f6bb17a02245a32c15ba02c0cc748b48139f10547e321e19","unit_id":"s003","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-115-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":43,"source_line_start":43,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The system separates economic accounting from a second concept named T-score.","text_sha256":"fab976ef607d0ab5aa9a2162ab1cd84578831a79db7ad0934182d28798ebe97c","unit_id":"s003","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-115-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":45,"source_line_start":45,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"T-score is designed as a bounded measure of observed transactional reliability inside TransAct.","text_sha256":"ad