INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-115-rd004',115,'TransAct',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','product_responsibility','positive','interpretive',0.343,2,241,'Section: Product Concept

The core product concept combines several connected workflows.

Developers have accounts inside the platform.

Brain Coin balances are derived from ledger postings.

Users can transfer Brain Coins directly.

Users can create project deals with other developers.

A developer can accept a proposed project commitment.

The requester can confirm completed work and release payment.

Either party can move accepted work into dispute.

Users can establish recurring salary-style payments.

Users can apply for Brain Coin loans.

Loan review evidence is assembled from recorded transactional history.

Qualification/context information is reviewed separately.

A mandatory administrator review period prevents immediate automated approval.

A human administrator approves or rejects the loan.

Approved loans are disbursed through the same ledger abstraction used by other money movement.

Repayments flow back to the system treasury.

Repaid or defaulted loans become future T-score evidence.

The workflows therefore feed one another.

Project outcomes and loan outcomes become reliability evidence.

Reliability evidence becomes part of future loan review context.

Money movement remains ledger-driven throughout those cycles.

Section: Product Engineering Evidence

TransAct is more than a numerical accounting demo.

It includes named actors, guarded workflows, user-facing pages, recurring processes, administrative review, and auditability.

The system distinguishes normal developer users from administrators.

It supports seeded counterparties so workflows can be exercised immediately.

It provides a dashboard and quick actions oriented around actual product journeys.

The product model is also careful about semantics.

T-score is labeled as transactional reliability rather than technical skill.','["t-score","product","concept","engineering"]','["Product Concept","Product Engineering Evidence"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":69,"source_line_start":69,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The core product concept combines several connected workflows.","text_sha256":"d9f888de20282a5d1fbb6dbd673585ac4a971253abd92a62f68eb875c745c2a5","unit_id":"s004","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":71,"source_line_start":71,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"1. Developers have accounts inside the platform.","text_sha256":"646af169100109a08b4321842a1449a370a5d544bdab8b14f45cb6bb9a3d25fa","unit_id":"s004","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":72,"source_line_start":72,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"2. Brain Coin balances are derived from ledger postings.","text_sha256":"e05b0c03afdfe07d9590a5cc86b979f8d977ca6624096ea0c3e8333d16916b9b","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","sou