":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":77,"source_line_start":77,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"7. Either party can move accepted work into dispute.","text_sha256":"49a202864865880ad76cfde173e4e329f5e10b6c6d86917a84b2066faf745cd6","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b009","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":78,"source_line_start":78,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"8. Users can establish recurring salary-style payments.","text_sha256":"34e1a5755fcd9fbbc30f1b508d031b1c2220976a72bad89dc433d4254354ba4d","unit_id":"s004","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b010","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":79,"source_line_start":79,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"9. Users can apply for Brain Coin loans.","text_sha256":"c46a81244cc5a5dee09bfb4346827538bcd0f4923900984fd0d86561b6dd47d0","unit_id":"s004","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b011","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":80,"source_line_start":80,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"10. Loan review evidence is assembled from recorded transactional history.","text_sha256":"8c20cd1a36d0ea25e0e166ac7c58c5cce90c153cee13fed7f1fe3046b60dd5ee","unit_id":"s004","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b012","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":81,"source_line_start":81,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"11. Qualification/context information is reviewed separately.","text_sha256":"d186c28015035c8f4f60095f2832ac5fa909b2682abd7e4929fa475d693c0f1f","unit_id":"s004","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b013","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":82,"source_line_start":82,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"12. A mandatory administrator review period prevents immediate automated approval.","text_sha256":"cfd79033ea665a4490128b2c13b5ecd8a32b321611840a40b3c4a5f7738bf524","unit_id":"s004","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b014","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":83,"source_line_start":83,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"13. A human administrator approves or rejects the loan.","text_sha256":"e40fe141106172341dae30830a8eb9bf7bf5b13fd9064d6c1784655b344fb8a2","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b015","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":84,"source_line_start":84,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"14. Approved loans are disbursed through the same ledger abstraction used by other money movement.","text_sha256":"e747c0d42b6fa70352c7abffc4bf84db02159e2f75f0a415b1da1656aaaf898d","unit_id":"s004","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b016","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":85,"source_line_start":85,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"15. Repayments flow back to the system treasury.","text_sha256":"2f93b598fae46733e1f5203e483e29cdd7979787726dd8a6a292170c5ab36b6e","unit_id":"s004","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b017","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":86,"source_line_start":86,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"16. Repaid or defaulted loans become future T-score evidence.","text_sha256":"5008881f7a00ced2517d618ca20621b1522306316cd829e64bc51d14eb3b8ddf","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b018","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":88,"source_line_start":88,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The workflows therefore feed one another.","text_sha256":"06fea188e680a998f000261ac6041d2c5cd097152f9fa7abb6cbd27568f18f1b","unit_id":"s004","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b019","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":90,"source_line_start":90,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Project outcomes and loan outcomes become reliability evidence.","text_sha256":"18eb268a520dbc07a58f32897aa2100ced31bfdb6bf9730e43f7301e3506cfc4","unit_id":"s004","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b020","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":92,"source_line_start":92,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Reliability evidence becomes part of future loan review context.","text_sha256":"299316ceb1d40e78a815da2f1f715ab06a8300cd4db014ee6e270753f122156a","unit_id":"s004","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s004-b021","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Product Concept"],"section_title":"Product Concept","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":94,"source_line_start":94,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Money movement remains ledger-driven throughout those cycles.","text_sha256":"7db1784a4290269ab8707e5cbf5bb4df260602ed00179397f0ecc6dd96423c84","unit_id":"s004","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-115-s085-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s085","section_path":["Product Engineering Evidence"],"section_title":"Product Engineering Evidence","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":963,"source_line_start":963,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"TransAct is more than a numerical accounting demo.","t