INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-115-rd011',115,'TransAct',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3637,11,311,'Section: Loan Application Workflow > Separate Review Channels

A second assessment evaluates the qualification/context statement and purpose.

Those assessments are stored separately in the loan entity and database schema.

The separation preserves provenance between behavioral history and applicant-supplied context.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Configurable Review Provider

AiReviewService defines the review abstraction.

The active repository implementation is HeuristicReviewService.

Its provider name is HEURISTIC_PLACEHOLDER.

The class labels every explanation as a pre-AI heuristic placeholder.

No external model is needed to exercise the workflow.

The abstraction nevertheless allows a later provider to implement the same assessment contract.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Deterministic Payment-History Heuristic

The placeholder payment-history review maps evidence into WEAK, MODERATE, or STRONG.

Defaults or multiple disputes lead to the weak band.

A repaid loan or at least two completed commitments can lead to the strong band.

Other current cases produce a moderate band.

The explanation records the T-score and the input counts used by the heuristic.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Deterministic Qualification Heuristic

The placeholder qualification review counts words in the applicant statement.

Longer statements cross deterministic thresholds into moderate or strong bands.

Its explanation explicitly states that the logic is only a stand-in for exercising the end-to-end process before a real reviewer is configured.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Mandatory Human Review Window

Submitting the application captures the current time.

The application computes adminReviewDueAt by adding the configured review-period duration.

The default is three days.

The resulting state enters administrator review.

An audit event records that review-window entry.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Human Approval Gate

Approval loads the application and verifies that it is in ADMIN_REVIEW.

The operation then checks the current time against adminReviewDueAt.

Approval before the review deadline is rejected.

Once the window has elapsed, an administrator can approve.

The service then transfers Brain Coins from the treasury system account to the applicant account.','["t-score","loan","application","workflow","separate","channels","configurable","provider","deterministic","payment-history","heuristic","qualification","mandatory","human","window","approval","gate"]','["Loan Application Workflow"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-115-s033-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s033","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Separate Review Channels"],"section_title":"Separate Review Channels","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":447,"source_line_start":447,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"A second assessment evaluates the qualification/context statement and purpose.","text_sha256":"daa810ce0fe3091147e3990e999a5fe3851f0379b60b72332c303a6022300cf4","unit_id":"s033","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s033-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s033","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Separate Review Channels"],"section_title":"Separate Review Channels","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":449,"source_line_start":449,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Those assessments are stored separately in the loan entity and database schema.","text_sha256":"18a61bf091fd3e14b3c38576d4913d27d0516b088989be6a5e09a46b17f62fb6","unit_id":"s033","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-115-s033-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s033","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Separate Review Channels"],"section_title":"Separate Review Channels","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":451,"source_line_start":451,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The separation preserves pr