mplate_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Once the window has elapsed, an administrator can approve.","text_sha256":"f9e5bcdbff86d99c6d5a15c86514b057eb2878d49a142e005c3302d68610e923","unit_id":"s038","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-115-s038-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s038","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Human Approval Gate"],"section_title":"Human Approval Gate","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":509,"source_line_start":509,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The service then transfers Brain Coins from the treasury system account to the applicant account.","text_sha256":"9efb8a8a33b0805f490015781c522b2ce1cfa8e68eab34ce33c442733adacbfc","unit_id":"s038","word_count":15}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","document_text_sha256":"35600c65906cd3ee361faf795e3277d3a60555361690940163fc1156474613d7","earliest_source_line":447,"embedding_text_sha256":"ef3427e24a87602d70609e2ee525fc3429e041a6c07b2ad316626d6b46bc9a67","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"3f660ba4e002117fd27f7c7fb9a3802fffe96d0bbda0475df9ebdaed0424ecae","repository_source_line_end":1271,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-115-rd012',115,'TransAct',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3517,7,286,'Section: Loan Application Workflow > Human Approval Gate

The loan receives an approval state and repayment due date.

An audit event explicitly records that a human administrator approved and disbursed the loan.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Human Rejection Gate

Rejection uses the same status and review-deadline gate.

The human administrator supplies or receives default explanatory notes.

The decision is audit logged.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Repayment

An applicant can repay only their own approved outstanding loan.

The repayment amount must be positive.

It cannot exceed outstanding principal.

The money movement goes from the applicant account back to the treasury through the central ledger service.

The loan then updates outstanding amount.

The repayment is audit logged.

Section: Loan Application Workflow > Scheduled Default Detection

An hourly scheduled operation finds approved loans whose repayment due date has passed.

If outstanding amount remains, the loan is marked defaulted.

A system-authored audit event records the transition.

Defaulted loans subsequently become T-score and payment-history evidence.

This creates a closed feedback loop between operational loan state and future reliability assessment.

Section: Recurring Salary / Direct-Deposit Workflow

The repository models recurring payments through SalaryAgreement.

A payer creates an agreement for a recipient developer.

The recipient must have the developer role.

The payer and recipient must differ.

The label is required.

Amount must be positive.

The interval must be between one and 365 days.

A first-payment timestamp in the past is normalized to the current time.

The agreement stores the next payment time.

Section: Recurring Salary / Direct-Deposit Workflow > Scheduler

SalaryService.runDuePayments is annotated with Spring scheduling.

The delay is configurable through transact.salary.scheduler-ms.

Each scheduler pass queries active agreements whose next payment timestamp is due.

Each due agreement is handed to SalaryPaymentProcessor.','["t-score","loan","application","workflow","human","approval","gate","rejection","repayment","scheduled","default","detection","recurring","salary","direct-deposit","scheduler"]','["Loan Application Workflow","Recurring Salary / Direct-Deposit Workflow"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-115-s038-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s038","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Human Approval Gate"],"section_title":"Human Approval Gate","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":511,"source_line_start":511,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The loan receives an approval state and repayment due date.","text_sha256":"fe8dfd0a83d267ac2d75700cbbc548881d34265a2d9de46ae8a027403a0f0567","unit_id":"s038","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-115-s038-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s038","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Human Approval Gate"],"section_title":"Human Approval Gate","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":513,"source_line_start":513,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"An audit event explicitly records that a human administrator approved and disbursed the loan.","text_sha256":"20344f2c7a697fb0d13a182c0927b295ef09b33275a69881c31e9eff0abb575a","unit_id":"s038","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-115-s039-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s039","section_path":["Loan Application Workflow","Human Rejection Gate"],"section_title":"Human Rejection Gate","source_file":"repositories/repo-115-TransAct/README.md","source_line_end":517,"source_line_start":517,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Rejection uses the same status and review-deadline gate.","text_sha256":"56806f