INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-115-rd015',115,'TransAct',NULL,NULL,'direct_evidence','identity_access_security','positive','repository_specific',0.4727,10,82,'Section: Security Baseline

The backend uses Spring Security.

Section: Security Baseline > Stateless HTTP Security

Session creation policy is STATELESS.

The health endpoint is public.

Administrative API paths require the ADMIN role.

Other API requests require authentication.

Section: Security Baseline > Method Security

@EnableMethodSecurity is enabled.

This allows controller or service methods to apply role annotations in addition to path-level authorization.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Security

Spring Security

stateless API configuration

HTTP Basic development authentication

administrator route authorization

method security

