INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-116-rd003',116,'Learning.English',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3597,17,249,'Section: What This Repository Is

Learning.English is a version-controlled English-writing practice corpus.

Its structure is divided into two directories:

WT1/
WT2/

The names and file contents correspond to two families of IELTS-style writing tasks.

WT1 contains Task 1-style analytical writing exercises.

WT2 contains Task 2-style essay exercises.

The repository records both the original prompts and written responses.

Many entries also preserve evaluation feedback beside the attempted response.

This makes the repository more than a folder of finished prose.

It records repeated practice, external assessment, corrections, and comparison between attempts.

Section: Repository Structure > WT1

The first writing-test directory contains five dated/day-numbered Markdown files.

Observed files:

day1.md

day2.md

day3.md

day4.md

day5.md

The files contain data-description prompts and learner responses.

Representative tasks require summarizing charts, tables, regional percentages, speeds, household characteristics, or comparable quantitative information.

The writing objective is therefore concise analytical description rather than open-ended opinion writing.

Section: Repository Structure > WT2

The second writing-test directory contains day files extending through Day 11.

The files hold essay-style prompts and responses.

A representative Day 11 prompt asks the writer to evaluate whether unpaid community service should be compulsory in high-school programs.

The response develops an introduction, opposing viewpoints, examples, and a conclusion.

The file then preserves structured feedback and a corrected-evaluation section.

Section: Task 1 Writing Practice

Task 1 files show a repeated workflow.

A quantitative prompt is preserved.

The data is represented in textual or Markdown-table form.

An answer is written in prose.

Evaluative feedback is stored beneath the answer.','["markdown","structure","task","writing","practice"]','["What This Repository Is","Repository Structure","Task 1 Writing Practice"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-116-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-116-Learning.English/README.md","source_line_end":32,"source_line_start":32,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`Learning.English` is a version-controlled English-writing practice corpus.","text_sha256":"90e7756c81f494b30995ddda443943e37eddc3031f68c2a0b5e8797ceb5d38ed","unit_id":"s003","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-116-s003-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-116-Learning.English/README.md","source_line_end":34,"source_line_start":34,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Its structure is divided into two directories:","text_sha256":"5987bbdbeeecfb6042c05b78a868e5a98dc13492daf19cd0e70576aa52e8e5ea","unit_id":"s003","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-116-s003-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Repository Is"],"section_title":"What This Repository Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-116-Learning.English/README.md","source_line_end":39,"source_line_start":36,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":96,"text":"```text\nWT1/\nWT2/\n```","text_sha256":"e2b49e5aaf5f50171042d1b0d00a024776e01b643e216d082035bbcb3e42317b","unit_id":"s003","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-116-s003-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":