requesting explicit band estimates,

recording criterion tables,

retaining feedback beside the attempted answer,

tracking corrected and uncorrected versions,

using CEFR labels as an additional language-proficiency reference.

Section: Learning Skills Demonstrated > Version-Controlled Learning

organizing practice by test family and day,

keeping Markdown source,

incrementally updating attempts,

retaining a historical record of changes.

Section: Portfolio Significance

This repository provides evidence of deliberate language-learning practice before the later product and research repositories in the portfolio.

The repository also shows an early pattern that reappears in later technical work: preserve the artifact, obtain structured feedback, revise, and keep the evidence trail.

Because evaluator prose is frequently externally generated, the strongest attributable evidence is the learner''s writing, repeated attempts, and deliberate use of structured evaluation to guide improvement.

