ImageProcessing is a compact MATLAB learning repository centered on spatial filtering.

Spatial Filtering/

spatialfilters.mlx

The Live Script is approximately 29 KB in the checked-in repository.

This is direct evidence of an interactive MATLAB notebook-style exercise devoted to spatial-filtering work.

Section: Repository Shape

The repository has a deliberately small topic hierarchy.

The root README establishes the image-processing scope.

The subdirectory names the specific subject.

The .mlx artifact contains the executable/interactive MATLAB work.

Section: MATLAB Live Script Artifact

.mlx is MATLAB''s Live Editor document format.

The checked-in file is a packaged Live Script rather than a plain .m source file.

Inspection of the container identifies MATLAB document/output entries such as:

matlab/document.xml
matlab/output.xml

That packaging is consistent with a Live Editor artifact that can combine executable MATLAB content with formatted explanatory material and captured output.

The portfolio evidence therefore includes use of MATLAB''s notebook-like Live Script workflow.

Section: Spatial Filtering Focus

The repository explicitly names its technical topic Spatial Filtering.

Spatial filtering is part of digital image processing where local pixel neighborhoods are processed to transform an image.

The corpus uses the repository''s explicit topic label as the evidence boundary.

The binary Live Script establishes that the topic was exercised interactively in MATLAB.

Specific filter kernels or mathematical operations are not inferred solely from the filename.

Section: Learning Workflow

The repository structure reflects topic-oriented technical study.

The overall subject is separated at the root.

A focused subtopic receives its own directory.

The practical work is placed in a Live Script.

This structure supports combining explanation, executable code, and visual output in one MATLAB learning artifact.

