":"Packet Index Extraction","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":236,"source_line_start":236,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It scans the message for the first `#` and extracts everything after that marker.","text_sha256":"2f210d993efbd61bb3fcee8b4f3817d43dfc1f1ce5e1c664c012928fb58773ff","unit_id":"s017","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-120-s017-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Packet Index Extraction"],"section_title":"Packet Index Extraction","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":238,"source_line_start":238,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is intentionally lightweight, but it gives the experiment a deterministic way to associate received messages with sender sequence numbers.","text_sha256":"35f44b65626475482291cbaad658398e51f54978cfdd126d44a2fcf239e13279","unit_id":"s017","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-120-s017-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Packet Index Extraction"],"section_title":"Packet Index Extraction","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":240,"source_line_start":240,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Later receiver variants use the parsed sequence number when recording simulated packet losses.","text_sha256":"71dbcca9f9a26cfe76a606971f4486555828d64cd92cbf4a748418914f50ae78","unit_id":"s017","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-120-s019-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s019","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Noise injection"],"section_title":"Noise injection","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":246,"source_line_start":246,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`AGWN/receiver.m` and the improved-readability AWGN variant convert each received datagram from `uint8` to `double` and invoke MATLAB''s:","text_sha256":"df4b606f478a9040b8ad2b34da0cb02ac7e97659ca0fa6a2fe10df38bf7d16a0","unit_id":"s019","word_count":17},{"block_id":"repo-120-s019-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s019","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Noise injection"],"section_title":"Noise injection","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":250,"source_line_start":248,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":96,"text":"```matlab\nawgn(dataDouble, snr, ''measured'')\n```","text_sha256":"3d3d7aa47896696615a30eab19327ca2345377a0d94295de764d5609db42db48","unit_id":"s019","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-120-s019-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Noise injection"],"section_title":"Noise injection","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":252,"source_line_start":252,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The code therefore uses MATLAB communications tooling to perturb the received byte values with additive white Gaussian noise.","text_sha256":"a899e385537dda8b611a04a9d475288dd5a4c598354d59c6e9215196245bd9d0","unit_id":"s019","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-120-s020-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Randomized SNR"],"section_title":"Randomized SNR","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":256,"source_line_start":256,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"For each processed datagram, the receiver samples:","text_sha256":"3e84b74b06cf4b4778c229abcbb3721a8d5fa6c4938ea22d1b244a755b91ec58","unit_id":"s020","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-120-s020-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Randomized SNR"],"section_title":"Randomized SNR","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":260,"source_line_start":258,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"```text\nSNR = 20 + 2 * randn\n```","text_sha256":"770383abd6e91b24e7438fcc5251307fe6ec392aabc08f7514c599359fbdf661","unit_id":"s020","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-120-s020-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["AWGN Receiver Experiment","Randomized SNR"],"section_title":"Randomized SNR","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":262,"source_line_start":262,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"so the impairment condition varies around a 20 dB mean with a 2 dB standard-deviation term.","text_sha256":"aa0756814553d545c95cf5dec1220158b24be6361b63cb8b0223f97c4baa8534","unit_id":"s020","word_count":16}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","document_text_sha256":"02581e08b58a373a64e3b8ca7dc49481e751e621cefb02b2ca1ee60a626f6a87","earliest_source_line":201,"embedding_text_sha256":"593f5049fc52df5b82aaf2a6f9b8efeafb1bfc7e31fe71dedeb1d9f1236f8bd2","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"280c87940f942f4a3f2d4a98614402b9512c86d73879a5a555742c98fb6acb7e","repository_source_line_end":519,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-120-rd005',120,'Matlab-Experiments',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3533,7,275,'Section: AWGN Receiver Experiment > Randomized SNR

This produces packet-by-packet variation rather than one constant channel condition.

Section: AWGN Receiver Experiment > Re-quantization

After noise is applied, the altered values are:

rounded;

clipped to the valid byte interval 0..255;

converted back to uint8.

The receiver can therefore compare the noisy quantized payload against the original datagram bytes.

Section: AWGN Receiver Experiment > Byte error-rate calculation

The code counts positions where:

noisyDataRounded ~= originalData

and divides by the total number of bytes.

The resulting errorRate is a byte-level corruption proportion for that simulated noise realization.

Section: AWGN Receiver Experiment > Error rate to packet-drop probability

The AGWN version scales the measured error rate and compares it with a random sample to decide whether to drop the packet from later processing.

This creates a stochastic packet-loss layer driven by the observed corruption level.

The improved-readability variant retains this mechanism while using a smaller scaling factor.

That is evidence of iterative calibration of the synthetic impairment model.

Section: Receiver-Specific Loss Tracking

The AWGN variants maintain separate lost-packet arrays for receiver instances.

When a simulated drop occurs, the code:

parses the original packet index;

associates the loss with the current receiver ID;

appends the index to that receiver''s loss list;

logs SNR and error rate;

skips normal packet processing for that datagram.

This preserves which sequence numbers were considered lost rather than recording only an aggregate count.

Section: Cleanup-Time Experiment Reporting

The AWGN receivers register an onCleanup callback.

This means termination of the long-running receiver triggers final experiment reporting.

The improved-readability version reports, for the active receiver:

total packets processed;

total packets lost;

