INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-120-rd007',120,'Matlab-Experiments',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3685,12,306,'Section: Technical Stack > udpport

The code exercises:

IPv4 datagram mode;

broadcast transmission;

shared local-port reception;

datagram callbacks;

reading buffered datagrams.

Section: Technical Stack > Communications Toolbox awgn

The AWGN variants use MATLAB''s awgn function with measured signal power.

Its role is specifically to perturb received byte-valued data for the impairment experiment.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Explicit experiment parameters

The sender exposes packet count, payload size, send interval, destination port, and destination address as named values.

The AWGN receiver similarly exposes the SNR model and drop scaling in source.

This keeps the important experiment conditions inspectable.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Sequence-aware instrumentation

Packet indexes survive from sender generation into receiver logging and loss tracking.

That makes individual packet outcomes traceable.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Variant preservation

Rather than replacing every prior experiment, the repository preserves multiple receiver variants.

For a learning/experimental repository, this helps retain how the test logic changed across iterations.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Termination hooks

onCleanup is used to surface final reliability statistics when a receiver is interrupted.

This is a practical lifecycle mechanism for an otherwise indefinite callback-driven process.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Communications experimentation

The repository materially uses:

SNR;

AWGN;

byte corruption comparison;

stochastic drop modeling;

packet error rate.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Experiment design

The sender controls offered traffic characteristics while receiver variants control observation and impairment behavior.

This separation supports repeatable changes to one side of the experiment without rewriting the other.

Section: Portfolio Significance

Within the portfolio, Matlab-Experiments is evidence of using MATLAB outside purely offline numerical analysis.

The repository applies MATLAB to live socket behavior, packet timing, multiple listener instances, and communications impairment simulation.

It also demonstrates a recurring engineering pattern in the portfolio: build a small traffic/control mechanism, observe its behavior with explicit metrics, then add controlled adverse conditions to study reliability.','["matlab","ipv4","awgn","technical","stack","udpport","communications","toolbox","engineering","practices","evidenced","experiment","parameters","sequence-aware","instrumentation","variant","preservation","termination","hooks","skills","demonstrated","experimentation","design","portfolio"]','["Technical Stack","Engineering Practices Evidenced","Skills Demonstrated","Portfolio Significance"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-120-s034-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s034","section_path":["Technical Stack","`udpport`"],"section_title":"`udpport`","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":401,"source_line_start":401,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The code exercises:","text_sha256":"3284689983a9d57023cc4c218cf4ebe3bbcda12efc5afbbbe321c6be12c0cfd2","unit_id":"s034","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-120-s034-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s034","section_path":["Technical Stack","`udpport`"],"section_title":"`udpport`","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":403,"source_line_start":403,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- IPv4 datagram mode;","text_sha256":"2df8f048c4dbe8431df01020acd22a38caf394641e201a2ec96c9a14c30332da","unit_id":"s034","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-120-s034-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s034","section_path":["Technical Stack","`udpport`"],"section_title":"`udpport`","source_file":"repositories/repo-120-Matlab-Experiments/README.md","source_line_end":404,"source_line_start":404,"specificity_score":0.