INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-121-rd002',121,'NetSeer',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3505,9,258,'Section: What This Project Is

NetSeer is a lightweight, browser-executed analysis tool for turning raw network-performance logs into readable metrics, smoothed time-series plots, and portable outputs.

They parse the text locally, derive numerical measurements, and present the result through interactive Chart.js visualizations.

The project therefore avoids an ingestion server or database and instead treats the browser as a small analysis workstation:

Section: Main Network Log Processor

index.html is titled Network Log Processor.

Its expected input format is represented directly in the interface:

The page provides:

a multiline log-input area;

processing status messages;

separate upload and download views;

an averaging-window control;

chart color selection;

editable chart title;

chart-to-clipboard output;

PNG chart output;

processed CSV output.

The whole pipeline runs client side.

Section: Log Parsing > Regular-expression extraction

The parser matches:

full date and time;

HH:MM:SS;

download bytes per second;

upload bytes per second.

It iterates through all regex matches in the pasted content and turns each line into a structured JavaScript object.

Section: Log Parsing > Explicit field correction

A repository-specific rule intentionally swaps the two speed fields:

The source comments explicitly identify this as a requirement.

This is significant because the application is not merely graphing source text verbatim; it contains domain-specific normalization logic for the format being analyzed.

Section: Time Normalization

The first valid entry becomes the temporal reference point.

parseTimeToSeconds converts HH:MM:SS into seconds.

For every record, the application computes:

The chart can therefore use experiment-relative elapsed time rather than absolute wall-clock labels.

This is well suited to comparing network runs that start at different times.','["html","javascript","network","processor","parsing","regular-expression","extraction","field","correction","time","normalization"]','["What This Project Is","Main Network Log Processor","Log Parsing","Time Normalization"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-121-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-121-NetSeer/README.md","source_line_end":18,"source_line_start":18,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`NetSeer` is a lightweight, browser-executed analysis tool for turning raw network-performance logs into readable metrics, smoothed time-series plots, and portable outputs.","text_sha256":"21d2ea74ad34e25c4d6b3afdd22fb4431942948818297f3ea76c2655485e6a3c","unit_id":"s002","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-121-s002-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-121-NetSeer/README.md","source_line_end":29,"source_line_start":29,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"They parse the text locally, derive numerical measurements, and present the result through interactive Chart.js visualizations.","text_sha256":"29e6028e4c67e638f3bdbb28a0bc35a3a975e8da782bba44a318e095f5abe1e7","unit_id":"s002","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-121-s002-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-121-NetSeer/README.md","source_line_end":31,"source_line_start":31,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequenc