INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-122-rd002',122,'ME-780-Project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3387,14,272,'Section: What This Project Is

ME-780-Project is a focused control-engineering repository that explores how a simulated mobile manipulator can move between task locations while progressively incorporating stability, obstacle safety, constrained optimization, and explicit escape behavior.

The inspected source contains concrete mathematical control laws, barrier constraints, QP construction, geometric path checks, fallback logic, and a pickup/drop-off mission executed against a mobile-manipulator unicycle simulator.

Section: Repository Structure

The source tree is compact:

Despite the small file count, the control files contain substantial experiment logic.

The commit history also preserves a clear evolution from an initial simulation file toward progressively richer combined CLF/CBF strategies.

Section: Simulation Interface

The controllers deliberately operate through a narrow simulator surface.

The source repeatedly uses:

get_poses()
set_mobile_base_speed_and_gripper_power()

The control code therefore computes action externally and sends:

linear base speed;

angular base speed;

gripper power.

This creates a useful separation:

Section: Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking

CLF.py implements the simplest repository variant.

Section: Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking > Pose and goal geometry

The controller reads:

x, y, theta

from the robot base pose.

For goal position (gx, gy), it computes:

dx;

dy;

Euclidean distance rho;

goal bearing;

heading error alpha.

The heading error is normalized through a wrap helper into the conventional angular interval.

Section: Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking > Linear control command

The desired forward velocity is:

v = k_rho * rho * cos(alpha)

This scales translation with goal distance while suppressing forward motion when the robot is badly misaligned with the goal.

Section: Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking > Angular control command

The rotational command is:

w = k_alpha * alpha

which drives heading error toward zero.','["structure","simulation","interface","control","lyapunov","function","goal","seeking","pose","geometry","linear","command","angular"]','["What This Project Is","Repository Structure","Simulation Interface","Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-122-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":18,"source_line_start":18,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`ME-780-Project` is a focused control-engineering repository that explores how a simulated mobile manipulator can move between task locations while progressively incorporating stability, obstacle safety, constrained optimization, and explicit escape behavior.","text_sha256":"591d7c04e514051716a4e3a603d5888f0911f762d1c3d192b62e07b31a2dd35b","unit_id":"s002","word_count":30},{"block_id":"repo-122-s002-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":44,"source_line_start":44,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The inspected source contains concrete mathematical control laws, barrier constraints, QP construction, geometric path checks, fallback logic, and a pickup/drop-off mission executed against a mobile-manipulator unicycle simulator.","text_sha256":"5374b88c758cdeb3a91ce06aae2bb530c7fd8a50a5db1d088fa4c4ad72f5762b","unit_id":"s002","word_count":27},{"block_id":"repo-122-s004-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s004","section_path":["Repository Structure"],"section_title"