INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-122-rd004',122,'ME-780-Project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3691,13,284,'Section: Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking > Control saturation

Both commands are clipped to configured bounds:

v_max = 0.08
w_max = 6.0

This gives the control law explicit actuator-like limits.

Section: CLF Pickup and Drop-Off Mission

The CLF.py main routine creates a mission containing:

initial robot pose;

pickup location;

drop-off location;

obstacle locations;

robot geometry parameters.

The pure CLF variant drives toward pickup until a configured stop distance is reached.

It then actuates the gripper positively for approximately one second.

After that it drives toward drop-off and actuates the gripper negatively to release.

This makes the control law part of a complete simulated manipulation sequence:

rather than only an isolated formula.

Section: Control Barrier Function Integration

CBF.py extends the goal-seeking behavior with obstacle constraints.

Section: Control Barrier Function Integration > Obstacle state

Obstacle locations are obtained from the simulator state.

The controller repeatedly evaluates distance from the robot to each obstacle.

Section: Control Barrier Function Integration > Barrier value

For an obstacle distance d and safety radius r, the source forms a squared-distance barrier of the form:

h(x) = d^2 - r^2

Positive values correspond to state outside the safety boundary.

Section: CLF-CBF Quadratic Program

The main combined controller uses CVXOPT to solve a quadratic program.

Section: CLF-CBF Quadratic Program > Desired control as optimization reference

The CLF produces nominal commands:

v_des
w_des

The QP is then structured to remain near these desired commands while respecting safety constraints.

Section: CLF-CBF Quadratic Program > Objective

The optimization penalizes deviation from desired CLF behavior and weights slack.

In the linear-backup variant, the documented objective is effectively:

This captures the central architecture:

Section: Velocity Constraints

The QP explicitly adds bounds for:

v <= v_max;

v >= -v_max;','["cvxopt","control","lyapunov","function","goal","seeking","saturation","pickup","drop-off","mission","barrier","integration","obstacle","state","value","clf-cbf","quadratic","program","desired","optimization","reference","objective","velocity","constraints"]','["Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking","CLF Pickup and Drop-Off Mission","Control Barrier Function Integration","CLF-CBF Quadratic Program","Velocity Constraints"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-122-s010-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking","Control saturation"],"section_title":"Control saturation","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":157,"source_line_start":157,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Both commands are clipped to configured bounds:","text_sha256":"45d82b37498b12308fca8c4893af57b07cb851b081a6f7918b30945dacec7814","unit_id":"s010","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-122-s010-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking","Control saturation"],"section_title":"Control saturation","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":162,"source_line_start":159,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"```text\nv_max = 0.08\nw_max = 6.0\n```","text_sha256":"114438407a7b24f394a1924aa777437fe0aca0a713fdda02c11a87602f7fb2e5","unit_id":"s010","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-122-s010-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Control Lyapunov Function Goal Seeking","Control saturation"],"section_title":"Control saturation","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":164,"source_line_start":164,"specificity_score":0.34,"template