INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-122-rd009',122,'ME-780-Project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3426,2,298,'Section: Candidate Escape Search

obstacle-proximity cost.

Only candidates passing both safety checks are eligible for selection.

Section: Obstacle Cost

The final variant computes an inverse-distance obstacle cost at the candidate endpoint.

Nearby obstacles contribute more cost than distant obstacles.

The candidate objective combines:

This prevents escape selection from considering only immediate collision freedom while ignoring the relative quality of the resulting state.

Section: Escape Execution

Once a safe candidate angle is selected, escape_to_safety:

rotates toward the selected heading;

continually rechecks rotation safety;

stops rotation when the heading error is small;

drives forward along the escape heading;

repeatedly rechecks the forward path;

halts if an unexpected obstacle invalidates the route.

The safety plan is therefore revalidated during execution rather than trusted blindly after one initial check.

Section: Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior

If no safe escape direction is found, the code sends zero base and gripper command and returns failure.

If a newly observed obstacle invalidates the chosen rotation or linear path, the controller similarly halts.

This is concrete fail-closed behavior in the simulated safety-control workflow.

Section: QP and Backup Separation

The final controller uses two modes with different purposes:

Section: QP and Backup Separation > Normal region

Use CLF-CBF QP to progress toward the target while satisfying barrier constraints.

Section: QP and Backup Separation > Danger region

Suspend ordinary progress optimization and execute a geometric escape routine.

This hybrid strategy is one of the repository''s most distinctive engineering decisions.

It recognizes that a controller optimized for normal progress can benefit from a separately understandable recovery mode near unsafe geometry.

Section: Gripper-Aware Goal Checking

The final navigation routine calculates gripper position from base pose and front offset.

Goal distance is measured from the gripper to the target.

This aligns navigation termination with the manipulation endpoint rather than only the base center.','["candidate","escape","search","obstacle","cost","execution","fail-closed","emergency","behavior","backup","separation","normal","region","danger","gripper-aware","goal","checking"]','["Candidate Escape Search","Obstacle Cost","Escape Execution","Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior","QP and Backup Separation","Gripper-Aware Goal Checking"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-122-s029-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s029","section_path":["Candidate Escape Search"],"section_title":"Candidate Escape Search","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":392,"source_line_start":392,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- obstacle-proximity cost.","text_sha256":"1179f0390deb6066a74c5a933cc63f8d2b20d7b2a17fd12fb7ffa72a7f129a88","unit_id":"s029","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-122-s029-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s029","section_path":["Candidate Escape Search"],"section_title":"Candidate Escape Search","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":394,"source_line_start":394,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Only candidates passing both safety checks are eligible for selection.","text_sha256":"948d45449f5a1533fec39961176f0fe9f0ed09df26a10d5c2f3d636388fa991d","unit_id":"s029","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-122-s030-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s030","section_path":["Obstacle Cost"],"section_title":"Obstacle Cost","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":398,"source_line_start":398,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The final variant computes an inverse-distance obstacle cost at the candidate endpoint.","text_sha256":"e6e8ef5041e2ebe2d88457939dc6245329d5cce324943160c6481fc833902efb","unit_id":"s030","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-122-s030-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s030","section_path":["Obstacle Cost"],"section_title":"Obstacle Cost","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":400,"source_line_start":400,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Nearby obstacles contribute more cost than distant obstacles.","text_sha256":"fc67e1936525ef949f904eb714ea03c95e99267bf0b82898fec00382823dec6d","unit_id":"s030","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-122-s030-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s030","section_path":["Obstacle Cost"],"section_title":"Obstacle Cost","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":402,"source_line_start":402,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The candidate objective combines:","text_sha256":"1ded646fdefca4c1740cc66ae40080465c6af264813e6eb1415757c0c7d69c04","unit_id":"s030","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-122-s030-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s030","section_path":["Obstacle Cost"],"section_title":"Obstacle Cost","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":410,"source_line_start":410,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This prevents escape selection from considering only immediate collision freedom while ignoring the relative quality of the resulting state.","text_sha256":"41c2d6132a804a240520bd35f3639ee2fadf4c2f211d5bf85de12a0ac7ca7331","unit_id":"s030","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":414,"source_line_start":414,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Once a safe candidate angle is selected, `escape_to_safety`:","text_sha256":"ea0cdd9693f41e44717c16b65fa33058873595798938072dbc8e807d41d25d0d","unit_id":"s031","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":416,"source_line_start":416,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"1. rotates toward the selected heading;","text_sha256":"fff71ebbe8119992ad099bdacfe64e799067ff249a41e1c69171438085494e42","unit_id":"s031","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":417,"source_line_start":417,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"2. continually rechecks rotation safety;","text_sha256":"c3b8128fc98acddfedae5f02c7863b6daf0cfcd16d8f7c7842c87da62f1f56cb","unit_id":"s031","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":418,"source_line_start":418,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"3. stops rotation when the heading error is small;","text_sha256":"2d21f18975764c17400cf631f71ed46149a9580b889c65142f19eeac44541724","unit_id":"s031","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":419,"source_line_start":419,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"4. drives forward along the escape heading;","text_sha256":"2582a2e5dc94a2234cf9e62ccf5f2e95135eae9f4eac55b98267e2060aa2ea77","unit_id":"s031","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":420,"source_line_start":420,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"5. repeatedly rechecks the forward path;","text_sha256":"99f2b1830a63b3254d1cad869e81b7c2ecd247e12f977a677f0dcf9e1e3edf25","unit_id":"s031","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":421,"source_line_start":421,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"6. halts if an unexpected obstacle invalidates the route.","text_sha256":"fea085200bcad58d33b057fb12288624c428097c65bd8ca866b1259f46c9cd94","unit_id":"s031","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-122-s031-b008","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["Escape Execution"],"section_title":"Escape Execution","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":423,"source_line_start":423,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The safety plan is therefore revalidated during execution rather than trusted blindly after one initial check.","text_sha256":"874158c4c460cff17271b7be6a7ae14a029c682ac755167acbd17e8327bdef1c","unit_id":"s031","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-122-s032-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s032","section_path":["Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior"],"section_title":"Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":427,"source_line_start":427,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"If no safe escape direction is found, the code sends zero base and gripper command and returns failure.","text_sha256":"5bd51fbf6b1d93cc30b069b2e53b6188361b1ce5d027213de422387049787b91","unit_id":"s032","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-122-s032-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s032","section_path":["Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior"],"section_title":"Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":429,"source_line_start":429,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"If a newly observed obstacle invalidates the chosen rotation or linear path, the controller similarly halts.","text_sha256":"ed4581d44c3fa8765e9f6b58cc12099c0b17bc871e95161a3388ee0b4ec527f1","unit_id":"s032","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-122-s032-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s032","section_path":["Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior"],"section_title":"Fail-Closed Emergency Behavior","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":431,"source_line_start":431,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is concrete fail-closed behavior in the simulated safety-control workflow.","text_sha256":"f7a085117ce7a0e1d5d6e24114890c59492ab306875b640b4bdc6c9d5ee20430","unit_id":"s032","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-122-s033-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s033","section_path":["QP and Backup Separation"],"section_title":"QP and Backup Separation","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":435,"source_line_start":435,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The final controller uses two modes with different purposes:","text_sha256":"0f57ea23a01af97f1122d214bc0a9e9edfad193980c2b7efcc453632be2e8f0a","unit_id":"s033","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-122-s034-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s034","section_path":["QP and Backup Separation","Normal region"],"section_title":"Normal region","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":439,"source_line_start":439,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Use CLF-CBF QP to progress toward the target while satisfying barrier constraints.","text_sha256":"6f646cb3e58e467d3643236180be71aebf8c57899a47fcf154ea52dd9a24c3a4","unit_id":"s034","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-122-s035-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s035","section_path":["QP and Backup Separation","Danger region"],"section_title":"Danger region","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":443,"source_line_start":443,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Suspend ordinary progress optimization and execute a geometric escape routine.","text_sha256":"e93124f5bfb32252ed150eac96e47242de08b504da635ba260a29102fbf81a8b","unit_id":"s035","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-122-s035-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s035","section_path":["QP and Backup Separation","Danger region"],"section_title":"Danger region","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":445,"source_line_start":445,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This hybrid strategy is one of the repository''s most distinctive engineering decisions.","text_sha256":"18fffbe55ec546dfd4a9b51f1d0505844121afffd45cd887ddb53c015092940f","unit_id":"s035","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-122-s035-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s035","section_path":["QP and Backup Separation","Danger region"],"section_title":"Danger region","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":447,"source_line_start":447,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It recognizes that a controller optimized for normal progress can benefit from a separately understandable recovery mode near unsafe geometry.","text_sha256":"eccc53f7bcde336f913758b185efae0cba189379a636aa0692cca40e112bb484","unit_id":"s035","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-122-s036-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s036","section_path":["Gripper-Aware Goal Checking"],"section_title":"Gripper-Aware Goal Checking","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":451,"source_line_start":451,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The final navigation routine calculates gripper position from base pose and front offset.","text_sha256":"8924c98dac34c91bdf0847174b399fe6333b88e9fd983faf190b2a048d8fd1f2","unit_id":"s036","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-122-s036-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s036","section_path":["Gripper-Aware Goal Checking"],"section_title":"Gripper-Aware Goal Checking","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":453,"source_line_start":453,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Goal distance is measured from the gripper to the target.","text_sha256":"0f83625fdcd259bcf960dca344956a91eebc20735ef47195f352d9608fd3f943","unit_id":"s036","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-122-s036-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s036","section_path":["Gripper-Aware Goal Checking"],"section_title":"Gripper-Aware Goal Checking","source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","source_line_end":455,"source_line_start":455,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This aligns navigation termination with the manipulation endpoint rather than only the base center.","text_sha256":"7ee49d56cf920f78e1f84f77d992d226ee936ae2f388782f4424aa621599dc1e","unit_id":"s036","word_count":14}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-122-ME-780-Project/README.md","document_text_sha256":"8a957ba2a6ab056f116c12230a2f8cf0c32e4578abc064f83db4b233ed8f6db2","earliest_source_line":392,"embedding_text_sha256":"151e8dc7b0e07432c54a6ced34dc738915f28b0cd145aedd81dfca7b09140453","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"5e2915f20a9cd0d9796819c2b4d9cd13da66c8e9dde2d7687608bc5a37b358e3","repository_source_line_end":657,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-122-rd010',122,'ME-780-Project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3826,15,292,'Section: Numerical Optimization Stack > NumPy

NumPy supports:

vector/matrix construction;

angle-scan generation;

distance calculations;

QP matrix preparation.

Section: Numerical Optimization Stack > CVXOPT

CVXOPT provides the quadratic-programming solver.

The code converts objective and constraint arrays into CVXOPT matrices and invokes:

solvers.qp(...)

Solver progress output is disabled to keep the experiment log focused on application diagnostics.

Section: Control-System Diagnostics

The source contains extensive runtime logging.

The final variant reports:

candidate escape angles;

blocked rotation arcs;

blocked paths;

target cost;

obstacle cost;

combined cost;

selected escape angle;

QP desired versus optimized controls;

slack.

These diagnostics make the controller''s decision process inspectable during simulation.

Section: Evolution of the Control Strategy

The commit history provides a useful conceptual progression.

Section: Evolution of the Control Strategy > Stage 1: simulation / CBF experiment

The initial simulation source was created and then renamed to CBF.py.

Section: Evolution of the Control Strategy > Stage 2: explicit CLF baseline

CLF.py was added as a pure goal-seeking baseline.

This isolates what the navigation behavior looks like without obstacle handling.

Section: Evolution of the Control Strategy > Stage 4: combined CLF-CBF without QP

The repository preserved an explicitly named alternative:

CLF-CBF-No QP - Inefficient

This records experimentation with a non-QP integration path.

Section: Evolution of the Control Strategy > Stage 5: QP plus linear backup

The final commit adds CLF-CBF-QPwithLinearBackup.

The architecture combines optimization-driven normal motion with explicit sampled geometric escape behavior.

The repository therefore documents reasoning through multiple controller organizations rather than presenting one unexplained final algorithm.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Parameterized control behavior

Important values such as gains, safety radius, margins, velocity bounds, scan count, slack weight, and sample counts are parameters rather than hidden constants throughout the implementation.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Geometric reasoning

