INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-123-rd005',123,'Apple-Project',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','deployment_operations','positive','interpretive',0.3461,3,154,'Section: FTP Operations Represented

The STFTPNetwork public interface represented in the repository covers several FTP workflows.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Connection

The documented API accepts:

FTP URL;

username;

password;

completion handler.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Remote listing / query

The query API returns an array of results through an asynchronous success handler.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Directory creation

A create call supports creating a remote folder with success/failure handlers.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Removal

The remove call handles files or folders and returns an STFTP error code on failure.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Download

The download interface exposes:

progress bytes completed;

progress bytes total;

downloaded NSData;

success/failure callbacks.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Upload

The upload interface similarly exposes byte-progress reporting and success/failure callbacks.

Section: FTP Operations Represented > Disconnect

The library includes an explicit disconnect operation.

