INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-126-rd003',126,'SedraFTPVariant',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3406,15,231,'Section: What This Project Is

SedraFTPVariant turns FTP transfer from a manual networking operation into a controlled experiment workload.

The server side provides FTP service and synthetic/generated content that can be consumed repeatedly without depending on a finite static test file.

The repository also contains an iOS client implementation whose UI and automation logic mirror the experiment-oriented workflow.

It is a repeatability harness for inducing network traffic under controlled timing and observing transfer behavior.

Section: Evolution From the Initial Design Specification

The root README records a concrete control concept.

It describes a network-scanning controller that:

scans a local subnet,

identifies responsive hosts,

represents clients in a GUI,

sends START_DOWNLOAD over UDP,

listens for completion/failure messages,

times the transaction,

returns each client to a ready state after completion.

The implemented repository develops the same broader idea of a control plane around network workloads.

The checked-in Python client uses explicit UDP commands:

START_DOWNLOAD,

STOP_DOWNLOAD,

START_AUTOTESTS,

STOP_AUTOTESTS.

It also has a UDP listener and a separate FTP data path.

That is a meaningful separation:

The control channel coordinates the experiment while FTP carries the actual bulk data.

Section: Python Desktop Client

Client/client.py is a substantial Python 3 GUI application.

Its module description identifies it as:

a Tkinter FTP client,

an automated-test runner,

a UDP-controlled application.

Section: Python Desktop Client > Configurable FTP Parameters

The client exposes configuration for:

FTP host,

FTP port,

username,

password,','["python","tkinter","evolution","from","initial","design","specification","desktop","client","configurable","parameters"]','["What This Project Is","Evolution From the Initial Design Specification","Python Desktop Client"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-126-s003-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":40,"source_line_start":40,"specificity_score":0.28,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`SedraFTPVariant` turns FTP transfer from a manual networking operation into a controlled experiment workload.","text_sha256":"52fe59030075b049e051e367e62508701db0eb5f23ca35046ac5551c3f115596","unit_id":"s003","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-126-s003-b012","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":55,"source_line_start":55,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The server side provides FTP service and synthetic/generated content that can be consumed repeatedly without depending on a finite static test file.","text_sha256":"050c16068fbb17fcc0631f5ceeeb118734417cd899baed62ac9c17b51f66b570","unit_id":"s003","word_count":22},{"block_id":"repo-126-s003-b013","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"methodology_or_interpretive","section_id":"s003","section_path":["What This Project Is"],"section_title":"What This Project Is","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":57,"source_line_start":57,"specificity_score":0.24,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository also contains an iOS client implementation whose UI and 