INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-126-rd005',126,'SedraFTPVariant',NULL,NULL,'chronology','chronology_growth','positive','repository_specific',0.3611,4,86,'Section: Python Desktop Client > Download Lifecycle

FTPDownloader.download() implements the transfer lifecycle.

The sequence is:

connect to the FTP server,

log in,

attempt to determine the remote file size,

begin binary retrieval,

write incoming chunks to a temporary .part file,

update byte-level progress,

atomically replace the final path when successful,

remove a partial file on failure.

The final rename is performed through os.replace.

