INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-126-rd007',126,'SedraFTPVariant',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3513,4,197,'Section: Automated Repetition

30,

60 seconds.

This is direct evidence of designing for repeated trials rather than single manual transfers.

Section: iOS Experiment Client

Client/main.m contains a repository-specific UIKit FTP experiment application.

It imports WhiteRaccoon as the FTP transport but builds experiment behavior around it.

Section: iOS Experiment Client > iOS Experiment UI

The source creates controls programmatically for:

status indicator,

test count,

separation interval,

FTP host,

username,

password,

start/stop automated tests,

manual download,

progress.

The client therefore does not depend only on a storyboard for its experimental interface.

Section: iOS Experiment Client > Automated Trial State

The Objective-C client tracks:

total tests,

tests started,

tests completed,

successful tests,

automation-running state,

separation interval,

current test number.

Preset choices include:

10,

20,

50,

100 trials,

30-second or 60-second separation.

Section: iOS Experiment Client > Milestone Logging

The iOS client creates a timestamped milestone log file for an automated run.

It:

generates the output filename,

writes a header,

writes an immediate initialization record,

uses a serial dispatch queue for file operations,

records the path and current test state.

This is concrete evidence of trying to make repeated mobile transfer experiments traceable rather than relying only on transient UI state.','["objective-c","uikit","automated","repetition","experiment","client","trial","state","milestone","logging"]','["Automated Repetition","iOS Experiment Client"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-126-s017-b018","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Automated Repetition"],"section_title":"Automated Repetition","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":281,"source_line_start":281,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- 30,","text_sha256":"02cb96a5077d70b7dc0eac7fd256eae88706c4405cc53f05027683a968766e2c","unit_id":"s017","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-126-s017-b019","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Automated Repetition"],"section_title":"Automated Repetition","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":282,"source_line_start":282,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- 60 seconds.","text_sha256":"c662c8fbeb17e0023c5ae4c715e6254d7cc290ee66ee5485dfa374c8fa5dd096","unit_id":"s017","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-126-s017-b020","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Automated Repetition"],"section_title":"Automated Repetition","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":284,"source_line_start":284,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is direct evidence of designing for repeated trials rather than single manual transfers.","text_sha256":"e442bab9112033e7a6162f17e09b883a8c576375308a412ce2392d53cad1b960","unit_id":"s017","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-126-s018-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2