INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-126-rd008',126,'SedraFTPVariant',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3533,15,281,'Section: iOS Experiment Client > iOS UDP Listener

The Objective-C source also declares:

a UDP socket,

a dispatch queue,

a dispatch source.

This extends the same remote-control experiment architecture into the native iOS client.

Section: Synthetic FTP Server

Server/server.py uses pyftpdlib.

Section: Synthetic FTP Server > Virtual Generated Files

The server defines InfiniteFile, a file-like object that generates data as it is read.

Generated chunks include a counter/timestamp and are padded to the requested size.

The file can therefore continue producing data without storing a correspondingly large object on disk.

Section: Synthetic FTP Server > Virtual Filesystem

VirtualFS extends AbstractedFS.

It advertises virtual paths including:

/infinite.txt,
/stream.dat.

It overrides filesystem behavior such as:

open,

stat,

isfile,

listdir,

lexists.

For virtual paths, the server returns generated data and synthetic metadata.

Section: Synthetic FTP Server > Why This Matters Experimentally

A synthetic effectively unbounded source is useful for throughput work because the server can maintain transfer pressure without preparing or repeatedly replacing a huge static file.

The workload becomes:

Section: Synthetic FTP Server > FTP Server Configuration

The service binds to:

0.0.0.0,
TCP port 2121.

The source configures multiple test users with read/list permissions.

That multi-user setup aligns with a laboratory environment where several clients can be assigned distinct credentials.

Section: External Networking Components > WhiteRaccoon

WhiteRaccoon provides the Objective-C FTP request/stream implementation.

It remains externally attributed to Valentin Radu.

Its capabilities include download, upload, delete, directory creation/listing, queues, stream callbacks, and FTP error mapping.

Those are library capabilities available to the project, not original design claims for this repository.

Section: External Networking Components > Apple SimplePing

SimplePing is explicitly Apple''s sample implementation.

It wraps BSD-socket ICMP behavior and supports IPv4/IPv6 ping operation.','["objective-c","pyftpdlib","experiment","client","listener","synthetic","server","virtual","generated","files","filesystem","matters","experimentally","configuration","external","networking","components","whiteraccoon","apple","simpleping"]','["iOS Experiment Client","Synthetic FTP Server","External Networking Components"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-126-s022-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["iOS Experiment Client","iOS UDP Listener"],"section_title":"iOS UDP Listener","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":344,"source_line_start":344,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The Objective-C source also declares:","text_sha256":"8ba345b161d23919923b715726b5bae1386b8438a184e0f9af7ee39dbc1d51ee","unit_id":"s022","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-126-s022-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["iOS Experiment Client","iOS UDP Listener"],"section_title":"iOS UDP Listener","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":346,"source_line_start":346,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- a UDP socket,","text_sha256":"2d040ff6d070da81e819bdccda8b799480e5988de29054ef9b104b2795c68f11","unit_id":"s022","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-126-s022-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["iOS Experiment Client","iOS UDP Listener"],"section_title":"iOS UDP Listener","source_file":"repositories/repo-126-SedraFTPVariant/README.md","source_line_end":347,"source_line_start":347,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- a dispatch queue,","text_sha256":"fb5c31c9ecc925a3202653f42e373f582a19f6e74310ca4bb8a879abec637478","un