INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-127-rd002',127,'Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3909,14,249,'Section: Collaboration and Evidence Context

This repository is a research tooling and operating journal rather than a conventional software product.

The root documentation explicitly names a Rogers Experiment.

It also refers to:

a Husky mobile robot,

University of Waterloo RoboHub infrastructure,

a credentialed UWaterloo QConnectManager repository,

Quectel cellular hardware,

Wi-Fi access-point configurations,

5G experiments.

The appropriate interpretation is therefore a research collaboration context.

Repository-specific HTML tools, experiment procedures, and analysis workflows are strong evidence of hands-on experimental engineering.

The QConnectManager driver itself is described as being cloned from a University of Waterloo repository and must be treated as external research infrastructure rather than owner-authored modem-driver code.

Section: What This Project Is

Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications is a research toolkit for collecting, aligning, processing, visualizing, and statistically analyzing wireless performance data while a mobile robot operates across Wi-Fi and 5G networks.

5G radio metrics,

5G modem operation,

5G data processing.

It records how the networking experiment is run, how clocks are normalized, how raw outputs are transformed, and how mobility events are related to network performance.

Section: Mobile Robot Experimental Setup

The root README documents basic Husky access.

The workflow includes:

configuring the Ethernet host on the same subnet as the Husky,

pinging the Husky to verify connectivity,

connecting through SSH,

enabling joystick operation.

This grounds the project in a physical robot workflow rather than a purely simulated network dataset.

Section: Rogers Experiment Workstreams

The documented completed work includes:

mid-range 5G modem sanity checking,

collecting useful AT-command behavior,

repeating a two-access-point Wi-Fi setup,','["quectel","qconnectmanager","html","uwaterloo","collaboration","context","mobile","robot","experimental","setup","rogers","experiment","workstreams"]','["Collaboration and Evidence Context","What This Project Is","Mobile Robot Experimental Setup","Rogers Experiment Workstreams"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-127-s002-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["Collaboration and Evidence Context"],"section_title":"Collaboration and Evidence Context","source_file":"repositories/repo-127-Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications/README.md","source_line_end":18,"source_line_start":18,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This repository is a research tooling and operating journal rather than a conventional software product.","text_sha256":"41cdef61dc765e196abcdb2218dc7d59bb27471f9cd01e2542305d9186ead679","unit_id":"s002","word_count":15},{"block_id":"repo-127-s002-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["Collaboration and Evidence Context"],"section_title":"Collaboration and Evidence Context","source_file":"repositories/repo-127-Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications/README.md","source_line_end":20,"source_line_start":20,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The root documentation explicitly names a `Rogers Experiment`.","text_sha256":"1675e135e8cce23b669e59f62cca36c874b6aa201c00fa230e50c0b4e46b051c","unit_id":"s002","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-127-s002-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s002","section_path":["Collaboration and Evidence Context"],"section_title":"Collaboration and Evidence Context","source_file":"repositories/repo-127-Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications/README.md","source_line_end":22,"source_line_start":22,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequ