INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-127-rd006',127,'Mobile-Robots-Telecommunications',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','positive','interpretive',0.3343,6,135,'Section: Wi-Fi Mesh / Roaming Analysis > Performance Overlay

The documented tap3 design overlays:

latency,

throughput,

AP1/AP2 presence.

The throughput stream is aligned with presence.

The tool also includes plot copy-to-clipboard behavior.

This is direct evidence of investigating network mobility rather than analyzing performance as a stationary aggregate.

Section: 5G Processing Suite > fg2: Throughput Versus Radio Quality

fg2 aggregates multiple runs.

It relates throughput to radio metrics such as:

RSRP,

SINR,

RSSI.

Outputs include:

box plots,

CDFs,

scatter plots,

correlation statistics.

Section: 5G Processing Suite > fg3: Latency Versus Radio Quality

fg3 applies the same multi-run analytical idea to latency.

This provides a direct way to investigate whether radio-state degradation corresponds to latency degradation.

Section: Scale and Complexity

