INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-128-rd006',128,'Indoor-Journal-',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','deployment_operations','positive','repository_specific',0.4081,11,172,'Section: 5G Data Collection and Modem Operations

The Data Collection/5G material documents the Quectel modem workflow in detail.

Section: 5G Data Collection and Modem Operations > Linux Setup

The documented environment uses Linux/Ubuntu.

The modem is connected over USB, with emphasis on the correct USB interface.

Section: 5G Data Collection and Modem Operations > ModemManager Coordination

The setup temporarily stops Linux ModemManager when direct control of the Quectel interface is required.

Section: 5G Data Collection and Modem Operations > QConnectManager Build and Install

The project documents:

cloning the UWaterloo QConnectManager repository,

compiling it,

installing its kernel module,

running quectel-CM.

The QConnectManager source itself is external research infrastructure.

The owner-attributable evidence is the setup, troubleshooting, automation, and use in the experimental platform.

Section: 5G Data Collection and Modem Operations > Automated Startup Script

The documented runtest workflow automates modem startup.

Its shell logic:

stops ModemManager,

removes/reloads QMI-related kernel modules,

waits between transitions,

runs QConnectManager with IPv4 and IPv6.

The script is described as a practical workaround for obtaining stable modem operation and throughput.','["quectel","qconnectmanager","data","collection","modem","operations","linux","setup","modemmanager","coordination","build","install","automated","startup","script"]','["G Data Collection and Modem Operations"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-128-s015-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":3,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s015","section_path":["5G Data Collection and Modem Operations"],"section_title":"5G Data Collection and Modem Operations","source_file":"repositories/repo-128-Indoor-Journal-/README.md","source_line_end":208,"source_line_start":208,"specificity_score":0.65,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The `Data Collection/5G` material documents the Quectel modem workflow in detail.","text_sha256":"eac58555b0646bceeb927cc9d8beaa5f3f63bc7b51426469f1272f6b35dc78fd","unit_id":"s015","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-128-s016-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["5G Data Collection and Modem Operations","Linux Setup"],"section_title":"Linux Setup","source_file":"repositories/repo-128-Indoor-Journal-/README.md","source_line_end":212,"source_line_start":212,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The documented environment uses Linux/Ubuntu.","text_sha256":"b0abe6604405e7b7e7adc7b3656333b9f037fe4b7c6d961227448c95630d2cf3","unit_id":"s016","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-128-s016-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["5G Data Collection and Modem Operations","Linux Setup"],"section_title":"Linux Setup","source_file":"repositories/repo-128-Indoor-Journal-/README.md","source_line_end":214,"source_line_start":214,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The modem is connected over USB, with emphasis on the correct USB int