INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-129-rd004',129,'Apple-Publication',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3838,17,230,'Section: Net++ iperf3 Suite Runner

Example source form:

automate(duration=30,cooldown=30,n=50);
sleep(10);

This shifts experiment automation from hard-coded GUI choices toward a declarative script.

Section: Net++ Command Model

The parser currently recognizes two command families:

automate,
sleep.

The language uses semicolons to delimit top-level commands.

Arguments can appear inside parentheses.

Section: Net++ Command Model > automate

The command requires:

duration,

cooldown,

n.

These parameters describe:

duration of each iperf test,

cooldown between tests,

repetition count.

Section: Net++ Command Model > sleep

The suite can explicitly insert idle time between experiment phases.

Section: Parser Engineering

NetPPParser is a real parser for the intentionally small command language.

Section: Parser Engineering > Top-Level Command Splitting

The parser scans source character by character.

It tracks:

parenthesis depth,

single-quoted strings,

double-quoted strings,

escape state.

A semicolon only terminates a command when the parser is outside nested parentheses and quoted strings.

This is more robust than blindly splitting the source on every semicolon.

Section: Parser Engineering > Comment Handling

The current parser removes # comments before command parsing.

The repository commit history explicitly records work to fix comment parsing.

That gives a direct example of language-tooling iteration based on a parser edge case.

Section: Parser Engineering > Argument Parsing

The parser supports:

named arguments,

positional values,

signed integers,

quoted strings.

Identifier names are validated.

Section: Parser Engineering > Build Diagnostics

The parser returns BuildIssue objects with:

severity,

