INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-129-rd005',129,'Apple-Publication',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3522,5,217,'Section: Parser Engineering > Build Diagnostics

source position.

The application can therefore perform a build/syntax-check phase before execution.

Section: Parser Engineering > Semantic Validation

For automate, validation includes:

required arguments,

integer type checks,

positive duration,

nonnegative cooldown,

valid repetition count.

This is not just string parsing.

The application performs basic semantic validation of the experiment program.

Section: Build / Run / Stop Workflow

The PyQt6 application exposes distinct concepts of:

Build,

Run,

Stop.

That resembles a miniature development environment for experiment scripts.

Each command can have a visible execution state.

The documented color convention is:

yellow: running,

green: passed,

red: failed.

This makes a long experiment suite inspectable at command granularity.

Section: iperf3 Integration

The Net++ runner executes TCP iperf3 client tests.

The design allows binding to a selected local IPv4/interface.

This is important when the research machine has multiple network paths and the experiment must force traffic onto a specific adapter.

Section: iperf3 Integration > Success Criteria

The source documents success as:

process exit code zero,
and, when JSON output is requested, successful JSON parsing without an iperf-reported error.

That is stronger than assuming process launch equals a valid experiment.

Section: PyQt6 Desktop Engineering

The suite imports a broad PyQt6 interface layer including:

main window,

plain-text editor,

status areas,

toolbar actions,

forms,

combo boxes,

spin boxes,','["pyqt6","iperf3","parser","engineering","build","diagnostics","semantic","validation","stop","workflow","integration","success","criteria","desktop"]','["Parser Engineering","Build / Run / Stop Workflow","iperf3 Integration","PyQt6 Desktop Engineering"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-129-s016-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Parser Engineering","Build Diagnostics"],"section_title":"Build Diagnostics","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":213,"source_line_start":213,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- source position.","text_sha256":"084fd8bfbcb2d05ec6a26de3303df1b6acec3b339a2c9aec9508832a0d95df86","unit_id":"s016","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-129-s016-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s016","section_path":["Parser Engineering","Build Diagnostics"],"section_title":"Build Diagnostics","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":215,"source_line_start":215,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application can therefore perform a build/syntax-check phase before execution.","text_sha256":"20fa206e7eaeff747c8034dbcc1a259c5c8d10ef84a659bd6575d9305b78a4c3","unit_id":"s016","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-129-s017-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s017","section_path":["Parser Engineering","Semantic Validation"],"section_title":"Semantic Validation","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":219,"source_line_start":219,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"For `automate`, validation includes:","text_sha256":"336199824c21d778899e6d7cded49be3ca51faba28e7ce307e1fd0e694402ace","unit_id":"s017","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-129-s017-b