INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-129-rd008',129,'Apple-Publication',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3431,4,299,'Section: TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis > Doubling Points

The tool finds the first timestamp at which cumulative data crosses:

B0 × 2^k

for successive values of k.

This converts raw packet-delivery output into explicit ramp/doubling timing evidence.

Section: TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis > Delivery Rate

The program also computes a per-bin rate:

Section: TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis > Visualization

The GUI can plot:

cumulative delivered bytes,

per-bin delivery rate,

vertical markers for doubling points.

Section: TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis > Focus Window

The user can restrict the visualization to the first few milliseconds.

That is useful for studying the early connection phase where TCP ramp-up behavior is most visible.

Section: TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis > Export

The tool supports:

PNG plot export,

CSV export of nonzero bins,

copyable doubling table.

This is a publication-friendly transformation from packet-capture data to structured transport-layer figures/tables.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Reuse Instead of Reinvention

Identical artifacts are carried from earlier repositories where their behavior already fit the new experiment.

This reduces duplicate implementation effort.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Extension at the Correct Layer

New work is concentrated where the publication experiment needs more capability:

iperf3 suite orchestration,

a command language,

parser diagnostics,

transport-layer ramp analysis.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Build Before Execute

The Net++ tool separates syntax/semantic checking from suite execution.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Explicit Execution Status

Each suite command has a visible run result.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Interface Binding

The workload can be directed through a selected local network interface.

Section: Engineering Practices Evidenced > Structured Export

Several analysis tools export data or figures into forms suitable for further research use.

Section: Skills Demonstrated > Experiment Automation

repeated test execution,

configurable duration,

cooldown control,

sequence scripting,

stop/cancel behavior,

status tracking.','["iperf3","parser","ramp","slow-start","doubling","points","delivery","rate","visualization","focus","window","export","engineering","practices","evidenced","reuse","instead","reinvention","extension","correct","layer","build","before","execute"]','["TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis","Engineering Practices Evidenced","Skills Demonstrated"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-129-s031-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis","Doubling Points"],"section_title":"Doubling Points","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":391,"source_line_start":391,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The tool finds the first timestamp at which cumulative data crosses:","text_sha256":"bae93bceb9348394207fb5fac8e30cbb040560a6cae9128ad650483866b0dfa2","unit_id":"s031","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-129-s031-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis","Doubling Points"],"section_title":"Doubling Points","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":395,"source_line_start":393,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"```text\nB0 × 2^k\n```","text_sha256":"5eee56fc03ffbd8c466936ba362bb445f997d3a9cac2440990255f3fb8b7457c","unit_id":"s031","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-129-s031-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s031","section_path":["TCP Ramp / Slow-Start Analysis","Doubling Points"],"section_title":"Doubling Points","source_file":"repositories/repo-129-Apple-Publication/README.md","source_line_end":397,"source_line_start":397,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"for successive values of `k`.","text_sha256":"af09d7a03a21d3605ac65891b4d17fa1a1