INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-130-rd005',130,'LogicApp',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.35,5,264,'Section: SQL Persistence > leakParams

the unique message ID;
the normalized event timestamp.

This creates an event-level persistence record before later notification logic.

Section: SQL Persistence > sensorDetails

The workflow loads a sensor row using the parsed MAC address.

Sensor metadata supplies business context such as:

associated client identifier;

physical location;

building;

floor;

unit;

spot;

leak-state fields;

notification-related state.

Section: SQL Persistence > clientInfo

The workflow resolves the client associated with the sensor.

Client data is then used to route direct email/SMS notifications.

Section: SQL Persistence > linkedUser

The workflow queries linked users by client identifier.

This supports one-to-many notification routing rather than assuming every sensor has only one human recipient.

Section: Leak-State Logic

The workflow contains conditional logic around the sensor''s leak-update state.

The orchestration is therefore not simply:

message -> send alert

It incorporates persisted sensor state before deciding how to proceed.

One observed branch updates a drying-day field to a fixed value under a condition and participates in the broader leak_update handling path.

This is evidence of business-state-aware orchestration.

Section: Demo Sensor Branch

The workflow includes a Demo Sensor condition based on sensor-location content.

This shows that the orchestration distinguishes special/demo devices from ordinary production routing inside the same workflow definition.

That distinction is implemented as workflow policy rather than a separate service.

Section: Snooze / Notification Suppression

The workflow contains conditions related to notification snoozing.

The important architectural point is that notification delivery is not treated as unconditional.

Stored business state can suppress or redirect outward communication.

This is a useful example of integrating operational state with notification side effects.','["persistence","leakparams","sensordetails","clientinfo","linkeduser","leak-state","logic","demo","sensor","branch","snooze","notification","suppression"]','["SQL Persistence","Leak-State Logic","Demo Sensor Branch","Snooze / Notification Suppression"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-130-s011-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["SQL Persistence","`leakParams`"],"section_title":"`leakParams`","source_file":"repositories/repo-130-LogicApp/README.md","source_line_end":184,"source_line_start":183,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- the unique message ID;\n- the normalized event timestamp.","text_sha256":"59bbc6f377f08119b1d0ee780e18a12a38a46f1a623840d03f68498bfc68cd27","unit_id":"s011","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-130-s011-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["SQL Persistence","`leakParams`"],"section_title":"`leakParams`","source_file":"repositories/repo-130-LogicApp/README.md","source_line_end":186,"source_line_start":186,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This creates an event-level persistence record before later notification logic.","text_sha256":"086fce12459d995431b48d409eab42592ee89879d122ad34f4b40056bbbb088e","unit_id":"s011","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-130-s012-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["SQL Persistence","`sensorDetails`"],"section_title":"`sensorDetails`","source_file":"repositories/repo-130-LogicApp/README.md","source_line_end":190,"source_line_start":190,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The workflow loads a sensor row using the parsed MAC address.","text_sha256":"466c82b956780fd0d035fb5deb864666e8c310d4349be9e9d68