6,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The README explicitly notes that UE-context release after successful registration can represent normal idle behavior rather than a failed registration.","text_sha256":"de92f148e3fa1521404e406d343f30bf452a50b0dab7dd6fb6468d71b4076890","unit_id":"s014","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-131-s014-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["UE Context Release Interpretation"],"section_title":"UE Context Release Interpretation","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":218,"source_line_start":218,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"This is useful troubleshooting evidence.","text_sha256":"71fc6230c827c1e04dfe34c7c6315fb4e1079d8602dc7172ec5572ea2140e2f6","unit_id":"s014","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-131-s014-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["UE Context Release Interpretation"],"section_title":"UE Context Release Interpretation","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":220,"source_line_start":220,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"It shows distinction between:","text_sha256":"e76f6edcd6114fa343759116c9e9b407f2f5c827e9af7c399e25b5a61070bc9e","unit_id":"s014","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-131-s014-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s014","section_path":["UE Context Release Interpretation"],"section_title":"UE Context Release Interpretation","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":223,"source_line_start":222,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"- registration failure;\n- successful registration followed by normal control-plane state transition.","text_sha256":"2a1af05794d6a442367a59a30c6883259a53803dadf0682b8b0bf7245d849be6","unit_id":"s014","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-131-s015-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Data-Plane Activation"],"section_title":"Data-Plane Activation","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":227,"source_line_start":227,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The runbook separates registration from data-session establishment.","text_sha256":"b6999fcea69b0e2f2f7491a7dce3718726161a29c81ef4a64c3749ebf51e82ff","unit_id":"s015","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-131-s015-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Data-Plane Activation"],"section_title":"Data-Plane Activation","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":229,"source_line_start":229,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"After registration, it brings the modem''s network interface up and invokes Quectel Connection Manager using QMI.","text_sha256":"c37597a7e59fcefebc21f6e711a4ff61cecdc5cafe17a2fcd3be7ef8efd5b732","unit_id":"s015","word_count":16}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","document_text_sha256":"b0d1147ff4dafcdc91cd6f7ad92c28437e450ffd2635a9888f833297ce12f021","earliest_source_line":166,"embedding_text_sha256":"8e87c254858785ab834279fdd7513c0b4f14adf14b5381392aeb019e39d9f06b","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"1bd2ffcd52109d45c1ffed3b101369b0f20c642be722cbfb14be3af4c261c23c","repository_source_line_end":534,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-131-rd005',131,'5G-SA',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','mixed','interpretive',0.3492,9,221,'Section: Data-Plane Activation

A configured DNN/APN must match the subscriber profile.

This shows understanding that successful 5G registration alone does not prove user-plane IP connectivity.

Section: Automatic File Discovery

The script searches for data by directory/file conventions rather than requiring every path as a CLI argument.

It identifies:

a throughput directory matching C_*logs case-insensitively;

a latency file in the scenario root, preferring names containing ping/latency/ICMP;

modem JSON under logs/, preferring modem_status*.json.

This reduces manual per-scenario configuration.

Section: Unit Normalization

The script handles multiple iperf unit scales.

Examples include conversion from:

Gbits/sec to Mbps;

Kbits/sec to Mbps;

bits/sec to Mbps;

GBytes/KBytes/Bytes to MB.

This is important when aggregating measurements because iperf may dynamically choose display units.

Section: Modem RF JSON Parsing

The script reads modem JSON samples and extracts serving-cell information.

Observed RF fields include:

RSRP;

RSRQ;

SINR;

cell state;

radio access technology;

PCI;

ARFCN;

band;

sample index;

timestamp.

This is direct evidence of cellular radio-metric processing.

Section: RF Metric Cropping

RF samples are also cropped to the throughput-derived clock window.

The result is three output tables that cover the same scenario interval:

throughput
latency
RF metrics

This supports later correlation or comparative analysis without repeatedly parsing the raw logs.

Section: CSV Output Design

The script emits explicit tabular schemas instead of writing loosely formatted text.

