INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-131-rd009',131,'5G-SA',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','neutral','interpretive',0.3425,1,164,'Section: Throughput Parsing

The extractor parses timestamped iperf3 text output with regular expressions.

For each interval it extracts:

wall-clock time;

interval start;

interval end;

transferred data;

transfer unit;

bitrate;

bitrate unit.

The output normalizes transfer values to MB and throughput to Mbps.

Section: Throughput Time Window

The parser derives an interval-start clock time from the reported interval-end wall clock and duration.

The first throughput interval becomes the scenario start boundary and the last interval becomes the scenario end boundary.

That time window is then reused to crop latency and RF data.

The throughput log therefore acts as the alignment anchor.

Section: Latency Parsing

Latency lines are parsed from timestamped ICMP output.

Extracted fields include:

timestamp;

ICMP sequence number;

latency in milliseconds.

The script accounts for the logger''s repeated-second timestamp artifact and reconstructs a conventional microsecond timestamp string.

Section: Latency Cropping

Latency rows are retained only when their wall-clock time falls within the throughput-derived start/end window.

This creates scenario-level temporal alignment across independently recorded tools.','["iperf3","throughput","parsing","time","window","latency","cropping"]','["Throughput Parsing","Throughput Time Window","Latency Parsing","Latency Cropping"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-131-s020-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Throughput Parsing"],"section_title":"Throughput Parsing","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":292,"source_line_start":292,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The extractor parses timestamped iperf3 text output with regular expressions.","text_sha256":"a6b7c4a50c2c354060588ee54939501ada5072d954c31497631d547969d16eaa","unit_id":"s020","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-131-s020-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Throughput Parsing"],"section_title":"Throughput Parsing","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":294,"source_line_start":294,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"For each interval it extracts:","text_sha256":"38efc05d231a4ab44dc004f90d82bf368a56b9099886233511291ec66a6849ef","unit_id":"s020","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-131-s020-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Throughput Parsing"],"section_title":"Throughput Parsing","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":296,"source_line_start":296,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- wall-clock time;","text_sha256":"c664ef9a00f91fbcfbf71e69c96a03a557a8aba2e5c430b8fa322af7ca4319ef","unit_id":"s020","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-131-s020-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Throughput Pars