INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-131-rd010',131,'5G-SA',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3519,10,158,'Section: CSV Output Design

Latency output includes timestamp, sequence, and latency.

RF output includes timestamped signal-quality and cell metadata.

This creates a clean intermediate representation for downstream analysis.

Section: CLI Usability

The script supports:

--out to override the output directory;
--name to override the output prefix.

Otherwise it uses the current scenario directory name as the label.

Section: Research Workflow Skills

The repository demonstrates:

controlled testbed bring-up;

layered cellular-network validation;

Linux service/process management;

AT-command modem configuration;

QMI data-session setup;

iperf3 measurement processing;

latency-log processing;

RF telemetry extraction;

temporal alignment across measurement sources;

reproducible scenario organization.

Section: Telecommunications Skills

The strongest telecommunications concepts evidenced here are:

5G Standalone architecture;

core-network functions;

AMF registration;

SMF/PDU-session reasoning;

gNB operation;

N2 connectivity;

NR band n78;

TDD radio configuration;

RSRP;

RSRQ;

SINR;

PCI;

ARFCN;

DNN/APN matching;

UE modem control.

Section: Systems Skills

The runbook shows practical work across:

Linux processes;

serial modem interfaces;

kernel/network interfaces;

QMI tooling;

SDR hardware;

IP networking;

service logs.','["pdu-session","iperf3","rsrp","rsrq","sinr","arfcn","output","design","usability","research","workflow","skills","telecommunications","systems"]','["CSV Output Design","CLI Usability","Research Workflow Skills","Telecommunications Skills","Systems Skills"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-131-s027-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s027","section_path":["CSV Output Design"],"section_title":"CSV Output Design","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":386,"source_line_start":386,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Latency output includes timestamp, sequence, and latency.","text_sha256":"26039cf0c27442c28185a9b5f4ef5d45a5dba12b18b4e535c1b972d0d517d90d","unit_id":"s027","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-131-s027-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s027","section_path":["CSV Output Design"],"section_title":"CSV Output Design","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":388,"source_line_start":388,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"RF output includes timestamped signal-quality and cell metadata.","text_sha256":"f6311366df493ba5dedc3758e6668a0a3f95ee4f8fc547c4e5b64f6d8535415f","unit_id":"s027","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-131-s027-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s027","section_path":["CSV Output Design"],"section_title":"CSV Output Design","source_file":"repositories/repo-131-5G-SA/README.md","source_line_end":390,"source_line_start":390,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This creates a clean intermediate representation for downstream analysis.","text_sha256":"04a6fdab9707bab522984a9251a5698ebfc39cf2690af57dae4f0edd2b461fe0","unit_id":"s027","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-131-s028-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_