Specific Salt","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":130,"source_line_start":130,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This means the same master key derives different byte streams for different services.","text_sha256":"f50194b23ee1e38dbdc427f7bba4bedb42fdd1f82c3632d6dbc12f2a998a2ee2","unit_id":"s008","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-133-s008-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Service-Specific Salt"],"section_title":"Service-Specific Salt","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":132,"source_line_start":132,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The project therefore avoids producing one identical password for every site when the service key changes.","text_sha256":"86e5d5b7b6a9ace60eee81d9c28c5f960d5ebcc7ba25cb8c428521506e683190","unit_id":"s008","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-133-s009-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Derived Bytes"],"section_title":"Derived Bytes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":136,"source_line_start":136,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"PBKDF2 produces the byte material used by the later password-construction steps.","text_sha256":"2f1f6c8837cf84079ccc015f23615dbb1b01e83524d88b0c58fc8c918ccc24f0","unit_id":"s009","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-133-s009-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Derived Bytes"],"section_title":"Derived Bytes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":138,"source_line_start":138,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The JavaScript consumes those bytes deterministically.","text_sha256":"89ca1dd918c1ffbe540680295855c87518f1fab6f36b95a2efebbce855ab24b4","unit_id":"s009","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-133-s009-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Derived Bytes"],"section_title":"Derived Bytes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":140,"source_line_start":140,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"No call to a random-number generator is required for the final password layout because repeatability is an explicit goal.","text_sha256":"facc9a8f813c4114a42ea15281538d16d043f2b33f8570e799af95c94f3853cc","unit_id":"s009","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":144,"source_line_start":144,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The output policy defines separate character sets for:","text_sha256":"de145abe6acb90da626bf777beed8ad98e548e89d17058b29cb072625b208942","unit_id":"s010","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":146,"source_line_start":146,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- uppercase letters;","text_sha256":"9ae3ebeeab6995bd198d9d4b35aba913c033430c430a3114caafef6918e6391d","unit_id":"s010","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":147,"source_line_start":147,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- lowercase letters;","text_sha256":"0c5300b1d6d18361509a40903f82b2b8d8519178d44c6f1154111fcc3db5fcea","unit_id":"s010","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":148,"source_line_start":148,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- digits;","text_sha256":"a6ed76333f5f0a45fda5605d63076db2b2798adee7294e6614934936789e2bd9","unit_id":"s010","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":149,"source_line_start":149,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- symbols.","text_sha256":"771a8186b433be32c3219f7a7c4d95d92c2a0eb75f21cab1a118c14f78bdb099","unit_id":"s010","word_count":2},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":151,"source_line_start":151,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The implementation ensures that at least one character from each class is selected before filling the remainder of the requested length.","text_sha256":"20a8bb0175bfad2ee1ea1a6c1bf22d6bf40d55b7075d1584e755ae1e62416390","unit_id":"s010","word_count":21},{"block_id":"repo-133-s010-b007","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s010","section_path":["Character Classes"],"section_title":"Character Classes","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":153,"source_line_start":153,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This is a practical compatibility feature for services that require multiple password character classes.","text_sha256":"400a3b8c1d67404c1a468ab47c4c84575f540e8ed421e0de86c2b10b85b17169","unit_id":"s010","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-133-s011-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Combined Character Set"],"section_title":"Combined Character Set","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":157,"source_line_start":157,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"After the required-class characters are chosen, remaining password positions are filled from the combined supported character set.","text_sha256":"54707e710a27ade636138c81b3aa833fb7a30259c30966fecf02717db8fb4e5b","unit_id":"s011","word_count":17},{"block_id":"repo-133-s011-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Combined Character Set"],"section_title":"Combined Character Set","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":159,"source_line_start":159,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Derived bytes select positions within that set.","text_sha256":"dc75320e65adcc879ac774010ec2ae3a433104335c465ddeb3991869e7e48145","unit_id":"s011","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-133-s011-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s011","section_path":["Combined Character Set"],"section_title":"Combined Character Set","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":161,"source_line_start":161,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The process remains deterministic because every selection is driven by PBKDF2 output.","text_sha256":"1ba7525c9b17f906a7c3e28a354db3b2ff3081236c2aa629a5a09c33279873f1","unit_id":"s011","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-133-s012-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Deterministic Shuffle"],"section_title":"Deterministic Shuffle","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":165,"source_line_start":165,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The application then shuffles the constructed characters using a deterministic Fisher-Yates-style process driven by derived bytes.","text_sha256":"c58fd15a50b53d0baff8f187014346a31a77172b1e77cb263ec6c3d4e81cf3c0","unit_id":"s012","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-133-s012-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Deterministic Shuffle"],"section_title":"Deterministic Shuffle","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":167,"source_line_start":167,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This prevents the first four output positions from permanently revealing a fixed uppercase/lowercase/digit/symbol ordering.","text_sha256":"600fa4d037209c17e6dd3c4110e4cd8ca4b1bbf5a4c4ff9f7e90cc7a95056e21","unit_id":"s012","word_count":14},{"block_id":"repo-133-s012-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s012","section_path":["Deterministic Shuffle"],"section_title":"Deterministic Shuffle","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":169,"source_line_start":169,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Because the shuffle source is also deterministic, reproducibility is preserved.","text_sha256":"0b33aa4c4a742da50d05860c96a7c285b93feacdd886e2ca35f78ff8e5b8ead2","unit_id":"s012","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-133-s013-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s013","section_path":["Why the Shuffle Matters"],"section_title":"Why the Shuffle Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","source_line_end":173,"source_line_start":173,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Without shuffling, a generator that always inserts required classes in the same positions would expose structural regularity.","text_sha256":"1b7e20b5a4b9437ed776fa61d78a71d39a17e8e78518adff5774d630f0eb1668","unit_id":"s013","word_count":17}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-133-Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden/README.md","document_text_sha256":"bdeab6b6dbd29e6ba00ca34b9cd0815a5fee8033979b0cf4fbe1bb8c286a1815","earliest_source_line":114,"embedding_text_sha256":"c1cd4b7353cf40e1a05a4335b6a3f934150a9ec62df693196ee818feccb27e4a","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"b9d205777d4f0dd9a9414293d307c8a6deecd85cf387f12cedd2aa479d49e277","repository_source_line_end":386,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-133-rd005',133,'Password-Hashing-Function-for-Bitwarden',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','interpretive',0.3424,3,233,'Section: Why the Shuffle Matters

The deterministic shuffle spreads those required characters through the password while keeping the same input-to-output mapping.

Section: Clipboard Integration

The UI includes a copy action using the browser clipboard API.

This avoids requiring the user to manually select the generated password text.

The clipboard feature is a convenience surface, separate from the derivation algorithm.

Section: UI Design

The page includes a dark, card-style interface.

The UI separates:

explanation/instructions;

master-key input;

service/account input;

length selection;

generation action;

generated password display;

copy action;

warning/information text.

The design is compact because the product has one primary workflow.

Section: No Build-System Dependency

The source is directly usable as a static HTML file.

That means the implementation does not depend on:

React;

Vue;

Angular;

a Node build process;

a backend API.

The corpus records this positively as a deliberately lightweight static-web implementation.

Section: Local Computation Boundary

Password derivation occurs locally in the observed JavaScript.

There is no custom application server in this repository receiving the master key.

That reduces architecture surface, but it does not by itself prove the utility is suitable for every production credential-management threat model.

Section: Password Policy Engineering

The character-class logic shows awareness of common password acceptance policies.

The generator ensures multiple character categories while still allowing configurable length.

That is application-level policy layered above the KDF.

Section: Browser Engineering Skills

This repository demonstrates:

vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript;

