INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-134-rd003',134,'Thesis',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','other_repository_evidence','positive','repository_specific',0.3657,6,315,'Section: Exact Motion Timestamp Handling

no ceiling;

no timestamp approximation.

This is a strong methodological choice because coarse clipping can move samples across motion boundaries and distort short transient behavior.

Section: Global Direction Assignment

The alternating forward/backward rule is based on the globally ordered motion-event sequence.

This matters when motion events are spread across multiple files.

The logic first gathers all events, sorts them, then applies odd/even direction.

That is more defensible than resetting the direction count inside every log file.

Section: Fixed Analysis Horizon

The standard throughput extractor retains normalized intervals whose start is at or before 57 seconds.

That creates a common motion-duration analysis window.

The script''s comments explicitly distinguish the retained 57.00-58.00 interval from later intervals that fall outside the configured start-time threshold.

Section: Why Local Time Matters

Different experiment runs begin at different wall-clock times.

Normalizing to motion-relative elapsed time permits cross-run aggregation without aligning unrelated clock timestamps.

The raw source time still determines clipping; local time is introduced only after the correct motion interval is identified.

Section: Deterministic Motion-Log Selection

The special all-forward workflow expects a prepared motion-log input and is designed to stop rather than ambiguously select from multiple possible prepared logs.

That reduces accidental preprocessing against the wrong motion reference.

Section: Old Output Cleanup

Several extractors intentionally clear old generated output before writing new derived files.

This prevents stale run artifacts from being mixed into a new analysis.

For research scripts, stale generated files are a real reproducibility risk because aggregate plotters may otherwise consume results that no longer correspond to the current raw inputs.

Section: Aggregate Time Axis

The plotter aligns runs onto a common elapsed-time axis.

This allows statistics such as mean and variability to be calculated at the same trajectory-relative time across repetitions.

Section: Smart Legend Variant

The latest commit adds plot-throughput-smartlegend.py.

That shows continued iteration on publication presentation after the main processing pipeline existed.','["exact","motion","timestamp","handling","global","direction","assignment","fixed","horizon","local","time","matters","deterministic","motion-log","selection","output","cleanup","aggregate","axis","smart","legend","variant"]','["Exact Motion Timestamp Handling","Global Direction Assignment","Fixed Analysis Horizon","Why Local Time Matters","Deterministic Motion-Log Selection","Old Output Cleanup","Aggregate Time Axis","Smart Legend Variant"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-134-s008-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Exact Motion Timestamp Handling"],"section_title":"Exact Motion Timestamp Handling","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":136,"source_line_start":136,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- no ceiling;","text_sha256":"004b8e4ddff51bd81ad1e98f9b088f48971f10158e7c914ca96caf0f0254ec15","unit_id":"s008","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-134-s008-b005","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Exact Motion Timestamp Handling"],"section_title":"Exact Motion Timestamp Handling","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":137,"source_line_start":137,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- no timestamp approximation.","text_sha256":"53ccaddb0fecdbc842311e6e209ddc6a6b8dafed13da1724aec9a2623a9048e7","unit_id":"s008","word_count":4},{"block_id":"repo-134-s008-b006","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s008","section_path":["Exact Motion Timestamp Handling"],"section_title":"Exact Motion Timestamp Handling","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":139,"source_line_start":139,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repos