,"source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":214,"source_line_start":214,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The script''s comments explicitly distinguish the retained `57.00-58.00` interval from later intervals that fall outside the configured start-time threshold.","text_sha256":"064eb269d147125949b05dd53753e47a9a0825969df91ad00bfce1a0b894577a","unit_id":"s014","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-134-s015-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Why Local Time Matters"],"section_title":"Why Local Time Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":218,"source_line_start":218,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Different experiment runs begin at different wall-clock times.","text_sha256":"545c59b8ca8255b15f98894e1116e9148cf67007bd70892e4af643f192aeb0c7","unit_id":"s015","word_count":8},{"block_id":"repo-134-s015-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Why Local Time Matters"],"section_title":"Why Local Time Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":220,"source_line_start":220,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Normalizing to motion-relative elapsed time permits cross-run aggregation without aligning unrelated clock timestamps.","text_sha256":"f2a386058d7a7b4c52b3b009141e18f3a943e92c2b2859924ae93e28175cb8c0","unit_id":"s015","word_count":13},{"block_id":"repo-134-s015-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s015","section_path":["Why Local Time Matters"],"section_title":"Why Local Time Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":222,"source_line_start":222,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The raw source time still determines clipping; local time is introduced only after the correct motion interval is identified.","text_sha256":"eabf0b5010d5f91393285f595f9540db9d25421c8aab5311be83acd9fadd0179","unit_id":"s015","word_count":19},{"block_id":"repo-134-s019-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Deterministic Motion-Log Selection"],"section_title":"Deterministic Motion-Log Selection","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":256,"source_line_start":256,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The special all-forward workflow expects a prepared motion-log input and is designed to stop rather than ambiguously select from multiple possible prepared logs.","text_sha256":"6eedc891d72e6c4900cf8c741c85fc78f927e89f0b0f02ec7a4bbd18e9d4b416","unit_id":"s019","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-134-s019-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s019","section_path":["Deterministic Motion-Log Selection"],"section_title":"Deterministic Motion-Log Selection","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":258,"source_line_start":258,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"That reduces accidental preprocessing against the wrong motion reference.","text_sha256":"77cd67f139571e0646a0cc8b515fe995f2d643395f8547820fe33dd2a874b108","unit_id":"s019","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-134-s020-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Old Output Cleanup"],"section_title":"Old Output Cleanup","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":262,"source_line_start":262,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Several extractors intentionally clear old generated output before writing new derived files.","text_sha256":"21c2ca76d65ed2ce6a7031569d9d7a02b51a6861f25aab5a2f926ffd540fe6e2","unit_id":"s020","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-134-s020-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Old Output Cleanup"],"section_title":"Old Output Cleanup","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":264,"source_line_start":264,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This prevents stale run artifacts from being mixed into a new analysis.","text_sha256":"d5e4a27971e3411773a4250e5e08d9918bd67309aa4042a88e9397181fd1d7b4","unit_id":"s020","word_count":12},{"block_id":"repo-134-s020-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s020","section_path":["Old Output Cleanup"],"section_title":"Old Output Cleanup","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":266,"source_line_start":266,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"For research scripts, stale generated files are a real reproducibility risk because aggregate plotters may otherwise consume results that no longer correspond to the current raw inputs.","text_sha256":"5ef399bec6f2b5148f6b4b9978985a22c334c612e9650aa537bdfdc4115a36a8","unit_id":"s020","word_count":27},{"block_id":"repo-134-s022-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["Aggregate Time Axis"],"section_title":"Aggregate Time Axis","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":276,"source_line_start":276,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The plotter aligns runs onto a common elapsed-time axis.","text_sha256":"e88ba0ae617904f53da8bb522ead367075c52fe331c7fa90601a8e2ec2b2e5c8","unit_id":"s022","word_count":9},{"block_id":"repo-134-s022-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s022","section_path":["Aggregate Time Axis"],"section_title":"Aggregate Time Axis","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":278,"source_line_start":278,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This allows statistics such as mean and variability to be calculated at the same trajectory-relative time across repetitions.","text_sha256":"f7e822ac18bee3da0869da1206623399c31fcdafdc2333629952cb2a6e150320","unit_id":"s022","word_count":18},{"block_id":"repo-134-s025-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s025","section_path":["Smart Legend Variant"],"section_title":"Smart Legend Variant","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":309,"source_line_start":309,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"The latest commit adds `plot-throughput-smartlegend.py`.","text_sha256":"6c3c271ca220e37ed433fd3e876505ea928067c12ab3181b9eb6b0116e360ccf","unit_id":"s025","word_count":5},{"block_id":"repo-134-s025-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s025","section_path":["Smart Legend Variant"],"section_title":"Smart Legend Variant","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":311,"source_line_start":311,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"That shows continued iteration on publication presentation after the main processing pipeline existed.","text_sha256":"510ceac5dceeab8a671cef186339de76bcf903202d72e7c284c7e859eab6ce07","unit_id":"s025","word_count":13}]','{"analysis_source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","document_text_sha256":"2f974e253619afa75e6e60370048a65e12b0a3a7e9971b554a86e1ed6f1071e1","earliest_source_line":136,"embedding_text_sha256":"1ef4d4f7234a7ac22772238b33b4b5ce9d8016ef95a2e524338655ad108b3afd","normalized_input":"rag-corpus/repositories.jsonl","repository_raw_sha256":"43b29a0119b0b5888c5177ec9edcfc0b18d55ec6f3f89a18b86e168bbbd083a1","repository_source_line_end":760,"repository_source_line_start":1}');
INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-134-rd004',134,'Thesis',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','neutral','repository_specific',0.382,5,278,'Section: Throughput Processing Family

The throughput pipeline has multiple variants for different experimental conditions.

Core scripts include:

normalized forward/back extraction;

non-normalized extraction;

all-forward special-case extraction;

special-duration variants;

aggregate plotting;

smart-legend plotting.

Section: Standard Throughput Extraction

extract-throughput.py scans the performance data and motion logs, parses motion events, sorts those events globally by exact start time, assigns direction, and clips timestamped iperf lines into motion-specific output files.

The documented direction rule is:

Direction is assigned after global timestamp sorting.

This avoids relying on file enumeration order as a proxy for experimental order.

Section: Throughput Log Parsing

Throughput input is timestamped iperf output.

The parser extracts the wall-clock prefix and interval fields from each line.

The script keeps raw lines associated with parsed timestamps so generated clips preserve the original measurement representation while rewriting interval columns only when normalization is requested.

Section: Throughput Interval Normalization

The standard extractor can normalize each clipped run so the first relevant iperf interval begins from a local zero-time origin.

Conceptually:

This makes multiple runs comparable on the same trajectory-relative x-axis.

Section: Non-Normalized Throughput Variant

extract-throughput-notnormalized.py preserves original timing rather than rewriting every run to a zero origin.

This variant is useful when the analysis needs to retain direct relationship to the original experiment clock or iperf interval numbering.

The existence of both normalized and non-normalized paths shows the preprocessing choice is explicit rather than accidental.

Section: All-Forward Throughput Variant

extract-throughput-allfwd exists for a trajectory/data condition where the standard alternating direction assumption is not correct.

In this special case, motion events are interpreted as forward instead of alternating forward/backward.

The script family therefore encodes experiment-specific exceptions rather than forcing every data set through one unsuitable assumption.','["throughput","processing","family","standard","extraction","parsing","interval","normalization","non-normalized","variant","all-forward"]','["Throughput Processing Family","Standard Throughput Extraction","Throughput Log Parsing","Throughput Interval Normalization","Non-Normalized Throughput Variant","All-Forward Throughput Variant"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-134-s009-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Throughput Processing Family"],"section_title":"Throughput Processing Family","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":143,"source_line_start":143,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The throughput pipeline has multiple variants for different experimental conditions.","text_sha256":"abe927349c07b092fb749d0067887e04b8f5a94c0cdfc97f9b32c7461992f1ec","unit_id":"s009","word_count":10},{"block_id":"repo-134-s009-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Throughput Processing Family"],"section_title":"Throughput Processing Family","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":145,"source_line_start":145,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"Core scripts include:","text_sha256":"2280303d6efa2741127df40e07812ef83a2196bfd18eaee53527daf86d4ed8db","unit_id":"s009","word_count":3},{"block_id":"repo-134-s009-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s009","section_path":["Throughput Processing Family"],"section_title":"Throughput Processing Family","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":147,"source_line_start":147,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"- 