INSERT INTO rag_documents (document_id,repository_index,repository_name,repository_slug,repository_url,retrieval_class,semantic_area,evidence_polarity,evidence_level,specificity_score,concrete_signal_count,word_count,text,topics_json,evidence_areas_json,related_skill_ratings_json,source_fragments_json,provenance_json) VALUES ('repo-134-rd006',134,'Thesis',NULL,NULL,'interpretation','performance_scale','positive','repository_specific',0.3604,3,231,'Section: Throughput Aggregation

plot-throughput.py and related plotters consume processed throughput runs rather than reparsing raw experiment directories each time.

The plotting layer computes summary data across multiple runs and writes both visual and machine-readable outputs.

Section: Throughput Summary Statistics

The throughput plotting family includes outputs for:

per-time aggregate behavior;

per-run statistics;

mean;

standard deviation;

minimum;

maximum;

sample count.

The scripts therefore preserve both central tendency and run-to-run variability.

Section: Camera-Ready Throughput Plots

The specialized aggregate plotting code is designed to produce thesis-ready figures rather than only interactive exploratory graphics.

Observed outputs include:

PNG;

PDF;

CSV;

checklist/report text.

The plotting style includes grayscale-oriented publication output in relevant scripts.

Section: Latency Processing Family

Latency processing mirrors the throughput architecture but accounts for the fact that hping produces multiple RTT observations per second.

Core scripts include:

standard exact-motion clipping;

all-forward clipping;

P50-only plotting;

P50-only all-forward plotting;

joint P50/P99 plotting.

Section: Latency Acquisition Format

The latency scripts parse timestamped SYN/hping response lines.

The analysis specifically uses response lines containing an RTT value.

Header/control lines are not treated as latency observations.

Section: Latency P50

P50 represents median latency behavior inside the relevant sample set.

The repository uses it as a robust central latency statistic for time-dependent plots.

Section: Latency P99

P99 is retained to capture tail latency.

This recognizes that wireless/network performance cannot be characterized adequately by a mean or median alone when rare spikes matter.','["throughput","aggregation","statistics","camera-ready","plots","latency","processing","family","acquisition","format"]','["Throughput Aggregation","Throughput Summary Statistics","Camera-Ready Throughput Plots","Latency Processing Family","Latency Acquisition Format","Latency P50","Latency P99"]','[]','[{"block_id":"repo-134-s021-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":2,"evidence_level":"repository_specific","section_id":"s021","section_path":["Throughput Aggregation"],"section_title":"Throughput Aggregation","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":270,"source_line_start":270,"specificity_score":0.58,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"`plot-throughput.py` and related plotters consume processed throughput runs rather than reparsing raw experiment directories each time.","text_sha256":"634a2c1aa678c4cbe0a73346495bd15c67538bf127064c050771bd4507552be4","unit_id":"s021","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-134-s021-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s021","section_path":["Throughput Aggregation"],"section_title":"Throughput Aggregation","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":272,"source_line_start":272,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The plotting layer computes summary data across multiple runs and writes both visual and machine-readable outputs.","text_sha256":"ea37b9c9928351893ceffc0e93eb29e6cef9357acdb7c2012f4ebeb293167273","unit_id":"s021","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-134-s023-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s023","section_path":["Throughput Summary Statistics"],"section_title":"Throughput Summary Statistics","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":282,"so