":464,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"This creates a time scale comparable to the normalized trajectory-analysis figures.","text_sha256":"f817305566c80ff862dfec116f3582b2066a6a5dd11837b2b3749053817948de","unit_id":"s042","word_count":11},{"block_id":"repo-134-s043-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s043","section_path":["Why MCS Matters"],"section_title":"Why MCS Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":468,"source_line_start":468,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"MCS is not just another throughput field.","text_sha256":"a0a2bb795d27c1635c76a35ee5540d081966784df6243d9d17a5ac5293a64cc1","unit_id":"s043","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-134-s043-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s043","section_path":["Why MCS Matters"],"section_title":"Why MCS Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":470,"source_line_start":470,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"It is a link-adaptation state that can help explain why throughput changes as the robot moves through different channel conditions.","text_sha256":"abb157f24c95f3508736355169391aad02e3d252edf73c97e5c70e8d052e2ec5","unit_id":"s043","word_count":20},{"block_id":"repo-134-s043-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":1,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s043","section_path":["Why MCS Matters"],"section_title":"Why MCS Matters","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":472,"source_line_start":472,"specificity_score":0.38,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"Including MCS alongside RSSI and performance metrics gives the thesis a multi-layer view of wireless behavior.","text_sha256":"a1229beb6099961a99552af2d5b75e4c855a94a2f0698011b477fdb26c80b80c","unit_id":"s043","word_count":16},{"block_id":"repo-134-s044-b001","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s044","section_path":["Exactness Versus Normalization"],"section_title":"Exactness Versus Normalization","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":476,"source_line_start":476,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"The repository repeatedly separates two different concerns:","text_sha256":"ccd0cb98dda0363b57281e4667de7b0f946507e5909a18ccc7527ff5218328f4","unit_id":"s044","word_count":7},{"block_id":"repo-134-s044-b002","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s044","section_path":["Exactness Versus Normalization"],"section_title":"Exactness Versus Normalization","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":479,"source_line_start":478,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":1,"text":"1. **exact raw temporal alignment** for deciding which samples belong to the motion interval;\n2. **normalized elapsed time** for comparing runs after clipping.","text_sha256":"f30b5f04bf2d9073c47eeffc8eb258e4c2cbca075909b0cc29947656e3cd8af8","unit_id":"s044","word_count":23},{"block_id":"repo-134-s044-b003","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s044","section_path":["Exactness Versus Normalization"],"section_title":"Exactness Versus Normalization","source_file":"repositories/repo-134-Thesis/README.md","source_line_end":481,"source_line_start":481,"specificity_score":0.34,"template_repository_frequency":0,"text":"This is a strong research-processing design.","text_sha256":"d91f294461624b6d7e2c2bc34287f8eca47765937288432d1b342264f3829104","unit_id":"s044","word_count":6},{"block_id":"repo-134-s044-b004","canonical_categories":[],"concrete_hits":0,"evidence_level":"interpretive","section_id":"s044","section_path":["Exactness Versus Normalization"],"section_title":"E